\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are looking forward to seeing them both. And now it's time to check the weather with Somara Theodore. And Somara, you're tracking storms from coast to coast here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMY WEATHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM TRACK\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, Erielle. So, we have our eye on the southeast, of course, where we have the threat for severe weather. But we can't forget the northwest where we have these series of storms, really a barrage of storms, and the next one is moving in as we head through Saturday. You can see the timestamp there. Between today and tomorrow, we could see heavy snow in parts of the Rockies into Idaho and heavy rain lining the coastline from Seattle down to Portland into Eugene. They could see anywhere from two to three inches of rain further inland, another one to two feet of snow.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIN/SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLD BLAST AHEAD\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This comes on the heels of those previous systems. Following that, the cold blast. Now, today, we could actually see record highs in Detroit, around 59 degrees. In Washington, DC, low 60s. But then, in the following days, we get a real big chill down, down to the 30s and 40s. That's a look at the forecast across the country. Let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's a look at your local forecast. Back to you, my friends.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: CAMPAIGN COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right, Somara, thank you so much. And coming up here on "Good Morning America," a closer look at the political headlines, the White House clarifying comments President Biden made about why he's running for reelection.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: CHRISTMAS ANGELS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And then, how country star Brad Paisley and wife, actress Kimberly Williams-Paisley, are playing the part of some Christmas angels.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bh\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "PLAY OF THE DAY"\b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's our "Play of the Day" now and the well-known couple helping to play Santa this year. Country music star Brad Paisley and his wife, actress Kimberly Williams-Paisley, are behind a store in Nashville where parents can shop for holiday presents for free. The two-day event started yesterday, parents getting the chance to load up on gifts that include stuffed animals, video games, clothes, makeup, musical instruments. The store received about 2,000 donated items so far. It has raised $20,000. It usually operates as a free grocery store to help families. Paisley says he loves this time of year and suggests he may even show up in a Santa costume next time.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a gift in and of itself.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That would be great. That would be great.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that idea that there're actually a lot of local toy stores that do something similar.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Where you can go in and buy a bunch of gifts that can then be handed out to families in need. So, you know, check, check your area.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Everyone deserves a Christmas.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is such a good idea.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: HOSTAGE RESCUE ATTEMPT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up here on "GMA" in our second hour an attempt by Israel to rescue hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: PERINATAL DEATH RATES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We also have our "GMA" Cover Story coming up. Fetal and early infant deaths found to be twice as high in babies born to Black women compared to Hispanic and white women. A look at the possible reasons why.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: DEALS & STEALS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And then it's "Deals & Steals" coming up, helping you find the perfect gift for everyone on your holiday list. Tory's here.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bk\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 US VETOES UN RESOLUTION FOR IMMEDIATE CEASE-FIRE IN GAZA US AMBASSADOR: "WILL ONLY PLANT THE SEEDS FOR THE NEXT WAR\b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Somara. We know you will keep following it for us. Now to the latest fighting in Gaza and the US blocking a \uc2 UN\uc2  motion, demanding an immediate cease-fire, as we're learning new details about a failed operation to rescue hostages kidnapped by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . ABC's Tom Soufi Burridge is in Tel Aviv with the latest on the ground. Good morning, Tom.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL/\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US VETOES \uc2 UN\uc2  RESOLUTION FOR IMMEDIATE CEASE-FIRE IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US AMBASSADOR: "WILL ONLY PLANT THE SEEDS FOR THE NEXT WAR"\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Erielle. Yes, some really sad news just in of the death of another Israeli hostage. And as this exhibition here in Tel Aviv shows, there'll be lots of empty places at dinner tables this Hanukkah weekend as the suffering and fighting inside Gaza intensifies and the US moves to block calls for a cease-fire at the \uc2 UN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dramatic images emerging this morning of the aftermath of an Israeli missile strike, with the US blocking a call for another cease-fire in Gaza at the \uc2 UN\uc2 . This morning, Israel thanking the US for using its veto, halting a Security Council resolution for an immediate cease-fire.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT WOOD (US DEPUTY AMBASSADOR)\par \par \uc2 Although the United States strongly supports a durable peace in which both Israelis and Palestinians can live in peace and security, we do not support this resolution's call for an unsustainable cease-fire that will only plant the seeds for the next war.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Israel intensifying its assault in areas of Gaza, the death toll rising to more than 17 and a half thousand people according to the \uc2 Hamas\uc2 - run health ministry. And that US move at the \uc2 UN\uc2  to block a potential cease-fire sparking anger.\par \par \uc2 GAZA RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaks foreign language).\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This man accusing the US of being against the people who are being killed day and night, he says, by American weapons. Here desperate scenes after 15 members of one family were killed in an Israeli strike, with the \uc2 UN\uc2 's \uc2 World Food Programme\uc2  warning, half of the population in Gaza is starving.\par \par \uc2 CARL SKAU (DEPUTY EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR WORLD FOOD PROGRAMME)\par \par \uc2 The humanitarian operation is collapsing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON RESCUE ATTEMPT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IDF\uc2  SAYS IT FAILED TO RECOVER HOSTAGES IN SPECIAL OPERATION\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Casualties streaming into this hospital in Khan Younis. Israel saying it's moving to eradicate \uc2 Hamas\uc2  strongholds in that southern city. Injured children being treated on the hospital's floor as the US pressures Israel to do more to protect civilian lives.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATION IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROUGHLY 350 US CITIZENS REMAIN AS BLINKEN URGES TO PROTECT INNOCENT LIVES\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2  (SECRETARY OF STATE)\par \par \uc2 It remains imperative that Israel put a premium on civilian protection. And there does remain a gap between exactly what, what I said when I was there, the intent to protect civilians, and the actual results that we're seeing on the ground.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAELI OFFICIALS SAY\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And amid the fighting, news just in this morning of the death of another Israeli hostage, Sahar Baruch, it comes after the \uc2 IDF\uc2  said overnight it raided a \uc2 Hamas\uc2  hideout where hostages were being held, but no one was rescued in the operation.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, the \uc2 IDF\uc2  so far not commenting on whether Sahar Baruch was killed in that failed attempt to rescue Israeli hostages. The hostage's family forum releasing a statement saying he was murdered in Gaza, his brother killed in that October 7th terror attack. Gio?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the Texas Supreme Court has temporarily blocked a woman from an emergency abortion.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On Thursday, a state court ruled in favor of 31-year-old Kate Cox, allowing the abortion to go forward. But Texas State Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  appealed the ruling within hours, asking the State Supreme Court to intervene. The mother of two has severe pregnancy complications. Texas law bans all abortions with one exception, to save the life of the mother or to prevent irreversible damage to a major bodily function. The state of Texas arguing, Cox does not meet the criteria.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, MATERNAL HEALTH CARE DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here on our "GMA Morning Menu," a new CDC report revealing perinatal death rates are still twice as high for black mothers still. We'll have the latest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 6 MINUTES, THE "WONKA" CAST\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, "GMA" sits down with the stars of "Wonka" to chat about Willy's adventures before the chocolate factory.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 24 MINUTES, WILL IT OR WON'T IT?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in more sweet news, Will Ganss, he's here with will it or won't. The gift-wrapping hacks and trending gifts to get the season. Oh, look at Archie right there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Getting through (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, man.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And welcome back. There's our holiday window display in Times Square. And it's time for our advent calendar deal, revealing a special item for our viewers as we count down to Christmas. And for day nine, we have sweatshirts from 30A. These are made from recycled plastic bottles. And the savings start at 50% off. You can just scan the QR code right on the screen for more information on that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bo\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REMEMBER RYAN O'NEAL ACTOR BEST KNOWN FOR "LOVE STORY" & "PAPER MOON" DIES AT 82\b0\par\par\uc2 994 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's an important reminder. All right, Reena, thank you so much for that. We're gonna turn now to the passing of a legendary actor, Oscar- nominee Ryan O'Neal, one of Hollywood's leading men for decades, appearing in films like "Love Story," "Paper Moon" and "What's Up Doc?" ABC's Chris Connelly is here in our studio to take a look at his life and legacy. Good morning to you, Chris.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING RYAN O'NEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTOR BEST KNOWN FOR "LOVE STORY" & "PAPER MOON" DIES AT 82\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And good morning to you, Gio. Yes, a handsome heartthrob since 1960s television, a leading man in films of the '70s and '80s. Ryan O'Neal knew great success as an actor, even as his often turbulent personal life attracted public attention of a different kind.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "PEYTON PLACE"\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Taxi, lady?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ryan O'Neal leapt to fame on the ABC drama "Peyton Place," alongside Mia Farrow.\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I was a little shook up last night, Alice. I wouldn't blame you if you just said forget it.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It opened the door to the movies. There, the former boxer's rugged good looks and charisma earned immediate attention. For many, his onscreen pinnacle would come in 1970 with his starring role in "Love Story" opposite Ali MacGraw.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "LOVE STORY"\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I give you my hand. I give you my love, more precious than money.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He'd star in Director Peter Bogdanovich's screwball comedy "What's Up, Doc," opposite Barbra Streisand.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "WHAT'S UP DOC"\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, god, I'd forgotten the point.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 1973's "Paper Moon," when he'd star with his daughter Tatum O'Neal, she'd be an absolute sensation as grifter-in-training Addie Pray.\par \par \uc2 TATUM O'NEAL (DAUGHTER OF RYAN O'NEAL/ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 And she wrote, "Happy birthday, Addie," on the end of it. You just go look and see.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At ten years of age, Tatum would be nominated for a best supporting actress Oscar and...\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM ACADEMY AWARDS 1974\par \par \uc2 TATUM O'NEAL (DAUGHTER OF RYAN O'NEAL/ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 All I really want to thank is my director, Peter Bogdanovich and my father. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "2001: A Space Odyssey's" Director Stanley Kubrick would cast O'Neal in the glowing-by-candlelight Barry Lyndon with Melissa Barrison.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "BARRY LYNDON"\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Sir, let those laugh that win.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By then, O'Neal's own intimate life and misadventures had made him a tabloid fixture. His rages and emotional volatility would color several of his well-chronicled relationships. In her memoir, Angelica Huston would describe O'Neal grabbing her hair and hitting her in the forehead. With some of his children, there would be conflicts and periods of estrangement. But overnight, his son Patrick O'Neal recalling the father he loved.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK O'NEAL (SON OF RYAN O'NEAL)\par \par \uc2 I just wanted to share what a special man my dad is, and I think sometimes that is lost when they, when they hear things about Ryan O'Neal. He was the greatest father that I could've ever asked for. I just love the man so much. I really do and it's a big loss for me.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the '80s, Ryan O'Neal's romance with Farrah Fawcett would grab headlines. Together they had a son, Redmond. After a 1997 breakup, they'd reunite in 2001 as O'Neal battled leukemia. Then, just as his character had done on screen in "Love Story," he'd be by his loved one's side as Farrah faced the ravages of cancer.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM 2009\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm very happy going to the, her house every day if she's awake or not, or, or, or tending to her. And that's, that's my life. I'm not interested in anything but seeing to her comfort.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her saga and theirs chronicled by Barbara Walters in a 2009 ABC News special.\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 She was everybody's love, wasn't she?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RYAN O'NEAL, 1941 - 2023\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the same hospital room where she passed away 14 years ago, Ryan O'Neal died Friday at the age of 82.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Patrick O'Neal calling Farrah Fawcett the love of his father's life. And on social media, Mia Farrow recalling her co-star from the 1960s, saying simply, "Rest in peace, dear Ryan."\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the same hospital room.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, just amazing.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Got chills.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. And, and Chris, so good to have you in here from LA. We really appreciate (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CONNELLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bc\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CRIME TOURISM ON THE RISE THIEVES USING SOPHISTICATED METHODS TO BREAK INTO HIGH-END HOMES\b0\par\par\uc2 664 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back now on "GMA" with the new efforts by law enforcement to crack down on suspected crime tourism rings targeting high-end homes across the country. Dozens of homeowners finding themselves victims and realizing their security systems may be no match for these crafty thieves. ABC's Reena Roy back now with more. Good morning, Reena.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRIME TOURISM ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIEVES USING SOPHISTICATED METHODS TO BREAK INTO HIGH-END HOMES ACROSS THE US\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Erielle, good morning to you. Police say these crime rings are sophisticated and the criminals unfortunately really seem to know what they're doing, and they're targeting some of the most expensive homes in America.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM SECURITY CAMERA FOOTAGE\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police in Michigan say what you're looking at is so-called crime tourism caught on camera, when groups of criminal burglars from abroad travel into the US to commit their crimes.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF MICHAEL J BOUCHARD (OAKLAND COUNTY MICHIGAN)\par \par \uc2 They're coming from other countries, South America specifically, and coming here specifically with training and intent to commit crimes.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Crimes include stealing high-end jewelry, watches, purses and safes, then fleeing and often evading capture.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF MICHAEL J BOUCHARD (OAKLAND COUNTY MICHIGAN)\par \par \uc2 They use punches on the windows to - to break windows and they go through them rather than opening them. The technology is a pretty sophisticated jammer system that tries to attack any wireless systems including alarms or cellular.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRIME TOURISM MAP\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it's not just a problem in Michigan. Authorities nationwide sounding the alarm about break-ins like these that have cost Americans millions in burglaries, particularly in wealthy US suburban neighborhoods. Michigan's Oakland County, which includes parts of Detroit, has seen about 30 to 40 of these break-ins since September.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF MICHAEL J BOUCHARD (OAKLAND COUNTY MICHIGAN)\par \par \uc2 They've stolen at least tens of millions of dollars out of our county.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Earlier this year, surveillance video also capturing this burglary in Wilmington, Delaware, the suspect exiting the back door with multiple backpacks full of stolen goods. Watch this man climbing down a column from the second floor after robbing this Mission Viejo home. The Oakland, Michigan, sheriff says he's created a new task force to help combat the problem and is asking the Federal Government for help.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF MICHAEL J BOUCHARD (OAKLAND COUNTY MICHIGAN)\par \par \uc2 Even though there are a couple teams in custody, there's estimations that there's probably 98 to 110 more out there in our country doing this very same thing.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And experts say if you have a high-end home, you've really got to up your game with these kind of criminals, especially when it comes to your technology. They say make sure your surveillance and alarm systems are both updated. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's good information there, Reena, thank you. We will be right back with our "Play of the Day." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bj\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 09:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Thanks for saving me.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Saving you? Is that what you think I was doing?\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Uh-huh.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Wrong-o. I merely noticed that you're improperly packaged, my dear.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wrong-o. Back now on "GMA" with "How the Grinch Stole Christmas" showing off his Cindy Lou wrapping expertise. Gifts come in all shapes and sizes. And coming up, Will Ganss, he's not going to tie up a human.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRAPPING HACKS, COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 He's going to try his hands at some creative wrapping hacks for beginners or even the most advanced wrappers. It's a will it or won't it that you don't want to miss.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Will is the opposite of the Grinch.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hate, hate, hate. Loathe entirely.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wow. Okay. And you're dressed in green.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And I'm in green.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yep.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right. First here, let's look at some of the stories making news right now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID HOSPITALIZATION UP\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 COVID-19 hospitalizations have been increasing following weeks of decline. The CDC is reporting that there were more than 19,000 weekly hospitalizations due to the virus in the last week of November compared to some 15,000 a month earlier. The most vulnerable, of course, are the elderly and children under the age of 4.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EU AGREES ON A.I. OVERSIGHT\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  is paving the way for oversight over artificial intelligence. Negotiators on Friday signed a tentative political agreement for the Artificial Intelligence Act. The deal, which is the first of its kind, includes oversight on generative AI and the use of facial recognition. Details for the new legislation will be ironed out. The new rules will take effect in 2025 at the earliest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD SIGN TURNS 100\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the iconic Hollywood sign just celebrated a big birthday. And the sign, which first came about as a publicity stunt to advertise a real estate development company, just celebrated 100 years.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wow.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wow, 100 years.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Isn't that amazing?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's amazing. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I had no idea the history there. Interesting one.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yep.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bu\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do begin here with the breaking news overnight. The Texas Supreme Court freezing a lower court's ruling that would've allowed a woman to get an emergency abortion. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze joins us now from the Supreme Court in Washington, where it's been nearly 18 months since the High Court overturned Roe v. Wade. Elizabeth, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Gio. And we have not seen a case like this since the Supreme Court issued its decision back on Roe v. Wade back in 1973. In this case, a woman in Texas with severe pregnancy complications is suing the state to allow her to get access to an emergency abortion. And now the state's highest court is weighing in, putting that request on hold. Overnight a setback for abortion rights advocates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE PREGNANCY COMPLICATIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, a set back for abortion rights advocates. In a first of its kind case, the Texas Supreme Court temporarily blocking 31-year-old Kate Cox from obtaining an emergency abortion. Cox, a mother two, filed the legal challenge at 20 weeks pregnant. Her doctors saying her fetus has virtually no chance of survival. They warn continuing to carry the pregnancy could jeopardize her health and future fertility.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (SEEKING EMERGENCY ABORTION IN TEXAS)\par \par \uc2 There's no outcome here, you know, that results in us taking home a healthy baby girl.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT RULING\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On Thursday a lower court red in favor of Cox, granting her request for an emergency abortion despite the state's near total ban. But hours later, Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  appealed the ruling asking, the State Supreme Court to intervene. Late Friday it did, putting a temporary hold on the lower court's decision without regard to its merits as it review Paxton's appeal. \uc2 Cox\uc2 's lawyer saying in a statement overnight, "We are talking about urgent medical care. Kate is already 20 weeks pregnant. This is why people should not need to beg for health care in a court of law."\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE (ATTORNEY FOR KATE COX)\par \par \uc2 Many of Miss Cox's health risks during this pregnancy will put her life in danger if left untreated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN EXCEPTIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Texas law bans all abortions with narrow exceptions to save the life of the mother or to prevent irreversible damage to major bodily function. The State argues Cox does not meet the criteria.\par \par \uc2 JOHNATHAN STONE (LAWYER/TEXAS OFFICE OF THE ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 They plaintiffs have not shown that they will suffer an immediate irreparable injury.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, it's not clear this morning when the Texas Supreme Court will issue its decision. And a ruling in this case only applies to Kate Cox in her pregnancy, not to other women in the state. At least 16 states have passed restrictions banning nearly all abortions since the Supreme Court Overturned Roe v. Wade. Whit?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR STORM SWEEPING ACROSS THE COUNTRY 11 STATES FROM VIRGINIA TO MAINE UNDER FLASH FLOOD WATCH\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Another major turn in this case. All right, Elizabeth, thank you. We do move now to the major storms affecting tens of millions of Americans from coast to coast. Let's get right to Somara Theodore with the timing and the track on this. Somara, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR STORM SWEEPING ACROSS THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 11 STATES FROM VIRGINIA TO MAINE UNDER FLASH FLOOD WATCH\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. A precarious situation has developed out in Little Cottonwood Canyon, Utah. You can see all the snow on the road here. Parts of Utah saw over two feet of snow, and they're gearing up for their next storm in a series of storms. Right now, I wanna to focus on this system that's developing in the southeast, high wind alerts, flood watches. Most importantly, the fear, the threat for severe weather through parts of the Tennessee Valley and down to our Gulf Coast states. This is 5:00 p.m. this evening.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA: STORY WEATHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING THE STORM\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Notice if you live in Alexandria, Louisiana up to Nashville, Huntsville, Alabama, Jackson, this evening you have the threat for a few tornadoes, very strong winds and large hail. That severe threat then makes its way into Georgia, into Atlanta right on up into Carolinas by tomorrow morning. And then, by Sunday night, the heaviest of the rain will be battering the I-95 corridor with snow farther west into states like Pennsylvania and into Upstate New York. This is prompting the threat for flooding. We could see up to three inches of rain coming down very quickly. That's a look at the weather. Back to you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 40 MILLION AMERICANS UNDER FLOOD WATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRAIL MIX: ON THE MINDS OF VOTERS AMERICANS REACT TO TRUMP'S COMMENTS AND LATEST DEBATE\b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, yeah. All right. We start at this hour with the 2024 campaign, the first caucuses and primaries weeks away, so we're extending our "Trail Mix" series, a deeper look at voter insights on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAIL MIX: ON THE MINDS OF VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS REACT TO TRUMP'S COMMENTS AND LATEST DEBATE\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, potential voters across the country from the University of Alabama to diners in Iowa...\par \par \uc2 POTENTIAL VOTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I want the best for our country.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...reacting to the top political headlines including former President Trump's comments earlier this week at a town hall when asked if he'd use his power as retribution.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 He says, "You're not gonna be a dictator, are you?" I said, "No, no, no, other than day one. We're closing the border and we're drilling, drilling, drilling. After that I'm not a dictator."\par \par \uc2 RYAN BARRANCO (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 We know what he truly meant was that he wants to take action quickly in the office to turn around the last four years of what Biden's been doing.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN RICHMAN (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 I think donald Trump is the most serious threat to our nation that we have had.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL UGWUEKE (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 He might say they're joking, but I don't think he's, they're joking. They think, he's taking it serious.\par \par \uc2 MARK DONOHUE (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 Trump just likes to make headlines and he always makes them and he wants a question like that to be out there. He won't be a dictator, but he'll do what he promised, just like he did in his first term.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Americans also weighing in on the fourth Republican debate and the candidates that spoke to the issues that matter to them.\par \par \uc2 POTENTIAL VOTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That was Vivek.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN DOYLE (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley I thought came out looking like the best candidate for the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE LEAR (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 I don't think any of them spoke to issues that really are central to this election.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And their thoughts on Nikki Haley's rise in the polls and if she could be a strong general election candidate.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm wondering if you think she would have any chance of beating Joe Biden in a general election.\par \par \uc2 POTENTIAL VOTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I think she would.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you think Nikki Haley could defeat Joe Biden in the 2024 election?\par \par \uc2 POTENTIAL VOTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Trump's got it all made. He, he's set.\par \par \uc2 ARIA DONN (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 I think it's gonna be kind of hard to galvanize the Republican base for anyone except Trump. It really is the party of Trump.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN DOYLE (POTENTIAL VOTER)\par \par \uc2 I voted for Joe Biden in the last election and he just looks so frail up there. And so, I don't agree with some of Nikki Haley's policies, but I'm closely following her.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The words of the voters right there as the campaign season heats up. And coming up here, White House correspondent MaryAlice Parks and our deputy political director Averi Harper will be back here to talk more about the GOP debate, as well as Trump's comments and the other political headlines this morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 US VETOES IN RESOLUTION FOR IMMEDIATE CEASE-FIRE IN GAZA US AMBASSADOR: "WILL ONLY PLANT THE SEEDS FOR THE NEXT WAR"\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First, the war in Gaza. We're learning new details this morning about a failed operation to rescue hostages kidnapped by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. VETOES IN RESOLUTION FOR IMMEDIATE CEASE-FIRE IN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. AMBASSADOR: "WILL ONLY PLANT THE SEEDS FOR THE NEXT WAR"\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go back to Tom Soufi Burridge who is in Israel with the latest on the ground. Good morning, Tom.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Erielle. Yes, sad news in this morning of the death of another Israeli hostage. And as this tribute to the hostages shows, there'll be lots of empty places at dinner tables this Hanukkah weekend as the fighting and suffering inside Gaza intensifies. And the US this morning facing criticism for blocking calls for a cease-fire at the \uc2 UN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dramatic images emerging this morning of the aftermath of an Israeli missile strike with the US blocking a call for another cease-fire in Gaza at the \uc2 UN\uc2 . The US using its veto, halting a Security Council resolution for an immediate cease-fire.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT WOOD (US DEPUTY AMBASSADOR)\par \par \uc2 We do not support this resolution's call for an unsustainable cease-fire that will only plant the seeds for the next war.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON RESCUE ATTEMPT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IDF\uc2  SAYS IT FAILED TO RECOVER HOSTAGES IN SPECIAL OPERATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL-\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Israel intensifying its assault in areas of Gaza, the death toll rising to around 17,500, according to the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  run health ministry. And that US move at the \uc2 UN\uc2  to block a potential cease-fire sparking anger.\par \par \uc2 RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language)\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This man accusing the US of being against the people who are being killed day and night, he says, by American weapons. Here, desperate scenes after 15 members of one family were killed in an Israeli strike with the \uc2 UN's World Food Program\uc2  warning, half of the population in Gaza is starving.\par \par \uc2 CARL SKAU (DEPUTY EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR WORLD FOOD PROGRAMME)\par \par \uc2 The humanitarian operation is collapsing.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Israel saying it's moving to eradicate \uc2 Hamas\uc2  strongholds in Khan Younis. Injured children being treated on the hospital's floor as the US presses Israel to do more to protect civilian lives. And amid the fighting, news just in this morning of the death of another Israeli hostage Sahar Baruch. It comes as the \uc2 IDF\uc2  said, overnight, it raided a \uc2 Hamas\uc2  hideout where hostages where being held but no one was rescued in the operation.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, the \uc2 IDF\uc2  so far, not commenting on whether Sahar Baruch died during that failed attempt to rescue hostages. The hostage's family forum saying, he was murdered in Gaza. His brother was killed during the October 7th terror attack. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Tom Soufi Burridge for us, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bm\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Breaking overnight, abortion battle. The Texas supreme court temporarily blocking a ruling that would've allow a pregnant woman to get an emergency abortion. What happens next?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CROSS-COUNTRY STORMS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Cross-country storms impacting tens of millions of Americans from coast to coast. Our weather team tracking the timing and the threat of tornadoes, snow and torrential rain.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESOLUTION VETO\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Resolution veto. The US blocking US motion demanding an immediate cease-fire in Gaza as israel reveals a failed rescue operation to free hostages.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 'TIS THE SEASON... TO BE SICK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 COVID hospitalizations on the rise. The word about a new subvariant.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SICKLE CELL TREATMENTS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, medical breakthrough. The new sickle cell treatments being called a functional cure for many patients.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING RYAN O'NEAL\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Remembering Ryan O'Neal, the star of "Love Story"...\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I'll give you my love, more precious than money.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "Paper Moon."\par \par \uc2 RYAN O'NEAL (FORMER ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Anything is possible but possible don't make it true.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The career that made him one of the best-known actors of his time and his highly publicized personal life including his relationship with Farrah Fawcett.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELPING HANDS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And helping hands. The food bank serving more than 120 million meals throughout southeast Texas.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 All right. You be blessed.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, how country star Brad Paisley and his wife, actress, Kimberly Williams Paisley are making Christmas wishes come true.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live from ABC News in New York, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. So great to have you with us on a Saturday. Great to have Erielle back on the desk with us once again.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good to be here.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Another busy weekend here. We've got that major storm system sweeping across the country, 15 states under winter weather alerts and 50 million Americans under floodwater watches.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, the US vetoed a \uc2 United Nations Security Council\uc2  resolution that demanded an immediate cease-fire in Gaza as the \uc2 IDF\uc2  confirms it, its forces tried to free hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , but that operation failed.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLY CAMPUS RAMPAGE INVESTIGATION 911 CALLS RELEASED IN UNLV SHOOTING, STUDENTS & STAFF HEARD PLEADING FOR HELP\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Truly emotional testimony, Morgan, thank you. This morning, new details are emerging about the school shooting at the \uc2 University of Nevada Las Vegas\uc2  and the frantic 911 calls as President Biden meets with the UNLV president and students. ABC's Jaclyn Lee has the latest details. Jaclyn, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CAMPUS RAMPAGE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 911 CALLS RELEASED IN UNLV SHOOTING, STUDENTS & STAFF HEARD PLEADING FOR HELP\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit, good morning. Those who knew the victims are speaking out on how dearly they will be missed as the university grapples with how to move forward.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, chilling 911 calls made immediately after shots rang out on the \uc2 University of Nevada Las Vegas\uc2  campus.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF 911 CALL\par \par \uc2 911 DISPATCHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 How many shots have you heard?\par \par \uc2 911 CALLER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Like, like, five. I'm hiding under my desk. I closed my door. It's locked.\par \par \uc2 911 DISPATCHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Have you heard anything else before or after?\par \par \uc2 911 CALLER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I heard some screaming.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One terrified caller telling 911 she thinks she saw the shooter identified by police as former \uc2 East Carolina University\uc2  professor 67-year-old Anthony Polito.\par \par \uc2 911 CALLER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No, I just saw a man that I usually don't see on the fourth floor, about 6'4", heavyset, white man.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM SURVEILLANCE CAMERA FOOTAGE\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This as we are learning more about the two university police officers who were able to confront the shoot on Wednesday, seen here on surveillance video. The suspect, wearing a long coat, pursuing one officer who then turns and opens fire killing the suspect. Authorities identifying the officers as Detective Nate Drum and Officer Damian Garcia.\par \par \uc2 ADAM GARCIA (UNIVERSITY POLICE SERVICES/SOUTHERN COMMAND)\par \par \uc2 These two officers are heroes. They kept the worst from becoming a bloodbath.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Three people were killed in the shooting, another still in the hospital fighting for his life. Authorities also now releasing the name of the third deceased victim, Dr. Naoko Takemaru, an associate professor in the Department of World Languages and Cultures.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR MARGARET HART (ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF FRENCH)\par \par \uc2 Naoko was frail physically, however, she was lion-hearted in kindness, lion-hearted in generosity and lion-hearted in humanity.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ABOUT HEROIC OFFICERS WHO STOPPED UNLV SHOOTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN MEET WITH UNIVERSITY PRESIDENT & STUDENT REPRESENTATIVES\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden meeting the UNLV president and members of the student body while in Vegas for an infrastructure investments announcement.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is not normal and we can never let it become normal.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As for the two officers involved in the shootout, Detective Nate Drum and Officer Damian Garcia are placed on administrative leave, which is authorities say is routine in a shooting investigation. Erielle?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS SATURDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air. Severe storms in the south as millions brace for a super soaker that could last into the workweek.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAMAGING TORNADO STRIKES SOUTH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 At least one tornado on the ground in Tennessee with homes damaged. Severe weather stretching from Texas to Ohio. The storm that buried the west in snow now threatening the northeast with drenching rains. Fifty-six million people under flood watches from Virginia to Maine. New York City warning of flooding on highways and in basements. Somara Theodore timing it all out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, the historic abortion battle playing out in Texas. The State Supreme Court steps in to stop a mother of two from having an emergency abortion. Doctors say her fetus is not viable and carrying it to term could threaten her health and future fertility. Why the Texas attorney general argues her case does not meet the state's criteria allowing for an abortion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking news, \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  President Liz Magill resigns. She'd been under pressure from donors and alumni after she appeared before Congress, declining to say a call for genocide against Jews would violate the university's code of conduct. What we've just learned.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIERCE FIGHTING IN NORTHERN GAZA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 To the Middle East and fierce fighting in the streets of Gaza. Israeli forces battling \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in the north. Tonight, the new threat to shipping in the Red Sea, and why the US vetoed a cease-fire resolution.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Countdown to Iowa. With the caucuses just over a month away, the Republican candidates flock to the state in search of support. What voters are saying about whether the field can catch up to former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN MURDER MYSTERY INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New developments in a murder mystery. A high school cheerleader found dead in her home. Her mother making the heartbreaking discovery. Police now releasing surveillance photos and looking for a person of interest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED ARSON ATTEMPT AT MLK HOME\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A woman suspected of trying to set fire to the birthplace of Martin Luther King Jr. The good Samaritans who stepped in to stop it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $700 MILLION BASEBALL DEAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Baseball's $700 million man. Two-way star Shohei Ohtani and the record deal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA STRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "America Strong" tonight. The lifesaving lesson that helped turn a seventh grader into a hero.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight."\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG STUDENT SAVES CLASSMATE FROM CHOKING\b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, NORTHUP, STONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 MAGILL, RESIGNATION, STEFANIK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , AID, WOOD, SELAVAN, RADMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIERCE FIGHTING IN NORTHERN GAZA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DESANTIS, HALEY, RAMASWAMY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 MEDINA, MURDER, ARSON, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN MURDER MYSTERY INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, EVERT, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS, HENRY, CARROLL, HEIMLICH MANEUVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, "America Strong." How a middle school lesson turned a student into a lifesaver.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Twelve-year-old Ethan Williams is still getting used to being called a hero.\par \par \uc2 ETHAN WILLIAMS (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Let's go to lunch.\par \par \uc2 BRYCE HENRY (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 It was the type of thing where it was a quick reaction, but it was also kind of scary at the same time.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ethan and his classmate Bryce Henry were eating lunch in their school's cafeteria near Philadelphia when Bryce started choking on a piece of apple.\par \par \uc2 BRYCE HENRY (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 I was just eating lunch, and it suddenly flew down my throat, and then I started choking.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bryce signaling he was choking grabbing his throat with both hands. Ethan jumping right into action.\par \par \uc2 BRYCE HENRY (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 While I was choking, he, like, grabbed my stomach and I didn't know what was happening. And then he did the Heimlich. He literally saved my life.\par \par \uc2 ETHAN WILLIAMS (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Go right behind him. One, two, three.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both boys were prepared, learning the Heimlich maneuver in class last spring.\par \par \uc2 MAUREEN CARROLL (TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 Come here. Let me see you, hero.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maureen Carroll was their proud teacher.\par \par \uc2 MAUREEN CARROLL (TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 For choking, did you go like this?\par \par \uc2 ETHAN WILLIAMS (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 And I still knew how to do it. So, I used it. And then I went, one, two, three.\par \par \uc2 MAUREEN CARROLL (TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 Textbook. He listened, he learned, he recognized what's happening, and he acted so fearlessly. And it validates all the hard work that we put into teaching. Way to go, Ethan.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Way to go, Ethan.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ethan sharing this advice for all of us.\par \par \uc2 ETHAN WILLIAMS (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 You don't always have to save someone's life, but get to know people, get to know the person, because then when they need you the most, you can be there for them.\par \par \uc2 ETHAN WILLIAMS (STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, thank you, thank you.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And he deserves all of that praise. Way to go, Ethan. Thanks so much for watching tonight. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. I'll see you on "GMA" in the morning. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES TEEN MURDER MYSTERY INVESTIGATION/ALLEGED ARSON ATTEMPT AT MLK HOME\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, NORTHUP, STONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 MAGILL, RESIGNATION, STEFANIK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , AID, WOOD, SELAVAN, RADMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIERCE FIGHTING IN NORTHERN GAZA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DESANTIS, HALEY, RAMASWAMY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 MEDINA, MURDER, ARSON, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN MURDER MYSTERY INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, the urgent search for the person who killed the high school cheerleader in Texas.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police releasing images of a person of interest now and his car. The body of 16-year-old Lizbeth Medina was found by her mother on Tuesday after she failed to appear at a Christmas parade. The small town of Edna coming together two days ago at a football game to honor her memory.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED ARSON ATTEMPT AT MLK HOME\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Atlanta, a woman was arrested for allegedly trying to set fire to the birthplace of Martin Luther King Jr.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tourists from Utah recorded video of the woman appearing to splash gasoline on the front of the house. Two retired officers from New York happened to be there and held her until \uc2 Atlanta police\uc2  arrived. The suspect, a Navy veteran, is charged with attempted arson.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back tonight, a tennis legend faces a new health crisis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Shohei Ohtani has a new team and a record contract that's shaking up baseball.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS FACED BACKLASH OVER CONGRESSIONAL TESTIMONY ON ANTISEMITISM\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, NORTHUP, STONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 MAGILL, RESIGNATION, STEFANIK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the news just coming in tonight, the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  president who had come under sharp criticism after her testimony on Capitol Hill on antisemitism has resigned. She declined to say that a call for genocide against Jews violated the university's code of conduct. Details now from ABC's Phil Lipof.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACED BACKLASH OVER CONGRESSIONAL TESTIMONY ON ANTISEMITISM\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, just days after her widely criticized testimony before Congress, embattled \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  president, Liz Magill, has voluntarily resigned, saying in a statement, "It has been an honor to work with our faculty, students, staff, alumni and community members to advance Penn's vital missions." On Tuesday, alongside the presidents of Harvard and MIT, responding to questions on antisemitism, it was this exchange that prompted calls for her to resign.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE ELISE STEFANIK (REP) (NEW YORK)\par \par \uc2 I am asking, specifically calling for the genocide of Jews, does that constitute bullying or harassment?\par \par \uc2 LIZ MAGILL (FORMER PRESIDENT UNIVERSITY OF PENNSYLVANIA)\par \par \uc2 If it's directed and severe or pervasive, it is harassment.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE ELISE STEFANIK (REP) (NEW YORK)\par \par \uc2 So, the answer is yes.\par \par \uc2 LIZ MAGILL (FORMER PRESIDENT UNIVERSITY OF PENNSYLVANIA)\par \par \uc2 It's a context-dependent decision, congresswoman.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hours after that testimony and bipartisan backlash, this apology.\par \par \uc2 LIZ MAGILL (FORMER PRESIDENT UNIVERSITY OF PENNSYLVANIA)\par \par \uc2 I was not focused on, but I should have been, the irrefutable fact that a call for genocide of Jewish people is a call for some of the most terrible violence human beings can perpetrate.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the October 7th terror attack on Israel and Israel's bombardment of Gaza, tensions flaring, especially on US college campuses. Since the start of this school year, the \uc2 Anti-Defamation League\uc2  says 73% of Jewish college students reported experiencing or witnessing antisemitism on campus. Less than half say they feel safe on campus.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Phil Lipof is back with us now. Phil, you're learning more about the Department of Education widening its investigation into antisemitism on college campuses?\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, Whit. The Department of Education has opened up investigations into ten universities and colleges. Now, the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  and Harvard are among them. These are schools where students report high incidents of antisemitism and islamophobia. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Phil Lipof tonight, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, NORTHUP, STONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 MAGILL, RESIGNATION, STEFANIK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENN PRESIDENT RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , AID, WOOD, SELAVAN, RADMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIERCE FIGHTING IN NORTHERN GAZA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DESANTIS, HALEY, RAMASWAMY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 MEDINA, MURDER, ARSON, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN MURDER MYSTERY INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, EVERT, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" now. And baseball has its first $700 million man.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Shohei Ohtani posted on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  that he's leaving the \uc2 Los Angeles Angels\uc2  for the Dodgers. Ohtani brings nearly unprecedented talent to the Dodgers. He's one of baseball's top hitters and pitchers. He just won his second MVP award. His new ten-year, $700-million contract is by far the largest ever in North American team sports.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tennis legend Chris evert has revealed her cancer has returned.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Evert, now 68 years old, was first diagnosed with ovarian cancer two years ago. The cancer had been in remission. In a statement, she said it was caught early and she's undergoing chemotherapy. Evert will not be part of \uc2 ESPN\uc2 's coverage of the Australian Open next month, but hopes to return for the rest of the grand slam season.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back here tonight, "America Strong" and lesson learned. How a 12-year-old became a lifesaver.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED STATE HIGH COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EARLIER JUDGMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, NORTHUP, STONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION RULING PAUSED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, a new twist in a Texas woman's challenge to one of the country's most restrictive abortion laws. The Texas Supreme Court putting on hold a lower court ruling that would have allowed Kate Cox to end her pregnancy. Doctors say her 20-week-old fetus has a fatal diagnosis, but the state of Texas says say she doesn't meet criteria for an abortion. The historic case is the first of its kind since Roe v. Wade 50 years ago. Here's ABC's Elizabeth Schulze.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE HIGH COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EARLIER JUDGMENT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a stark reversal in an historic case over access to an abortion in the post-Roe era. The Texas Supreme Court Friday night temporarily blocking 31-year-old Kate Cox from obtaining an emergency abortion after Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  appealed to the court writing, "Nothing can restore the unborn child's life that will be lost as a result. Time is of the essence." The state's highest court putting a hold on a lower court's ruling Thursday that said Cox qualified for an abortion, despite the state's near total ban.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How urgent is it for Kate Cox right now to be able the get access to an emergency abortion?\par \par \uc2 NANCY NORTHUP\uc2  (PRESIDENT CENTER FOR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS)\par \par \uc2 Time is of the essence. I mean, the clock is ticking. Every day that goes by, the risk to her health and life and future fertility increase.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cox, a mother of two from Dallas, is 20 weeks pregnant. Her doctors told her last week her fetus has virtually no chance of survival because of a severe condition called trisomy-18. They warn, if she continues to carry the pregnancy, her health and future fertility could be at risk.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (PLAINTIFF IN ABORTION CASE)\par \par \uc2 There's no outcome here, you know, that results in us taking home a healthy baby girl.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Cox\uc2 's suit was the first known case of a woman seeking a court order for an emergency abortion since Roe v. Wade in 1973.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Texas, one of 21 states enforcing restrictions on the procedure since Roe was overturned. Under Texas law, abortions are banned except if a mother's life is at risk or if it prevents irreversible damage to a major bodily function. The state arguing, Cox does not meet those criteria.\par \par \uc2 JOHNATHAN STONE (TEXAS ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE)\par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs have not shown that they will suffer an immediate and irreparable injury.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze joining us now. And, Elizabeth, with this mother arguing her health is in imminent jeopardy, how quickly might the Texas Supreme Court act on this?\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, the court has given no sense of a timeline here of whether it will allow the lower court's decision to stand, permitting Cox to have an abortion. And this is just the beginning of cases appealing directly to courts for the right to an abortion in states where it's banned. A woman who is eight weeks pregnant in Kentucky has just filed a similar lawsuit. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020231213ejc900003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE STATE AG THREATENS ACTION AFTER JUDGE GRANTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY REQUEST\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTER BIDEN CHARGED\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, INDICTED, TAXES, WEISS, JEAN-PIERRE\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, UNIVERSITIES, TESTIMONY, ANTISEMITISM\par \par \uc2 UNLV, RAMPAGE, SUSPECT, VICTIMS, GARCIA, MCMAHILL\par \par \uc2 SYNAGOGUE, SHOTS, SUSPECT, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , ANTISEMITISM\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, OUTRAGE, PALESTINIANS, HUMANITARIAN, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 JOBS, ECONOMY, INFLATION, FED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN STORMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "DANCING WITH THE STARS"\par \par \uc2 MURDER, MEDINA, CHEERLEADER, MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 PILOT, SABOTAGE, COURT, MENTAL HEALTH, EMERSON\par \par \uc2 CRACKDOWN, THIEVES, PACKAGES, GAMBLE, CLAWSON, HARKINS, PORCH\par \par \uc2 HOUGH, ERBERT, CRANIAL HEMATOMA, SURGERY, TOUR\par \par \uc2 "BILLBOARD", TOP FIVE, SONGS, CHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTER BIDEN INDICTED\par \par \uc2 GAMBLE, COX, DUANE, STONE, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ok, Pierre. Thank you. Now to the abortion battle playing out in Texas. The first publicized case of its kind. A woman sued the state for emergency permission for the procedure after the fetus was diagnosed with medical condition that is almost always fatal. The judge ruled in her favor but the state may still try to stand in her way. Rachel Scott has the story this morning. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Juju, good morning to you. We haven't seen anything like this since the fall of Roe versus Wade. A judge stepping in, allowing a Texas woman to get an emergency abortion. A direct challenge to one of the strictest bans in the country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning an unprecedented challenge to the Texas abortion ban. A judge intervening to allow 31-year-old Kate Cox to get an emergency abortion.\par \par \uc2 JUDGE MAYA GUERRA GAMBLE (TRAVIS COUNTY 459TH DISTRICT COURT)\par \par \uc2 The idea that Misses Cox wants desperately to be a parent and this law might actually cause her to lose that ability is shocking and would be a genuine miscarriage of justice.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At 20 weeks pregnant, Cox learned her fetus has a severe abnormality and virtually no chance of survival. Her doctors warn continuing the pregnancy could jeopardize her own health.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 There's no outcome here, you know, that results in us taking home a healthy baby girl.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Texas banned abortion outright, with one narrow exception to save the life of the mother or prevent irreversible damage to a major bodily function. Kate told me she was almost certain she would qualify.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I could see in this case surely I would qualify for that exemption. So my doctor told me that I did not have that option to stay in Texas. I was shocked.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So she and her husband sued the State of Texas. In an extraordinary live streamed court hearing her lawyer describes how Kate had to go to the emergency room four times in just the last month.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE (ATTORNEY FOR KATE COX)\par \par \uc2 Many of Misses Cox health risks during this pregnancy will put her life in danger if left untreated.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The state argued they needed more evidence.\par \par \uc2 JOHNATHAN STONE (LAWYER TEXAS OFFICE OF ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs have not shown they will suffer an immediate and irreparable injury.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE LONGER MISSES COX STAYS PREGNANT, THE GREATER RISKS TO HER LIFE."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the judge siding with Kate saying the longer Misses Cox stays pregnant, the greater risk to her life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's unclear if the state will try to fight this ruling but this morning the Texas Attorney General, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is threatening to go after any doctor who might perform Kate Cox's abortion. Saying that despite this ruling they could still face serious penalties including loss of license and up to life in prison, even her husband could be at risk for aiding and abetting an abortion, DeMarco.\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That story is far from over. Rachel, thank you for that report.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240102ejc800038\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNPRECEDENTED ABORTION CASE PREGNANT WOMAN ARGUED STATE'S BAN ENDANGERS HER HEALTH\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLITO, GARCIA, MCMAHILL, WHITTINGTON\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, HOCHUL, WRAY, SYNAGOGUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOTS FIRED OUTSIDE NY SYNAGOGUE\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , AL-MADHOUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: ISRAEL MAY FLOOD HAMAS TUNNELS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL CROSS-COUNTRY STORM\par \par \uc2 COX, ABORTION, DUANE, GAMBLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNPRECEDENTED ABORTION CASE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to Texas tonight, and to the issue of abortion. Tonight, the case of a young woman with her husband today, she is 20 weeks pregnant. Her doctors say her own health is in danger because of complications now, going before the judge after being told in Texas she still cannot have an abortion. Tonight here, the judge's ruling and how the state is now responding. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREGNANT WOMAN ARGUED STATE'S BAN ENDANGERS HER HEALTH\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a first-of-its-kind case playing out in Texas. In an extraordinary livestreamed court hearing, 31-year-old Kate Cox and her husband Justin begging a judge to let her have an emergency abortion currently banned under Texas law.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE (ATTORNEY FOR KATE COX)\par \par \uc2 Today, we are seeking a temporary restraining order to allow Ms. Cox to get the abortion that she needs now to end her suffering and protect her fertility.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cox, a mother of two, is 20 weeks pregnant. But doctors have told her her fetus has a severe abnormality and virtually no chance of survival. What's more, they said continuing the pregnancy could put her health at risk and prevent her from getting pregnant again. Texas now bans abortion outright with one narrow exception, to prevent major bodily harm or save the life of the mother. Kate told me she was certain that would apply to her.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Now, you could see in this case, surely, I would qualify for that exemption. So, my doctor told me that I did not have that option in the state of Texas, I was shocked. My husband as well.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, today, Kate and her husband listened as her lawyer described how Kate had been to the emergency room four times in just the last month.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE (ATTORNEY FOR KATE COX)\par \par \uc2 Many of Ms. Cox's health risks during this pregnancy will put her life in danger if left untreated.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She argued the law in Texas outlining exceptions is just too vague, calling it cruel and dangerous.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE (ATTORNEY FOR KATE COX)\par \par \uc2 Now, a patient must be about to die before a doctor can rely on the exception.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still, today, the state insisting Kate Cox needs to provide more evidence to prove she qualifies.\par \par \uc2 JOHNATHAN STONE (SPECIAL COUNSEL TEXAS ATTORNEY GENERAL'S OFFICE)\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs have not shown they will suffer an immediate and irreparable injury.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Judge Maya Guerra Gamble ruling on the spot that Kate Cox could get the abortion she is seeking.\par \par \uc2 JUDGE MAYA GUERRA GAMBLE (TRAVIS COUNTY DISTRICT COURT)\par \par \uc2 The idea that Ms. Cox wants desperately to be a parent and this law might actually cause her to lose that ability is shocking and would be a genuine miscarriage of justice.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The judge adding, "The longer Ms. Cox stays pregnant, the greater risks to her life."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's unclear if the state will try to fight this ruling. But tonight, the Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  is threatening to go after any doctor who might try to perform Kate Cox's abortion, saying they could still face sere you penalties, including the loss of their license and up to life in prison. Even her own husband could be at risk on charges of aiding and abetting an abortion, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott live in Washington. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231211ejc70002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 USS CARNEY, ATTACK, DRONES, HOUTHI, VESSELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHIPS UNDER ATTACK IN THE RED SEA\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, ASSAULT, GAZA, CIVILIANS, ELDER, AUSTIN, HARRIS, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL EXPANDS GROUND ASSAULT\par \par \uc2 PARIS, STABBING, VICTIMS, SUSPECT, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARIS TERROR PROBE\par \par \uc2 STORMS, SNOW, RAIN, ADVISORIES, AVALANCHE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS COAST TO COAST\par \par \uc2 STABBINGS, RAMPAGE, VICTIMS, INURED, HENDRY, MADDREY, FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY NEW YORK CITY RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 ATC, SAFETY, "NEW YORK TIMES", DRUNK, ASLEEP, SAFETY,\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIR SAFETY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 SERIAL KILLER, ARREST, POWELL LUNA, MOORE, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SERIAL KILLER ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 MT HOOD, SURVIVAL, JAMES, BASKETBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIRACLE SURVIVAL STORY\par \par \uc2 EUROPE, SNOWSTORM, COLLEGE FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 EARL, CANCER, GRATITUDE, LEGACY\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally tonight, "America Strong." Last Sunday, we featured Michelle Earl, an example of gratitude personified. This week, she lost her battle with breast cancer but leaves behind quite a legacy.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 18 months ago, when 55-year-old Michelle Earl, a mother of three from Wisconsin, was diagnosed with an aggressive breast cancer, she didn't let the doctor's prognosis decrease her faith.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE EARL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 It would have been really easy to lose hope and lose faith. But then what happened was I just changed what I was dreaming about.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her dreams of tomorrow became her plans for today, as she embraced the time she had left. Michelle and her husband, Joe, made a conscience decision to love every moment, creating a bucket list, crossing off each and every item, including sky diving, a family trip to Hawaii, taking a hot air balloon ride together.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE EARL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 That was amazing.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And getting baptized again. Michelle and Joe also gave back, walking with supporters to raise more than $12,000 for the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 . Last Sunday, surrounded by dozens of her family and friends, there's Michelle, watching our "America Strong" segment.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Two days later, she passed away, but not before her story inspired people from around the world to send messages to her family, noting Michelle's strength and positivity.\par \par \uc2 JOE EARL (HUSBAND OF MICHELLE)\par \par \uc2 And the message is to love every moment and not waste time because you can't get it back.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Their neighbors' homes now lit up in pink, in honor of Michelle and the countless others battling breast cancer, her husband with some of Michelle's words of wisdom.\par \par \uc2 JOE EARL (HUSBAND OF MICHELLE)\par \par \uc2 Do not wait for some day, make some day today. Laugh with others, but most importantly, laugh at yourself and be vulnerable in life and love.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Great advice there. Thanks so much for watching. I'm Linsey Davis. David Muir right back here tomorrow. I'll see you first thing on "GMA." Until then, good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020231206ejc30000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG GRATITUDE PERSONIFIED\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN AMONG RELEASED HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 HOSTAGES, FREED, IDAN, PRISONERS, CEASE-FIRE, HUMANITARIAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN AMONG RELEASES HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HOSTAGES, CEASE-FIRE, ISRAEL, EGYPT, QATAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: WON'T STOP UNTIL EVERY HOSTAGE RETURNED\par \par \uc2 SIT-IN, SHOOTING, PALESTINIANS, HATE CRIME, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTS DOWN MANHATTAN BRIDGE\par \par \uc2 STORM, WINDS, ACCIDENTS, TRAVEL, TSA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY WINTER STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 CHAUVIN, STABBED, FLOYD, PRISON, O'HARA, ELLISON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEREK CHAUVIN STABBED\par \par \uc2 DRONES, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA LAUNCHES MASSIVE DRONE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 CANADA, VILLANI, CHINA, RESPIRATORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUPLE IDENTIFIED IN BORDER CRASH\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, E-COMMERCE, RECALL, SALMONELLA\par \par \uc2 ERAL, BREAST CANCER, BUCKET LIST, FORTUNATE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, "America Strong." Many might have considered it a death sentence, but tonight, we introduce you to someone who was inspired to live.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Michelle Eral is gratitude personified. 18 months ago, when the 55-year-old was diagnosed with an aggressive breast cancer, she didn't let the doctors' prognosis decrease her faith.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE ERAL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 It would have been really easy to lose hope and lose faith. But then what happened was I just changed what I was dreaming about.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her dreams of tomorrow simply became her dreams of today as she embraces the time she has left. Michelle and her husband Joe made a conscious decision to love every moment, creating a bucket list. And with the help of family and friends, this past year they managed to cross off every single item, including skydiving, a family trip to Hawaii.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE ERAL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 We wanted to go see "Hamilton." That was a big thing for me.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Taking a hot air balloon ride together.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE ERAL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 That was a big one, too. That was amazing.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And getting baptized again. Michelle and Joe are also giving back. Last month, this group of supporters sported T-shirts with Michelle's motto, love every moment, raising more than $12,000 for the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 . They show up at doctor and hospital visits with dozens of cookies for the staff, as a way to show how grateful they are.\par \par \uc2 JOE ERAL (HUSBAND OF MICHELLE)\par \par \uc2 It helps to have those random acts of kindness.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This Thanksgiving, thanks to the Earls' friends, a feast was prepared for the family for what is likely their last holiday together. Michelle surrounded by her husband, daughter, sons, and grandson.\par \par \uc2 SON OF MICHELLE ERAL (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Every moment does matter and every relationship does matter.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE ERAL (DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 It goes back to that word, fortunate. I just find myself extremely fortunate.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 An inspiration. Thanks so much for watching. I'm Linsey Davis. We'll see you tomorrow on "GMA." Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020231128ejbq0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 SULLIVAN, ISRAEL, HOSTAGES, GAZA, HOSPITALS, NETANYAHU, LAWLER, MOSKOWITZ\par \par \uc2 MOORE, HARRIS, DEMOCRATS, BIDEN, 2023, VOTERS, AXELROD, MANCHIN\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM WEDNESDAY\par \par \uc2 "TIRED OF WINNING", BOOK, TRUMP, 2020, LINDELL, ELLIS, BROOKS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM MARCH 25\par \par \uc2 MANCHIN, NO LABELS, DEMOCRATS, GOP, ABORTION, BIDEN, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JOE MANCHIN\uc2  (DEM) (WEST VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 I have made one of the toughest decisions of my life and decided that I will not be running for reelection to the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . But what I will be doing is traveling the country, and speaking out to see if there is an interest in creating a movement to mobilize the middle and bring Americans together.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Democratic Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  of West Virginia announcing he's not running for reelection, but clearly leaving the door open for a possible third-party run for president. The Roundtable is here to break it all down. We have former DNC Chair Donna Brazile, "Politico" senior political columnist Jonathan Martin, "Politico Playbook" co-author, Rachael Bade, and co-host of "The View," Alyssa Farah Griffin, who served as communications director in the Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, J. Martin, let me start with you. Manchin...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...is he gonna run for president as a third party, No Labels candidate?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEST VIRGINIA'S MANCHIN ANNOUNCES RETIREMENT FROM SENATE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Well, first of all, I think that this almost guarantees that the GOP takes over the Senate next year. It leaves almost no margin for error for Democrats. They, they now have to win a series of tough states, including Montana and Ohio. So, I think that's the headline. Yeah, look, Manchin is still teasing the possibility of running third. And I think the combination of that tease from Manchin that you just played and Jill Stein, a name that'll trigger Democrats out there, Jill Stein's entry...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES SAY MANCHIN NOT RULING OUT PRESIDENTIAL RUN\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 ...as a Green Party candidate this week should really wake Joe Biden up to the multi-dimensional threat he could face next year, a four-way or five-way race that could be...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bobby Kennedy Jr...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yes. Jill Stein...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cornell West.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Cornell West, and potentially No Labels type candidate. And, Jon, I think it's imperative, and a lot of Democrats do as well, that President Biden get people like \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , like his buddy, \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , who he's talking to a lot these days, by the way, Manchin is, get them to the White House and say, you don't want Trump to be president again any more than I do. The only way to stop him is for me to win reelection. Maybe you don't like everything that I've done as president, but the goal has got to be to keep Trump out of the Oval Office, stop the BS, guys. Let's stop Trump.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, Donna, this has got to be triggering you a bit. I mean, I remember hanging out with you in 2000. You were working for a guy named \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , there was \uc2 Ralph Nader\uc2 . How many...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the Green Party. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...how many, how many votes did he have in Florida?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, one too many. Let's just say that (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. So, so how worried, how worried are you this could...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO WILL THIRD-PARTY CANDIDATES HURT AND HELP IN 2024?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first of all, we continue to underestimate Joe Biden. We underestimated him last week. We were just talking about his poll numbers and, you know, Joe Biden should dismiss himself from the stage. Look, Joe Biden continues to overperform, defy expectations. The Democratic Party is winning. The Democratic Party is able to put together their coalition. If Joe Biden has some free time, I wouldn't invite someone who's resigning or, or retiring from the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . I would get more young people.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I would get the kind of voters that Joe Biden will need in 2024 in order to put together that same electoral coalition that provided over 80 million votes. You know, talk about tired of losing. When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came down those stairs, and Alyssa, you will love this, there were 54 Republican senators. There were over 247 House members. They, they, that's the party that should be worried about their coalition, not the Democratic Party. We proved on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, but this third party, you aren't worried that, that, that...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course, you should always worry about what I call, you know, all of the various spices and all of the seasoning that goes into an electoral gumbo.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But here's what Joe Biden knows, he has the Tabasco. He has the receipts. He has the winning message that I think the American people think about, and that is Joe Biden is providing relief to American families.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachael...\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, I don't understand this from a messaging standpoint. I mean, you had the Maryland governor on the show just a few minutes ago, and we're talking in the green room watching him. He's very much just a, you know, dismissing this idea of unity candidates, third parties, candidates being a threat to Joe Biden. Why not raise the alarm on this? Why not say, okay, a vote for one of these candidates is a vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? I mean, like, by downplaying it here, I almost wonder if they're getting - gonna miss an opportunity to very much snuff it out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOW BIDEN POLL NUMBERS WORRY SOME DEMOCRATS\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in terms of \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , we should also go back to the Senate here. We're talking 2024. But this is really, you know, the institution of the Senate is very much changing right now. He is one of the few dealmakers that is still left in the upper chamber. And we've seen in recent years people like \uc2 Jeff Flake\uc2 , \uc2 Bob Corker\uc2 , \uc2 Lamar Alexander\uc2 , these dealmakers, they leave the Senate and they're replaced by Trump accolades who want nothing to do with compromise. And this is very much gonna change the institution of the Senate beyond the 2024 (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you have Tommy Tuberville.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, he's, he's really interested in compromising.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Consensus maker. And listen, Tuesday was unequivocally a good night for Democrats. But I think it would be a mistake to assume that just because the Democratic brand is strong right now, especially with abortion politics being front and center, that that means Joe Biden is strong right now. I mean, we've seen the polling. Six in ten Americans do not want the dreaded Trump versus Biden rematch. So, there is going to be, if this kind of third party ticket emerges, a tremendous amount of interest in it from the average voter who doesn't feel like they're represented by those two options.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATIC INCUMBENTS FACE TOUGH SENATE MAP IN 2024\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 But I also think that, 'cause I, I worry Democrats are maybe being overly confident coming off of Tuesday. We've seen "The New York Times"/Siena polling. We've seen the CNN polling. Joe Biden's underperforming with all of the key groups he needs, young people...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 ...Black voters. Black men are, in a, in a large part, moving toward Trump in a way we haven't seen in a Republican candidate in 20 years. So, I think the White House needs to be open-eyed about the struggle that is ahead.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS NOTCH KEY WINS IN 2023 RACES\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, listen, there's one thing to, there's one thing to move, but I think they're flirting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They're not moving. And at the end of the day, Black women will essentially...\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Will never go near \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And why should we? But I also think this, this electoral anxiety that people tend to want Democrats to have, it's misplaced. What Democrats should be focusing on right now, they have elect, electoral anxiety and they cannot get Mr., Mr. Sleep Pillow to put him to bed, is go out and register new voters.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They need to begin to communicate where people live, where they work, where they play, and where they pray. Democrats need to continue to talk about the things that Biden is doing to help everyday Americans, the fact that prices are coming down, it's taken a while, but Biden has the receipts, meaning he has done the work and that's what Democrats need to focus on.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 But, yeah. "Don't, don't agonize. Organize," is the saying. But that, that advice could be applied to Joe Biden himself, who, when he goes to the South Lawn of the White House and faces the camera, doesn't drive a message about how he's helping everyday Americans. He stands there and litigates the polling with the White House Press Corps about...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LESS THAN ONE YEAR UNTIL 2024 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Argues about how many polls he's up, how many polls he's down.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) but why is he doing that instead of driving a message, Donna?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, look, I'm not there to give him advice, but I...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 You should be.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's why.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 They're gonna hire you after the show.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, no, I'm past my prime in doing that stuff.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'll say this (inaudible). I, I was just gonna say, I mean, we should talk about the (inaudible) one place where Democrats, I mean, their confidence is well-placed and that's the abortion issue after Tuesday. It's interesting because I was talking to both Democratic strategists and Republican strategists on Election Day, and both of them were sort of tell me they thought the abortion issue wouldn't be as salient during this election and during 2024...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...as it was during the midterms when Republicans barely flipped the House and certainly didn't take the Senate. And yet, both of them were shocked to learn that, okay. It's...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION REMAINS GALVANIZING ELECTION ISSUE POST-ROE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So how were...\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...just as big of an issue for Democrats as it was back (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, how are Republicans gonna pivot on this or are they? I mean...\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 So, I think...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...you have the most pro-life, anti-abortion rights speaker of the House that we've ever seen.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Which that will be a challenge. So, listen, I think Nikki Haley gave the road map. It's, talk about it with nuance, with compassion, saying, we need to have judgment-free from how we talk about it. And 15 weeks, that models most of Europe. That's like 69 percent of Americans, some support somewhere between 15 and 20. If you can get in a place where that's what you're talking about and say, by the way, if we are going to be...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's what Youngkin tried, though.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 If we're gonna be a pro-life party, we also have to be the party of paid family leave, greater investment in foster care. We need to be pro-life throughout life. My issue with Youngkin is, I think he, he really tried, but he didn't, he talked about it like a pro-lifer rather than trying to reach people who are on the choice side of this. I think his messaging was a bit off in it. That's where they need to be. But the wild card here is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bears the most responsibility of...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 ...any living person for the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 So, is he, is that gonna pan out on the campaign trail? If I were the Biden folks, I would be saying, he is who took down Roe. And I don't feel like that message has been going because he dances around it. I don't think people...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 ...see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as pro-life, but he is literally the most responsible for that decision.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, at one point, there is tape of him saying that the woman should be punished.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 There is.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Correct.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 It's his biggest accomplishment.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Yet, yet...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 It's his biggest accomplishment as president, overturning a half century of, of legal abortion, and he's clearly embarrassed by it now but he thinks it's a political loser.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 But he is on tape saying it and I'm sure Democrats are gonna punish him for that. Look, I think that the GOP does not have a good answer for this issue because they refuse to concede to public sentiment.\par \par \uc2 ROUNDTABLE GUEST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 The country does not want to outlaw abortion, and that has been clear in every state that has voted on it. And there's not any reflection at all among Republicans about that fact. And when you can't even talk as a party about where the, where the country is, where the voters are, and what your policy is, that's gonna create some challenges because they've refused to move off their hardline for their base.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You saw a little bit of, I thought the debate was interesting. The debate that came just 24 hours after, you know, this message was sent on abortion.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Interesting's the word, yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has backed a 15-week abortion ban nationwide. This is something he has....\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He signed a six-week...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOURTH GOP PRIMARY DEBATE SET FOR DECEMBER 6 IN ALABAMA\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  has encouraged, you know, Republicans to...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...to embrace that, thinking okay, that's a (inaudible) safe strategy, you won't be punished by swing (inaudible). Voters (inaudible) that was not the case in Virginia. And \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  didn't, you know, reiterate his position on that. In fact, he talked about how, okay, different states are gonna do different things. And that is, that's not where he was just a couple of weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP REMAINS GOP FRONTRUNNER AS RIVALS AIM TO OVERTAKE HIM\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 But, can I say, though, what Nikki Haley does that is right, and you know this better than anyone, is, there are not votes in the Senate to codify a federal ban on abortion. So, I do think it's important to remind voters this is a state issue largely. You're not gonna see greater restrictions coming from the federal level unless the makeup of the Senate fundamentally changes. But I would remind Republicans in Ohio and Kansas, Republicans voted for abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 We need to hear from our voters. The politicians in DC are disconnected from where the public is.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and not just Kansas, not just Kentucky, Montana.\par \par \uc2 ROUNDTABLE GUEST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ohio. And, and Jonathan, you know what? The pro-choice community will go one step further. They're going to get ballot initiatives across the country, starting in...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To mobilize the voters.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 That'll help Biden too, right?\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Will, so, so listen, we're, we're, we're almost out of time. But what, what was your sense hearing, to, to that reporting on, on, on Trump, who, literally thinking he could get reinstated as president?\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 I mean, just...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Even after he left the White House?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BOOK REVEALS TRUMP BELIEVED HE COULD BE REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 ...stunning and you know, you know this well. This theory emerged from QAnon, from some of the darkest corners of the fringe conspiracy on the Internet, this idea he'd be reinstated and people started to believe it. But the fact that someone who's the former Commander in Chief, very well could be again, was buying into something so absurd, so patently false, underscores how dangerous \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is. There's some incredible "New York Times" reporting from Jonathan Swan about what a second term would look like.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IS THE 2024 CAMPAIGN SHAPING UP AS A BIDEN-TRUMP REMATCH?\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA FARAH GRIFFIN (THE VIEW CO-HOST)\par \par \uc2 And I think we need to, that is what Joe Biden should be talking about, by the way, is how dangerous a second term of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would be because it's terrible. They're talking about rounding up immigrants and putting them into more or less concentration camps. He's, you know, once again would try to overthrow an election, and also wanting to punish people like myself or Chairman Milley who spoke out against him.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He, he, he wants to go after those RINOs and those Liberals like Bill Barr.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And those Never Trumpers like my good sister over here. Look, the bottom line is Joe Biden knows how to litigate this race for 2024, and it is a choice election. And he is going to point out to the American people what he has done to help improve their lives and what this other guy is going to try to do to try to destroy this country.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 As Biden likes to say, compare me to the alternative, not the Almighty.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not the Almighty. All right, we...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN (POLITICO SENIOR POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 And that's gonna be key going forward.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...we're out of time. Thank you to all of you. Still ahead, a look at the nationwide teacher shortage through the eyes of one Texas school district. It's part of our network-wide series "The American Classroom." Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020231121ejbc0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MARYLAND GOVERNOR WES MOORE DEMOCRATS NOTCH KEY WINS IN 2023 RACES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,719 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 SULLIVAN, ISRAEL, HOSTAGES, GAZA, HOSPITALS, NETANYAHU, LAWLER, MOSKOWITZ\par \par \uc2 MOORE, HARRIS, DEMOCRATS, BIDEN, 2023, VOTERS, AXELROD, MANCHIN\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM WEDNESDAY\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I think voters have been clear, regardless of whether they're in a so-called red or blue state, that one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the Government should not be telling a woman what to do with her body. And so, it was a good night. And the President and I obviously have a lot of work to do to earn our reelection, but I am confident we're gonna win.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS NOTCH KEY WINS IN 2023 RACES\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That was Vice President Harris fresh off big Democratic wins on Tuesday night in multiple states, driven in large part by support for abortion rights. So, what does it all mean for 2024? We're joined now by Maryland's Democratic Governor, Wes Moore. And you're obviously a member of the Biden/Harris advisory team.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for being here, Governor. You were out campaigning. You were campaigning in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was the message that you heard from voters?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, the energy was real, and, and, and people were, were motivated not by the, not by the, the, the - partisan issues. They were - motivated by the issues of actually things getting done in a bipartisan way. And I think that's what we saw in Virginia, where we were able to, you know, have now the first African American Speaker of the House, a complete repudiation of the type of things that, that Governor Youngkin was talking about, about which week should you do an abortion ban? They were talking about things like jobs and infrastructure, and it resonated with the people. And I think that's the message that is going to be continued to push, and why, I think, we're gonna continue, seeing how the people will continue to resonate with these kind of messages.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO EXIT POLL: 73% OF VOTERS DON'T WANT BIDEN TO RUN\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's, it's no doubt that abortion hurt Republicans in Virginia, hurt them in Ohio, hurt them in Kentucky, but you still have these concerns about President Biden. In - in Ohio, where abortion rights, strong support for abortion rights, you saw 73 percent in the exit poll. Seventy-three percent of those who voted said that they do not, they would prefer somebody other than Biden to run. And that's even more that 63 percent said they would prefer somebody other than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to run. So, how does President Biden deal with these questions?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 I mean, I know there's still, you know, there's still the idea and the handwringing of what polls look like a year away from Election Day. And, you know, I'm, I'm, I'm not a pundit.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're not concerned about this at all, concerns about his age (inaudible) ?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 I'm, I'm not. I mean, I, I think about where the polls were for my race. A year before Election Day, I was polling a little over one percent. By Election Day, I ended up winning with more individual votes than anyone who's ever run for governor in the history of the state of Maryland. I think, when, when you're looking at polls a year out, they are worth the paper that they are written on. And I think when you continue looking at the work that's being done and the product that's being produced, just this past week, we saw how over $7 billion of investment was coming to the state of Maryland for infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 We announced a couple weeks back that, you know, a quarter of a billion going towards broadband and Wi-Fi construction. We are actually rebuilding things in a bipartisan way. And when you think about what people are asking for, bipartisan leadership, and you can get things done, the PACT Act, the Bipartisan Infrastructure Act, that's President Biden. And I think that will show up in the - in the, in the election for next year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOW BIDEN POLL NUMBERS WORRY SOME DEMOCRATS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But let me ask you then about what David Axelrod said. Now, David Axelrod, obviously, one of President Obama's top political strategists, smart guy, Democrat, supportive of President Biden, but he said this, "Only \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can make this decision about running again. If he continues to run, he will be the nominee of the Democratic Party. What he needs to decide is whether that is wise, whether it is in his best interest or the country's." The suggestion here, obviously, is that he shouldn't run. And that's from Axelrod. What do you, what do you say to him?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 I, I would say President Biden has already made the decision. He's running.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Clearly.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 He's, he is running for reelection. And listen, I, I, I think about, I think about what's happening in our state, right, where we are, we have now literally announced billions of dollars of infrastructure that's gonna be happening. We're, we're now for the first time going to be putting east-west transit within the Baltimore region, which is gonna be monumental when it comes to economic growth within, within the state of Maryland. We're looking at the fact that now we've been able to, now Maryland has a lowest unemployment rate in the entire country, right?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 We are moving fast and we're making sure that we're leaving no one behind in the process, but that's being done because we're working in partnership with the Biden administration. So, I would just, I would just, and, and we'll continue to make sure that people remember this is about performance, not personalities. And that's why his performance is the reason that I believe deeply that the American people will give him a second term.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEST VIRGINIA'S MANCHIN ANNOUNCES RETIREMENT FROM SENATE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So what about Manchin? Joe Manchin announced he's not running for reelection to the Senate. He's clearly talking about running for party as a, running for president on, as a third party ticket, No Labels. He's talking about trying to have a movement to mobilize the middle in this country. What, what's your message to Joe Manchin?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 My message to, to Joe Manchin is, I, I thank him for his service. And I think he's had a, a year, a, a career of distinguished service both as a governor...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Forty-two years in public office.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 That's right, both as a governor, senator. I would urge him not to mar his legacy by getting involved in something so foolish.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So foolish, why?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Because if you know what No Labels is, No Labels literally has no plan, has no path, has no policy platform. They don't even have a candidate. What No Labels is, it's a, it's a, it's a configuration made up of dark money that won't disclose its donors, but is frankly just going to simply hand an election off by, by, by being able to not actually come up with a solution, but just continuing to throw wood into this flame of disillusionment. It is not real.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much, how much of is a threat, though, is the idea of a No Labels candidate, Cornell West, you have Jill Stein running again as the Green Party candidate and running for the Green Party nomination. Bobby Kennedy Jr. is out there. Could we see third-party candidates cost Biden his election, actually get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 No. Because I, I, I think what, what President Biden is gonna continue to show is that results do matter. You know, it's, it's, it's one thing to, to say we're going to rail against the system, and it's another thing to actually work to make systems better. And that's what I think President Biden has continued to show. You know, when you think about the, the bills that he has passed, the work that he has done all throughout this country in urban, rural, and suburban parts of this country, about economic growth and economic upliftment, about being able to make sure the people's freedoms are actually protected and everybody is seen in conversations and not just some, that's what President Biden has been able to push on.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 That's what he, what's he's been able to get done, not rhetoric, not, not, not, not handwringing, not, not fist-banging, but actually real, productive results for people of his country. And so, I think all the other things will just sound like noise while - President Biden's results will sound like actually what they are, real, productive momentum for the people of this country.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Governor Wes Moore of Maryland, thank you for joining us. And on this Veterans' Day weekend, thank you for your service as well.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 Thank you (inaudible). Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, the bizarre plot \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  believed could get him back into the White House before the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020231121ejbc0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LOOMING GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN EFFECTS IF CONGRESS FAILS TO REACH AN AGREEMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,308 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL-\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR: CRITICAL CONDITION\par \par \uc2 GAZA, HOSPITALS, ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, DIPLOMATS, WARNING, IMAGE, XI\par \par \uc2 ADAMS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , SEARCH, SEIZURE, PHONE, IPAD, FUNDRAISING\par \par \uc2 U.S., CREDIT RATING, MOODY'S, NEGATIVE, DOWNGRADES\par \par \uc2 MCSALLY, ATTACK, INVESTIGATION, HENTON\par \par \uc2 HARBOUGH, BANNED, LAWSUIT, MICHIGAN, WALTERS, THAMEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHIGAN TAKES LEGAL ACTION AFTER BIG TEN SIDELINES COACH: UNIVERSITY FILES FOR TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER FOR HARBAUGH SUSPENSION\par \par \uc2 LUDWIG, SHOOTING, STRAY BULLET, TAYLOR, FRESHMAN\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , AMPTP, DRESCHER, CRABTREE-IRELAND, SALLOUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  BOARD VOTES ON TENTATIVE AGREEMENT: WHAT'S IN THE DEAL THAT ENDED THE 118-DAY WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 SHUTDOWN, ELECTIONS, POLL, ECONOMY, INFLATION, MANCHIN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alright, we do start this half hour with a look at this week's top political headlines and White House correspondent MaryAlice Parks is back with ABC political, deputy political director Averi Harper. Good morning to both of you.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Got you the coffee mugs in the mix. Get you going on a Saturday. MaryAlice, let's start with you because we've now talked about this a couple times, the looming government shutdown, apparently it's back again. The new House Speaker, this will be a big test for him.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOOMING GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN: EFFECTS IF CONGRESS FAILS TO REACH AN AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is there any indication that they're going to be able to avoid this?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first, government shutdowns are costly.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is expensive for these agencies to have to shut down programs, start them again. They can't plan. They tell us that they just can't do their work. And we know that some essential programs like relief for and aid for baby formula, food for some of the poorest kids and moms in the country, all that is at risk. Air traffic controllers would be asked to work without pay. This time, even members of the military would be asked to work without pay.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we know that Speaker, the, the new Speaker, Mike Johnson, is planning to introduce a bill later today. The big question is, what exactly will be in it? Democrats are worried it could include, still, some Republican proposals on abortion or the border and that would make it almost completely a non-starter in the Senate. Remember, that's what he did with Israel funding, he tacked on cuts to the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , even though he knew that Democrats were just not gonna take that up.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll definitely keep an eye on that but we're also just a few days away from a big election, Averi.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S ON VOTERS' MINDS: ECONOMY & INFLATION TOP THE LIST\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we know that, we, you saw again, this week, that when abortion's directly on the ballot, voters are coming out and demanding abortion access even in red states like Ohio. Are parties changing their strategies after these results?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, abortion is really a losing issue for Republicans, especially when it's explicitly on the ballot like we saw in Ohio earlier this weekend. With the possibility of it being on the ballot in big battleground states next year, like Florida and Arizona, I think we're already starting to see some shifts in the messaging around this. Within the anti-abortion movement there's this, a real push to use the word "limit" to describe restrictive abortion legislation rather than the word "ban."\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we can even look to some of what the candidates said on the debate stage earlier this week, too. Nikki Haley calling for consensus saying that those who are pro-abortion should not be demonized. Tim Scott calling for policy that addresses the needs of helping women and children after the babies are born. They are all attempts to bring people into the tent on this. Whether it works is gonna be a different story.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion a huge issue, but also our ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  polls actually showing that the economy is really driving this election next year. So, what are voters saying? How are they feeling?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right. When you look at our latest ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll, what we found is that Americans say that the economy and inflation are their top concerns ahead of the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP ISSUES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 74% ECONOMY VERY IMPORTANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 69% INFLATION VERY IMPORTANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 35% TRUST REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 25% TRUST DEMOCRATS\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And there are more Americans that trust Republicans to tackle those issues over Democrats. So, when we talk to the Biden administration, they point to factors like job growth or the unemployment rate and say, "Well, the economy's doing fine," but I'll tell you, our reporters are fanned out across the country. They're talking to voters all over the place and there's a real negative perception about the state of the economy. There's this feeling that costs have gone up for food, for gas, for housing and that wages haven't kept up. That's something that the Biden campaign should be worried about entering the election year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN JOE MANCHIN NOT SEEKING RE-ELECTION: IS HE EYEING A RUN FOR PRESIDENT?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alright, speaking of 2024, let's go back to MaryAlice Parks on this one because Joe Manchin might be causing some kind of domino effect here, saying he's not gonna run in the Senate now. That will hurt Democrats but also, could he run on some kind of unity ticket and what would that mean?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first in the Senate...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For president, that is.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, right, but first, let's talk about the Senate. So, put aside West Virginia. Democrats also have to defend Senate seats in Ohio, Michigan, Montana, Arizona, Nevada. I mean, we are looking at a really tough map for Democrats next year. So, this definitely makes it harder for them to hold the Senate. Not impossible, but tough. And then, of course, the big question about whether or not he's considering a run for president as an Independent. His team is not ruling that out. The White House has to be worried.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They put out a statement publicly just thanking Joe Manchin for his service, for their work together. But the irony is here, that while he might not pull Democratic base voters he could run potentially pitching himself as this alternative for never-Trump Republicans. But in doing so, could he end up actually being the reason Trump wins if Trump's the nominee and he runs as an Independent and siphons votes away from Biden? That's what people in Washington are worried about, Democrats in Washington are worried about.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are already some Independents, you know, running. Well, you have RFK, Jr., you've got Jill Stein. I mean, this could be a really interesting race...\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...in so many ways. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's good to have you.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you so much. So much to watch, so many twists and turns.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231212ejbb00034\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT KEY RACES ACROSS COUNTRY WITH IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, DEMOCRATS, ABORTION, REPUBLICANS, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 DEMOCRATS, ELECTIONS, REPUBLICANS, BESHEAR, YOUNGKIN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Mary, thanks very much. Let's bring in our chief Washington correspondent \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 . And, Jon, let's take a look at the overall results right now. President Biden may not be very popular, but Democrats continued their winning streak on the power of this abortion rights issue.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, Republicans have been on a remarkably consistent losing streak with very few exceptions, going all the way back to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's victory in 2016. And this one, despite Biden's unpopularity, despite the concerns about the economy, you saw Democrats beat Republicans in solidly Republican states. Kentucky, Ohio and in key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There was a key race in Pennsylvania as well as those legislative races Mary talked about in Virginia. So this, abortion in these races was overwhelming the issue. The only place Republicans scored a significant victory was in Mississippi, where abortion was not on the ballot. So, you know, look, Biden still has problems but consider this, in Kentucky, since 2003, the party that won the governor's race went on to win the presidency. That's every presidential race over the last 20 years.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You mentioned Kentucky. Contrasting nights for two possibly future presidential hopefuls, the Governor of Kentucky, the Governor of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the contrast couldn't be more stark. In Virginia, \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  had been hoping for a victory to recapture the legislature in Virginia to propel him to the national stage. Some Republicans who are pro Youngkin thought this could be a chance for him to actually run for president next year. He lost. Beshear, that victory, George, you can imagine, without doubt, he will be talked about as a future national candidate in 2028.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb80002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REPUBLICANS GEAR UP FOR THIRD PRIMARY DEBATE WHAT TO WATCH FOR AS FIVE PRESIDENTIAL HOPEFULS FACE OFF\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, DEMOCRATS, ABORTION, REPUBLICANS, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 DEMOCRATS, ELECTIONS, REPUBLICANS, BESHEAR, YOUNGKIN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, REPUBLICANS, DESANTIS, HALEY, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 , thanks very much. Republican debate tonight, Republican presidential debate. Let's bring in Rachel Scott for a preview. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS GEAR UP FOR THIRD PRIMARY DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO WATCH FOR AS FIVE PRESIDENTIAL HOPEFULS FACE OFF\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning to you. The third Republican debate kicks off here in Miami in just a matter of hours. And this will be the smallest stage yet. Five Republican candidates have qualified for tonight's debate. But all eyes will be on Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley. DeSantis will be on his home turf tonight. He's long been seen as the top rival to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But he's also been slipping in the polls, and Nikki Haley has been gaining momentum. Haley and DeSantis already clashing on a number of issues, from foreign policy and how they should respond to the war raging in Israel, to also the issue of abortion. DeSantis supports a six week abortion ban here in Florida, a 15 week abortion week nationwide.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Haley has called federal bans on abortion unrealistic. Missing from the stage tonight of course is former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He'll be holding a rally just a few miles away. It's not only a smaller stage, the field is also growing smaller. Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  dropping out of the race, struggling to break through, just like the others, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb80002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT KEY RACES ACROSS COUNTRY AND IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, DEMOCRATS, ABORTION, REPUBLICANS, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 DEMOCRATS, ELECTIONS, REPUBLICANS, BESHEAR, YOUNGKIN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, REPUBLICANS, DESANTIS, HALEY, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRAIL, FRAUD, TESTIMONY, IVANKA\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, GAZA, CIVILIANS, HAND, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NETANYAHU, PAUSE, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 TLAIB, HOUSE, CENSURE, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , PALESTINIANS\par \par \uc2 CREDIT CARD, DEBT, BALANCES, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DENSE FOG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, TRIAL, HILL, JURORS, GRIFFIN\par \par \uc2 VENCILL, AMERICAN AIRLINES, UNACCOMPANIED, MISPLACED\par \par \uc2 PANDAS, NATIONAL ZOO, CHINA, RETURN, SMITH\par \par \uc2 NEWLYWED, MARRIED, DAISY, ADOPT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANTA ANA WINDS\par \par \uc2 DEMOCRATS, ELECTION, ABORTION, OHIO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY RACES ACROSS COUNTRY AND IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's start with a look at the top stories breaking at 8:00, the election results across the country. Top story, we're going to look at what they could mean for 2024. And Ohio has delivered a message with national implications. They approved a measure protecting abortion rights. Let's go back to Mary Bruce in Columbus. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning again, George. Yeah, this was a big night for Democrats, winning in some key races, showing the political potency of the fight for abortion rights and giving Democrats a big boost with the presidential election now just one year away. Here in red-leaning Ohio, voters enshrining the right to an abortion into the state's constitution, a clear sign that abortion is the issue energizing the party's base.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Kentucky, a rare democratic governor re-elected in a red state, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  running against the state's total ban on abortion to defeat the Trump-backed candidate, Daniel Cameron. And in Virginia, Governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  there tried to carve out middle ground on abortion, promising to pass what he called reasonable restrictions if Republicans won control of the state legislature, but it didn't work, Democrats actually gaining seats there to retake control. The big question now, guys, will this momentum translate to an unpopular President Biden? Will any of this quiet concerns about his 2024 run, Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is the big question. Okay, Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb80003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT KEY RACES ACROSS COUNTRY WITH IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, DEMOCRATS, ABORTION, REPUBLICANS, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Ohio possibly delivering a message with national implications approving a measure protecting abortion rights. Mary Bruce is in Columbus, Ohio, with the latest on that and the key races. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY RACES ACROSS COUNTRY WITH IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Yeah, this was a huge night for Democrats, scoring big wins in several races, proving the political potency of the fight for abortion and giving the party a big boost with the presidential election now just a year away.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, Democrats on a winning streak, scoring victories in Ohio, Kentucky, and Virginia, powered by support for abortion rights. In Ohio, voters enshrining a right to abortion access in the state's constitution. It's the seventh straight victory for abortion rights in a state referendum since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS SCORE BIG WINS ON ELECTION NIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO VOTERS APPROVE MEASURE PROTECTING ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 LAUREN BLAUVELT (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR PLANNED PARENTHOOD OHIO)\par \par \uc2 Abortion access is the law of the land in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 14 point win in the red leaning state, a strong sign for Democrats that abortion is the issue energizing the party's base.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How important is the issue of abortion?\par \par \uc2 OHIO RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I think it's number one on the ballot right now.\par \par \uc2 OHIO RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Women's rights are under attack.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The big question now, will this momentum translate to an unpopular President Biden? In deep red Kentucky, Trump backed candidate, Republican \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , tried to take down Democratic Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  by linking him to Biden, but it didn't work.\par \par \uc2 GOV ANDY BESHEAR (DEM) (KENTUCKY)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Beshear carved out his own brand as a popular bipartisan problem solver and ran against Kentucky's total ban on abortion, winning even as Republicans swept every other state wide office.\par \par \uc2 GOV ANDY BESHEAR (DEM) (KENTUCKY)\par \par \uc2 Kentucky made a choice. A choice not to move to the right or to the left, but to move forward for every single family.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Virginia, the Republican Governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , tried to stake out middle ground on abortion, promising if Republicans won the state legislature they'd pass what he called reasonable restriction, 15 week abortion ban with exceptions for rape, incest and the life of the mother. But it backfired.\par \par \uc2 VIRGINIA STATE OFFICIAL (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The people of the commonwealth of Virginia have spoken.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats not only holding on to the state's senate, but retaking the house of delegates, too.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORY IN PHILADELPHIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHERELLE PARKS ELECTED CITY'S FIRST FEMALE MAYOR\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And where abortion wasn't an issue, Republicans won easily. In Mississippi, Republican Governor \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  winning reelection there. The Democrat, Brandon Presley, underperforming. And, guys, in Philadelphia this morning, history being made. \uc2 Cherelle Parker\uc2  now the city's first female mayor. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb80002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KEY ELECTION TAKEAWAYS DEMOCRATS CELEBRATE VICTORIES IN SEVERAL STATES\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AIRSTRIKES, SYRIA\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOSTAGE NEGOTIATIONS INTENSIFY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL FRAUD, TRIAL, JAMES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IVANKA TRUMP TAKES THE STAND\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, YETMAN, STASI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR JANUARY 6TH SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 FIRE, EXPLOSION, EVACUATIONS, CAPERS, HARFIELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUGE PLANT FIRE FORCES EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, HARRIS, ABORTION, BESHEAR, YOUNGKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY ELECTION TAKEAWAYS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, five Republican candidates who want to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the Republican nomination will debate. They are at least 40 points behind Trump. It all comes after the election yesterday, voters protecting abortion rights in this country from Ohio to Virginia. And a Democratic governor in Kentucky, of course, a deep red state, winning re-election. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS CELEBRATE VICTORIES IN SEVERAL STATES\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Democrats pointing to victories in Virginia, Kentucky, and Ohio as proof abortion is increasingly the issue that decides elections.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The voters said, look, the government should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden declaring, "Democracy won and MAGA lost." And in an attempt to dismiss his own sliding poll numbers, he added, "Voters vote. Polls don't." In Ohio, voters overwhelmingly choosing to protect abortion rights in the state constitution. In Virginia, voters rejected the Republican governor's effort to flip the state legislature from Democratic control. He promised to sign a 15-week abortion ban with exceptions, casting it as a compromise. Voters rejected that.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 I'm a little disappointed, to be clear.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in the south, a rare red state Democratic governor winning re-election, fending off his opponent's effort to tie him to President Biden.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR ANDY BESHEAR (DEM) (KENTUCKY)\par \par \uc2 It was a victory that sends a loud, clear message. A message that candidates should run for something and not against someone. That a candidate should show vision, and not sew division.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  winning despite President Biden's low approval ratings. The President is hoping to turn those around. Tonight, his Republican challengers will take the stage for the third Republican presidential debate. Of course, all of them still trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by more than 40 points. And Trump sitting this one out once again, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, you'll be following the debate for us. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTER & JAMES BIDEN SUBPOENAED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On Capitol Hill, the House Oversight Committee issuing subpoenas for the testimony of members of President Biden's family, including his brother James Biden, and son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The committee escalating its investigation. So far, chairman James Comer's committee has produced no evidence of crimes by the President. Today, the White House dismissed the impeachment inquiry as a baseless smear campaign that has turned up zero evidence.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231110ejb800007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PUSHBACK TO THE POLLS BATTLE OVER ABORTION RIGHTS\b0\par\par\uc2 2,098 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DEAL, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, ABORTION, FRICK, BLAUVELT, REGAN, CARTER\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the pushback at the polls. While voters consistently rank inflation and the economy as their top concerns, yesterday's election made clear that putting abortion on the ballot can motivate people to the polls.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "NIGHTLINE", YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE, ONE YEAR OUT, 2024\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Part of our ABC News series "Your Voice, Your Vote: One Year Out," here's ABC's Eva pilgrim.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 So, let's get into this right now. Start to take a big, big breath in. And then take a full exhale breath out.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the wall of her yoga studio is a word written in neon and sacred to Sarah Frick.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Grace is giving people the opportunity to try again. Right?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the name of her firstborn, who died at just 3 days old from a birth defect. When she got pregnant again, she says doctors told her that baby would likely also face the same issue. She then chose to terminate that pregnancy, a decision she says forced her to give Grace to herself.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 It was an awful decision I had to make, but I made it. And I can't imagine having to make it while at the same time having to justify it.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Could you imagine what the alternative was?\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, having another baby that would die. And that is why I think that choice is so important because, you know, we need more than one chance.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That painful and personal choice was one Sarah was able to make because there were fewer restrictions at that time in South Carolina, where she lives. Shortly after, she met Ashley Regan in one of her yoga classes and shared with her what she'd been through.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is not black and white. After you listen to this story, what these families go through is devastating.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ashley says Sarah's personal story made her feel everyone should have access to an abortion without restriction, a view that was cemented by the overturning of Roe v. Wade last year. But Ashley says she knows her position isn't in line with her political party.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm curious, do you guys, if you identify as Republican or Democrat?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm a Republican.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I'm a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ashley says, she never considered ether she was for abortion rights or not.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 The moment that Roe fell, I sent her a screenshot. And it's not like we, anything we had talked about, I just knew that, all of a sudden, because of this, we were going to battle.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you think women in South Carolina are talking about this? Do you think it's really a voting issue?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Behind closed doors? Yes. Away from their husbands? Yes. Away from social media? Yes. They're not taking it to the streets. I'm hoping they take it to the ballots.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And yesterday, in Ohio, they did. Voters there passing an amendment to enshrine abortion rights into their constitution. A state that's gone Republican in the last two presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN BLAUVELT (OHIOANS UNITED FOR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS CAMPAIGN)\par \par \uc2 And abortion access is the law of the land in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ohio became the seventh state to protect abortion rights since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June 2021.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We've seen abortion turn folks out not only in blue states, not only in the battleground states, but in ruby red states as well. And so, it is definitely something that should be of concern to Republican candidates and campaigns heading into the election year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BANNED OR RESTRICTED ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, at least 16 states have enacted near total bans on abortion with five more restricting access after the first trimester. All 21 states, Republican-led. That's despite the majority of Americans, 62%, who say abortion should be legal in all or most cases. And earlier tonight on the debate stage in Miami, it was clear that the issue is top of mind for a number of GOP candidates as well.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Let's find consensus. Let's agree on what, how we can ban late-term abortions.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TIM SCOTT (REP-SC) (2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I would certainly, as president of the United States, have a 15-week national limit.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Senator Tim Scott and Nikki Haley are both from South Carolina, a deeply red state where abortion was legal until the 22 weeks for the first year after Roe fell unlike surrounding states. It became an unexpected oasis for southerners seeking an abortion. The last southern holdout. During that time, Sarah and Ashley fundraised and protested for abortion rights, even testifying before the South Carolina state legislature.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party that I have grown up knowing as a conservative, middle of the road, heartbeat of America, is gone. And it's leaving voters feeling confused, betrayed, and left behind. South Carolina has an opportunity, excuse me, to be on the right side of history.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 You know, in the south, we're taught to, like, kind of be quiet and polite. And we weren't very polite about this.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 No. That was probably the hardest part, as a Republican, the hardest part.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They eventually lost their battle in August this year when a new all-male court, the only one of its kind in the country, upheld a six-week abortion ban. Now, the closest state for southerners to get an abortion is in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have you ever thought about leaving South Carolina?\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 I don't think leaving is going to make a difference. You have to stay to make a change.\par \par \uc2 SARAH FRICK (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY REGAN (SOUTH CAROLINA VOTER / YOGA INSTRUCTOR)\par \par \uc2 Which is why I'm still in the Republican Party. I can't, I'm not going to make any changes in the Republican Party if I leave.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But trying to change the Republican stance on abortion from within isn't always possible. 2,000 miles away in Arizona, Heather Carter says she learned that lesson the hard way.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 I was actually defeated in my Republican primary over this issue. I stood up for what I believed.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She served as a Republican in the Arizona state legislature for nearly a decade and says there was no room for nuance on abortion.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 When I was asked when I was first running for office to check a box pro-life, pro-choice, I picked pro-life. When I got down to the Capitol, I realized there's a lot more conversations that needed to be had in this space.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Carter was chairwoman of the House Health Committee, which took up the state's proposed abortion bills.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 I was newly elected. There was probably the most comprehensive abortion bill that we had seen in Arizona that was being brought forth. And I tried to talk to people about what the unintended consequences of this bill would be, and it was really, really stressful.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why were you so stressed out during that time?\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 Because I was asking questions, and people were trying to stop me from asking questions. And I was bringing up concerns with the legislation. And next thing I know, I'm like clenching my teeth and grinding my teeth.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It got so bad, she says she needed oral surgery, which caused her to miss the vote on that controversial bill.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was the response from your Republican colleagues as you started to speak up and voice concern about the nuance of it all?\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 When you speak up against a position that is in your party, many times, you are ostracized.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why speak up?\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 Because it's the right thing to do. When you are a female legislator and a mother, you bring your experience to the Capitol. So, it's really important to really follow your gut based upon your own experiences.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Following her gut on abortion cost her her job. She left the Republican Party and is now an independent, an increasingly powerful voting bloc in Arizona that has the potential to swing elections.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Arizona has this long tradition of independent voters. What makes elections in the state nail-biters is because folks are not voting along party lines, but are rather voting with their conscience. There is the potential for those voters who swing one way or the other when it comes to a particular candidate or issue.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Carter says, if Arizona tries to ban abortion outright with a ballot measure next year, it will fail.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER CARTER (REP) (FORMER ARIZONA STATE SENATOR)\par \par \uc2 I think a hardline stance without any exceptions is not where the voters of Arizona are. It's not going to work in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As it is now, abortion in Arizona is legal up to 15 weeks, but several battles are underway to restrict access even further. Democrats are pushing to put abortion on the ballot next year, similar to what Ohio just did. Dr. DeShawn Taylor is on the frontline of the fight.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (SOLO PRACTITIONER DESERT STAR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 It's hard to say the word hope in Arizona as an abortion provider.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's been the solo practitioner of her own clinic in Phoenix for ten years. Before Roe, she could perform abortions up to 24 weeks. Now, because of the limited window, she has fewer patients and what she says is the heavy burden of having to turn some away.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (SOLO PRACTITIONER DESERT STAR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 In that anguish, that horrible cry that people have when they realize that they have to stay pregnant, it is something that I, it's haunting. I don't ever want to hear it.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's now channeling that pain into political action. Once an independent voter, she's now a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (SOLO PRACTITIONER DESERT STAR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 It is very interesting that the majority of people who are creating these legislations, restricting people's access to reproductive health care have absolutely no idea of how reproductive functions work. Oh, there's a question in the chat.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Every week, Dr. Taylor meets with a group focused on turning the Arizona legislature blue.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (SOLO PRACTITIONER DESERT STAR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 My hope doesn't lie with the people who run this state. The people that I'm on the ground fighting with, advocating with, trying to strategize proactive policies with, that is where the hope lies.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACHEL PLATTEN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, singer Rachel Platt shares the difficult times that led to her writing her latest song, "Girls."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020231110ejb800003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ELECTION DAY IN AMERICA WHAT'S AT STAKE ACROSS THE COUNTRY AS VOTERS GO TO THE POLLS\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S AT STAKE ACROSS THE COUNTRY AS VOTERS GO TO THE POLLS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big question. What message will voters be sending looking ahead to 2024. The state of Ohio getting a lot of attention because the issue of abortion is on the ballot. Mary Bruce is in Columbus with the details and then the key races to watch around the country. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well, it is election day in several states and cities. The country closely watching these races for signs of what is to come in the upcoming presidential race. Now, here in Ohio, as you can see, the polls are open.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS ON THE BALLOT IN OHIO\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the ballot, whether to enshrine abortion access into the state's constitution. This is a key test for Democrats who are looking to see just how much this issue will motivate voters next year, especially as we have seen those concerns about President Biden's dismal approval rating. Now, we have seen in other states, voters coming out to protect abortion rights, even in deep red states. And, George, voters here tell me this issue is mission critical.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And abortion is going to play a big role in the Virginia races as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY RACES ACROSS THE COUNTRY WITH IMPLICATIONS FOR 2024\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is, George. Now, look, the governor there is not on the ballot, but \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  is certainly hoping that this issue will motivate voters. He is promising to pass a 15-week abortion ban if voters deliver him a Republican-controlled state legislature. He's promising to act on a host of issues if he simply has the team to back him up. And George, of course, lingering over that race, those questions, those lingering whispers about whether \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  will be a late entry to challenge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in this presidential race.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there are two big governors' races.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are, George. Take a look at this. You have, down in Kentucky, the popular Democratic governor there, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 . He's looking for a second term in that Republican-dominated state. And his challenger Daniel Cameron, though, is trying very hard to tie him to President Biden. And down in Mississippi, this is a really incredible race, a very tight, surprisingly tight race between an unpopular incumbent who is now mired in a welfare fund scandal. His opponent, George, get this, only in Mississippi, he's also a cousin of Elvis Pressley. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is something. Mary Bruce, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does she have to say with my home state of Mississippi? What are you trying to say there, Mary? Okay.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb700002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ELECTION DAY IN AMERICA WHAT'S AT STAKE ACROSS THE COUNTRY\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S AT STAKE ACROSS THE COUNTRY AS VOTERS GO TO THE POLLS\par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, CIVIL FRAUD, JAMES, ENGORON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CLASHES WITH JUDGE ON THE STAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S TENSE TESTIMONY IN NY CIVIL FRAUD CASE\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU, GUTERRES, MOKHALLALATI, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR\par \par \uc2 TERROR THREAT, WAR, PROTESTS, KESSLER, HOMICIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. TENSIONS RISE AS MIDEAST CONFLICT RAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JEWISH MAN DIES AFTER INCIDENT AT CALIFORNIA PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GUN BAN, DOMESTIC ABUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TAKES UP GUN CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL REVIEW BAN ON GUNS FOR DOMESTIC ABUSERS\par \par \uc2 STAND UP FOR HEROES, SPRINGSTEEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRINGSTEEN'S "STAND UP FOR HEROES" SURPRISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BOSS RETURNS TO STAGE TO PERFORM AT ANNUAL EVENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "LOVE ACTUALLY"\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, GUATEMALA, NG, SHARPE\par \par \uc2 DRUG BUST, FENTANYL, LEVY, MILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE DRUG BUST IN MASSACHUSETTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEIZURE INCLUDING FENTANYL SHAPED LIKE VALENTINE'S CANDY\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, DEALS, STREAKS, DEMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEAST MODE...FOR FREE?!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE TO SCORE THANKSGIVING DINNER GOALS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE BASKETBALL, JOHNSON, WATKINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEGAN FOX OPENS UP, 8:15\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, AMERICA, OHIO, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S AT STAKE ACROSS THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First, a look at the top stories breaking at 8:00, starting with election day. Big question, what message will voters be sending as we head to 2024. The state of Ohio getting a lot of attention because the issue of abortion is on the ballot. Want to go back to Mary Bruce in Columbus. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning again, George. Well, it is election day in several states and cities, the country, as you said, closely watching for signs of what is to come in the upcoming presidential race. Now, here in Ohio, as you can see, the polls are now open. On the ballot here today, whether abortion access should be enshrined into the state's constitution. This, of course, is a key test for Democrats, who are looking to see how much this issue will motivate voters next year, especially given concerns about the president's low approval rating, but voters here tell me this issue is mission critical. We are closely watching Virginia, where the governor there is hoping that abortion will also be top of mind for voters. \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  is promising to pass a 15-week abortion ban if Republicans win the state legislature. Now, Youngkin is not on the ballot there, but two governors are on the ballots are, in Mississippi and Kentucky. Robin, lots of races to keep a close eye on today.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, now, tell us a little nugget that you know about Mississippi. Go ahead, it's okay. You said it in the 7:00 hour. You can share it again.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, I have nothing but love for Mississippi. This is a, my favorite fact of the day. The candidate down there happens to just be a cousin of Elvis Presley. Just for you, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Only in Mississippi. That's right, thank you, Mary, appreciate you, as always.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231207ejb70000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ELECTION DAY SHOWDOWNS WATCHING KEY RACES & ISSUES IN OHIO, KENTUCKY, & VIRGINIA\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TERROR THREAT, SECURITY, MERRELL, MANGER\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: FIGHTING IN "HEART" OF GAZA CITY\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , KESSLER, FRYHOFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JEWISH DEMONSTRATOR'S DEATH INVESTIGATED\par \par \uc2 SPANGLER, YOUNGKIN, CAMERON, BESHEAR, BOWER, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY SHOWDOWNS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is election night in America, one year now until the presidential election. But there are key races tonight. And the issue of abortion driving voters from Ohio to Virginia, and what this could signal. Mary Bruce from Ohio tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WATCHING KEY RACES & ISSUES IN OHIO, KENTUCKY, & VIRGINIA\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, all eyes on voters from Ohio to Virginia to Kentucky for signs of what's to come in the presidential race, now just one year away. In Ohio, a state that's been leaning red, a big test for Democrats. Voters deciding whether to enshrine the right to an abortion in the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO EXIT POLLS, ABORTION SHOULD BE LEGAL IN ALL OR MOST CASES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YES: 61%; NO: 36%\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Preliminary exit polls show they overwhelmingly think abortion should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How important is this issue to you?\par \par \uc2 SAMANTHA SPANGLER (OHIO VOTER)\par \par \uc2 Extremely important. It determines whether or not I'm going to continue living here.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But for Republicans like Joyce and John Bower, who voted against the amendment, abortion won't be their top issue next year.\par \par \uc2 JOYCE BOWER (OHIO VOTER)\par \par \uc2 The economy is really bad. I mean, really, it really is. We need to go back Republican or maybe an alternative, independent. I will not vote for Biden.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Kentucky, a rare Democratic governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , challenged by Attorney General \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , who's been eager to tie him to the President.\par \par \uc2 DANIEL CAMERON\uc2  (REP) (KENTUCKY ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , there's not a dime's bit of difference between them.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bashear keeping his distance from the White House.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR ANDY BESHEAR (DEM) (KENTUCKY)\par \par \uc2 I run as a proud Democrat. But you saw the moment I won, I took that hat off and I served every single family.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Virginia, the popular Republican Governor Glenn Youngkin not on the ballot this year, but campaigning hard for Republicans to recapture control of the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 Hold the House, flip the Senate.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There, too, abortion top of mind for voters. Youngkin says, if Republicans control the governor's mansion and the statehouse, they will ban abortion after 15 weeks with exceptions for rape, incest, and life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLEN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 I think this is a chance for Virginia to prove to be a leader to bring people together around one of the most difficult topics in America. And I think we can lead here.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, Ohio and Virginia are key battleground states, critical to the upcoming presidential election. Democrats tonight hoping that abortion will prove to be a powerful motivating issue that will continue to drive voters to the polls. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know you'll be tracking it right into the night for us. Mary Bruce, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SUPER FOG PILEUP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the deadly pileup in Louisiana yet again. Drivers blinded by smog and smoke, the collisions closing down parts of Interstate 10 east of downtown New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Drivers blinded just before dawn today by that fog and smoke from marsh fires. Police responding to a number of accidents. At least one person has been killed. It was just last month, seven people were killed in a series of super fog pileups on I-55 outside New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231109ejb700005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE BREAK DOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, JOURNALISTS, GAZA, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , BEN-ANAT, BIDEN, BLINKEN, FINER, AID, SCALISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTTLE DIPLOMACY\par \par \uc2 IPSOS, POLL, VOTERS, BIDEN, TRUMP, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BREAKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One year from today, voters will cast the final votes on what may be the most consequential election of our lives. And this morning, we have a new poll with \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  that offers a snapshot of where they stand today. Political director Rick Klein is here to break down the results. And Rick, the poll confirms what we've been seeing, voters are in a sour mood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP VOTER ISSUES\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, George, voters are just plain frustrated across the border. Seventy-six percent of adults in this poll say the country is headed in the wrong direction. Only 23 percent, less than a quarter of the country say that we're headed on the right track. And, and the issues that are animating voters' frustration, it, it's almost unspeakably vast and broad. Economy, 74 percent of Americans say it's very important to them personally. Sixty-nine percent say the same about inflation. Those are issues in poll that tend to favor Republicans. Voters say they trust Republicans more than Democrats on those issues, other issues including health care abortion rights, a little bit lower on the priority list, but at least now tend to more favor Democrats.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Neither \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  nor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  popular.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN-TRUMP IMPRESSIONS\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and this is such a remarkable moment in this country, George, because a year from the election, it looks very likely that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is gonna be the Republican nominee. He's the frontrunner. And the Democratic nomination is almost assuredly gonna go to President Biden. But people don't like either one of these men. Look at this. Only 33 percent of the country now saying they have a favorable opinion of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That's one-third compared to half of the country that has an unfavorable view.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IF BIDEN ISN'T THE NOMINEE?\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's numbers, even worse, twenty-nine percent favorability compared to 60 percent who say they view him unfavorably right now. And in this poll, George, we asked the "What if" question. What if the nominees aren't Biden and/or Trump? What does that do to your vote? On the question of Biden, 29 percent of Americans saying they're more likely to vote for a Democrat who isn't the current president. As for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , 31 percent say they're more likely to vote Republican if the nominee isn't Trump. And in both of those cases, the number of Independents even higher, about 38 percent in both, in both matchups say they're more likely to vote for that party if the current frontrunner is not the nominee.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we've got some key state elections this week.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ACCESS POST-DOBBS\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and I want to focus on the state of abortion rights in this country, George, because we talk a lot about it and it could be determined by the result in a couple of key states. The green states here are states where abortion remains widely legal and available. The red states are where it's banned. Orange and yellow, somewhere in between. And we've got gubernatorial races in two states that are very heavily Republican, including Mississippi and Kentucky. In Kentucky, the Democratic governor running for reelection against the state's current abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) An interesting race also in Ohio. There's a ballot initiative that would put abortion rights into the state constitution. If that goes down, then you could see an effort to revive the six-week ban in that state on abortion. And very closely raced, watched races is in Virginia, the state legislature on the line. And if Republicans take control of the state House of Delegates and the state Senate, you're going to see Governor Glenn Youngkin push a 15-week ban on abortion. Virginia, right now, the only state in the South where abortion remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020231121ejb500003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VIRGINIA GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN VIRGINIA TO HOLD STATE LEGISLATURE ELECTIONS TUESDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,487 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, JOURNALISTS, GAZA, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , BEN-ANAT, BIDEN, BLINKEN, FINER, AID, SCALISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTTLE DIPLOMACY\par \par \uc2 IPSOS, POLL, VOTERS, BIDEN, TRUMP, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BREAKDOWN\par \par \uc2 YOUNGKIN, VIRGINIA, LEGISLATURE, 2024, ABORTION, 2020, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIRGINIA TO HOLD STATE LEGISLATURE ELECTIONS TUESDAY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rick Klein, thanks very much. Let's bring in the Virginia Governor, Glenn Youngkin. Governor Youngkin, thank you for joining us this morning. That, that 15-week ban is front and center in the campaign right now. Are you worried that it's gonna cost you the - the legislature?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC THIS WEEK: EXCLUSIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION EMERGES AS TOP ISSUE GOING INTO VIRGINIA ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, George, good morning. And there are, there are huge elections in Virginia that on Tuesday, three short days away, and I appreciate you covering them 'cause I think they're the most important elections in America, because these issues that are so important to Virginians are also the ones that are gonna be so important to Americans next year. And on the topic of abortion, this is a tough topic. It's one of the most divisive topics across Virginia and America today. And, and I'll just remind you that just four years ago, in Virginia, they were one, they were one vote away from the Democrats passing a bill that would extend abortion rights all the way up through and including birth paid for by taxpayer money.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 I really feel that this is a moment for us to come together around reasonable limits where we can protect life at 15 weeks where a baby feels pain, with full exceptions in the case of rape and incest, and when the mother's life is at risk, and I think this is a place that Virginians can come together. All the way up through booth, birth is way too extreme. This is a place we can come together and settle on a very difficult topic and I think we can lead here as opposed to fight.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you, but current Virginia law says you can, has 26 weeks, has abortion access up to 26 weeks. Why not just leave that law in place?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, what, what I'm hearing from Virginians, and nearly 70 percent have responded that they would support a bill to protect life at 15 weeks with full exceptions where a baby can feel pain, and I think this is a reasonable place for us to land, and what's on the ballot, I think is a choice between no limits and reasonable limits, and I think this is a reasonable place for us to land. And what's on the ballot, I think, is, is a choice between no limits and reasonable limits. And I think this is one where Virginians come together around reasonableness, and it then allows us to move onto really important topics, George.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 We, we, of course, foresee the impact of runaway inflation scaring Virginians and they're worried about how to make ends meet. Sixty percent of Americans are living paycheck to paycheck. They're spending $700 a month more on buying the basics of groceries and clothing for their children than, than they did just two years ago for the same things. I hear this all across the Commonwealth. They're worried about jobs. They're worried about inflation. They're worried about education. They're worried about public safety, and they're really worried about behavioral health. And we have led on all of these topics.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 We have 230,000 more people working today in Virginia than just 22 months ago. We passed record education budgets with 12 percent raises for teachers just in the last 18 months. We've - we've had a massive transformation of our behavioral health system which, which desperately needs it 'cause it's overwhelmed. And we've really gone to work to increase funding into law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIRGINIA GOP AIMING FOR SWEEP IN LEGISLATIVE ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 These are the topics that I hear about every day as I travel around the Commonwealth from a vast array of Virginians, Democrats, Republicans, Independents, who are discussing these real-life concerns every day around their kitchen table. We've delivered results and that's why I'm excited about what's gonna be on the ballot. I think we can hold our House and flip our Senate. We can keep going 'cause there's so many important topics for us to focus on to drive Virginia to be the best place to live in America, we're seeing a lot of people move here as a result of the great actions I think we've taken.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got a lot of Republicans around the country who want you to run for president, as you know. You just saw the poll we had that showed both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  unpopular. Now, I know you say you're not gonna address this until after the Tuesday election. But I just want to know, have, have you ruled out running for president in 2024, or is that still a possibility?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL VIRGINIA GOVERNOR MAKE LATE ENTRY INTO 2024 GOP RACE?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, well, well, George, I am, I'm a, I'm a homegrown Virginian who, who 40 years ago was washing dishes and taking out trash, and to even have my name tossed around in this is incredibly humbling. I'm excited about the fact that people are, are, are encouraged by what's happening in Virginia where common-sense policies really are working, working to generate job growth, and, and we have a huge tax rebate that has gone out.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 We've had $5 billion of tax relief, people like this. And so, I continue to be very focused on Virginia. I've, I've said over and over again, I've been at the Rockingham County Fair, not the Iowa State Fair. I'm campaigning across Virginia and focused on Virginia, not in New Hampshire, not in South Carolina, not in Nevada. I'm focused on Virginia, and that's where my attention will continue to be.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's about the answer I was expecting. It wasn't exactly a no, but thank you for, for, for addressing the question. Let me just finally ask you the question I asked Steve Scalise. He couldn't answer yes or no on whether the 2020 election was stolen. Can you?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP MAINTAINS BIG PRIMARY LEAD ONE YEAR FROM ELECTION DAY\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, I, I've consistently said that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was legitimately elected president. He's sleeping in the White House. I wish he weren't. In all candor, the chaos that we see around the world and at home is, is his projected weakness. International foreign policy has resulted in multiple spots of chaos from Israel, to Ukraine to China. His, his foreign policy weakness again has resulted in bad adversaries being funded like Iran. And then we see his weakness at our border, which has turned every state into a border state. The free flow of illegal drugs and crime has really invaded everywhere.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 We have five Virginians a day on average that die from fentanyl overdoses. And, of course, the chaos in our economy is not only hurting Virginians and Americans, but it projects weakness around the world yet again. And so, I wish he weren't our president. We can't afford to have him be our president again. And Virginians are telling me every single day that these issues, these issues of jobs and inflation and public safety and great education for their children are so important. That's where we need to be focused.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GLENN YOUNGKIN (REP) (VIRGINIA)\par \par \uc2 And common-sense policies do work. We've demonstrated it in Virginia. And I'm looking forward to having Virginians come to the polls on Tuesday and hopefully hold our House, flip our Senate so we can do even more to drive Virginia forward.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for answering the question. Governor Youngkin, thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Up next, Devin Dwyer takes a closer look at a growing legal effort to block \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the 2024 election, from the 2024 ballot. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Roundtable's coming up. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM MONDAY\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020231121ejb500004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ELECTION DAY 2023 TOP POLITICAL RACES & ABORTION RIGHTS IN OHIO\b0\par\par\uc2 1,368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL DISMISSES HUMANITARIAN PAUSE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PAUSES, GAZA, DRONES, HOSTAGES, BLINKEN, NETANYAHU, JORDAN\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR PLANT, SECURITY, WHISENHUNT, CRENSHAW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MAINE, VICTIMS, SHOOTINGS, CARD, GUN, LAWS, SCHEMENGEES, TEXTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL, FRAUD, TRIAL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 NURSING HOME, DEATHS, PRESSDEE, INSULIN, HENRY, BOWER, PEIRCE\par \par \uc2 PORTLAND, TEACHERS, STRIKE, PAY, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, REPORT, WAGES, WALL STREET, STOCKS, INTEREST, RATES, MORTGAGE\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, COLD, TEMPERATURE, HIGHS\par \par \uc2 SIMS, OHIO STATE, PENN STATE, "COLLEGE GAMEDAY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM PERFORMANCE BY MISSY ELLIOTT\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, ABORTION, GUNS, BIDEN, TRUMP, TUBERVILLE, MILITARY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are gonna start here on this half hour with a closer look at the top political headlines this week. And joining us are ABC White House correspondent MaryAlice Parks and our deputy political director Averi Harper. Good morning to both of you.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's jump right into it. Averi, let's start with you because you're, we're talking about the election 2024. But there is an off-season one happening in 2023, and some big races, including the issue of abortion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ELECTION DAY 2023\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP POLITICAL RACES & ABORTION RIGHTS IN OHIO\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. I am watching a few key races. There's two governor's races, one in Mississippi. The incumbent governor there, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 , he's going up against a Democrat named Brandon Presley. Interestingly enough, he's a relative of Elvis Presley. We think of Mississippi as a deep red state. But that race is actually pretty close. And so, in Kentucky, we're looking Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 . He's going up against a, a Republican Mayor, Daniel Cameron, who has the backing of both Daniel, excuse me, of Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But all eyes are really gonna be on Ohio, where voters there are gonna be casting ballots on the issue of abortion there. Abortion is quite literally on the ballot. And folks are gonna be looking at that race to see what happens in other abortion-related measures that could see happen next year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUN CONTROL & 2024 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECENT MASS SHOOTINGS BRING ISSUE TO FOREFRONT\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we remember how it turned out in Kansas last year. MaryAlice, wanna bring you in. President Biden, he visited Maine Friday to comfort the relatives still grieving, who lost loved ones in the mass shooting, with gun issue, gun control a major issue looking ahead to 2024. But he didn't call for a full-on assault weapons ban.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, the White House has called for that. But you're right, this is absolutely gonna be an issue, especially for voters under 40 who have had to grow up as a generation with school shootings. And we saw the President there in Maine. He did say he that he thought there was, consensus was ultimately possible. It's about common sense, reasonable measures. You know, even though he made these sort of remarks about coming together, there's a lot of gun safety advocates who just think he's not doing enough, that he's not using that bully pulpit. He's not talking about it enough.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, he thinks that Congress is not doing enough. He's asking Congress to literally do anything on this issue. And the White House is spending a lot of time instead, with nothing getting done on Capitol Hill focused, on the states, trying to help states pass their own red flag laws. And it's interesting that we're gonna have this back in front of the Supreme Court again. Just next week, the Supreme Court is gonna hear a case about whether a 30-year-old law that bans people who are under domestic abuse protective orders or restraining orders can have a gun. And, and they're gonna hear next spring a case about whether the government can, in fact, ban those bump stocks. Both those cases could just have huge implications.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 'S BALLOT BATTLES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACING LAWSUITS IN COLORADO AND MINNESOTA OVER 14TH AMENDMENT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, such an important topic there. And Averi, let's go ahead and switch gears here and turn to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , okay? Because he faces those two lawsuits to keep him off the ballot in 2024. We already knew about the one in Colorado, but we also see one now in Minnesota. So, so what does this mean for him looking forward?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, Colorado and Minnesota are actually just the first states to hold hearings on this issue. We know that Michigan is actually gonna start oral arguments later this week. And there's other states that can follow suit. This is all about the 14th Amendment. There's a clause in it, came about after the Civil War, where it says that if you are someone who takes the oath of office to protect the Constitution and then you participate in an insurrection or a rebellion, that you should be barred from holding public office.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, there are legal scholars, including legal, Conservative legal scholars who say that there are grounds based on Trump's actions around January 6th for him to be disqualified. We are gonna have to wait to see what each of the states decides in this. But it's very likely that we're gonna see the Supreme Court asked to weigh in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAPITOL HILL GRIDLOCK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN. TUBERVILLE PRESSURED TO END HOLD UP ON MILITARY NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Something to watch closely. Let, let's talk about gridlock on Capitol Hill. MaryAlice, let's bring you back in. We were talking about the Speaker's race before. And now, for people who maybe aren't paying that close of attention, it's confusing what's happening in the Senate over the military nominations, holdups over something, one Senator involved, something that has very little to do with the military. Where do things stand now?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. One Senator, Tommy Tuberville from Alabama has put his foot down, and he's holding up, we're talking about nearly 400 promotions. And these are military families totally left in limbo. And right now, Republicans are starting to call him out, especially Republicans who are veterans themselves. They say this is reaching a breaking point. It is starting to put our national security at risk. Now, he is making this protest, making this stand, based on the military's policy to let people have time off if they have to travel across state lines to get an abortion.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They changed that rule after the abortion laws changed. And of course, the military was under a lot of pressure to offer a policy like this. You had women that were stationed in states where the laws were changing, so the Senate's probably gonna have to change the rules. But I will say, it was interesting, they did get around his holdup to make one pretty historic, hugely historic, appointment just this last week. The Senate confirmed that a first woman to run the Navy, the top post in the Navy, she'll be the first woman on the Joint Chiefs of Staff.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A big move there.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And they were able to do it once which shows they can also do it again.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're determined.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Ladies, thank you so much. It was great having you here to have this little conversation.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We loved this. This was amazing.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was great, yeah.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231205ejb400034\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW REPORT ON CANCER & YOUNG PEOPLE FINDS 15% INCREASE IN THE RATE OF CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE TO ESCAPE GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, GAZA, STRIKES, REFUGEE, EGYPT, CIVILIANS\par \par \uc2 WRAY, THREATS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , CORNELL, TERRORISTS, ROSEN\par \par \uc2 WINTER, FREEZE, ALERTS, SNOW, OUTAGES\par \par \uc2 TEMPERATURES, FREEZING, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, JOHNSON, FUNDING, ISRAEL, AID, UKRAINE, IRS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TRIAL, TESTIMONY, FRAUD, PENALTY\par \par \uc2 FEDERAL RESERVE, HIKE, ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 REALTORS, LIABLE, \uc2 NAR\uc2 , JURY, SELLERS, AWARD\par \par \uc2 PARK SERVICE, BABY BEAR, CLOSURE, PROTECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILDER DAYS AHEAD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PAPINI, DIVORCE, CHILDREN, COURT, FINANCES, HIGGINS\par \par \uc2 SERAFINI, MURDER, COURT, SPOHR, GIRE, MLB\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, PRICES, TURKEY, CRANBERRIES, SWANSON\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, RANGERS, \uc2 DIAMONDBACKS\uc2 , TITLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CARIBBEAN HEAT\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2 , TERRORISM, HATE CRIME, CORNELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  WARNS OF INCREASED U.S. TERROR THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR: MIDEAST WAR HAS RAISED DANGER LEVEL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, WINTER, FREEZE, TEMPERATURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EARLY WINTER COLD BLAST ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS ACROSS 18 STATES ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 CHRISTOPHER, "GENERAL HOSPITAL", DEATH, ACTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING TYLER CHRISTOPHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "GENERAL HOSPITAL" STAR PASSES AWAY AT AGE 50\par \par \uc2 CANCER, YOUNG PEOPLE, RATE, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT ON CANCER & YOUNG PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINDS 15% INCREASE IN THE RATE OF CANCER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "GMA" cover story. A new report out of Florida found an increase in the past decade in the number of younger people being diagnosed with cancer. That echoes numbers we're seeing nationwide. We're going to speak with Dr. Ashton right after this.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a new medical report out of Florida highlights a 15 percent increase in the rate of cancer in people 20 to 39, that's from 2010 to 2020, with breast cancer being the most common cancer in that age range, as well as thyroid cancer and melanoma. The findings are largely consistent with national trends that show increased diagnoses in people under 50, especially for breast cancer and colon cancer and higher early cancer rates in women than in men. The screening ages for both types of cancer recently lowered. For women like Indiana resident Lauren Dages, who was diagnosed with breast cancer at 31, it can come out of the blue.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I was completely shocked, mainly because there wasn't any type of strong cancer history in my family that I knew of, and I missed a lot of the early warning signs. It wasn't on my radar at all.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for Markeeta Morrow, who got her breast cancer diagnosis at 33 and is now cancer free, she is hoping to get the message out that it can happen to anyone.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It is very important that you are aware of your body, making sure that you are taking care of yourself, eating healthy, exercising and doing self-exams to make sure that if anything changes, or if there's something going on with your body, you can find it, and you be an advocate for yourself.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, let's bring in our chief medical correspondent, Dr. Jen Ashton. Let's start off with this case, specific to Florida.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it was, and this data comes as a result of an initiative that was launched last year by the first lady of Florida, really trying to get a grip on what's going on in terms of cancer in that state. Take a look at some of their findings. Number one most lethal cancer, lung cancer, not a surprise. Female breast cancer is the most common, and it's most diagnosed at an early stage. Skin cancer in the state of Florida is higher than the national average, again most of those diagnosed early stage. And then overall, women found to be at higher risk of early onset cancers. That represents an increase over this 10-year period. So again, most of these were in line with global trends, but applause to them for trying to get a specific look on what's going on there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND THE INCREASE?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does the science say about why this is happening?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, there are a lot of theories, no one firm answer because, again, when you talk about cancer, it's like talking about the weather, different types of cancer, different reasons. You know, this is going up worldwide. We don't totally understand why. Environmental exposure has to be considered, things like air quality, water quality, chemicals in our environment. Our behavior very important, how much alcohol is being consumed, diet, obesity, less active, more sedentary lifestyles. And then the more you screen for something, particularly diagnostic methods being better, the more you're going to pick up, and that's a cause for some of it, as well.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You mention behavior. How do young people reduce the risk?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WAYS TO STAY HEALTHY & HELP PREVENT A CANCER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think, you know, as my mom used to say, who was a nurse, control the controllables, right. You can't control your genetics. You can't control a lot of things. You can control how you eat, how you move, not smoking, getting vaccinated against HPV, human papilloma virus, in terms of following age recommendations for screening and knowing your family history. I think all of those, absolutely important.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jen Ashton, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231201ejb10003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG "MOM-BIES" DANCE IN THE STREETS TO RAISE AWARENESS ABOUT BREAST CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, CONRICUS, BESEISO, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 ABUAYYASH, GEKMAN, WRAY, MILLER, ROSEN, TERROR THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2 : U.S. THREAT AT "WHOLE OTHER LEVEL"\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, AUSTIN, WAR, BLINKEN, PROTESTS, JOHNSON, AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTERS DISRUPT AID HEARING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLOWEEN DEEP FREEZE\par \par \uc2 CARD, SHOOTING, MENTAL HEALTH, WARNING SIGNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARMY WARNING ABOUT GUNMAN\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, HAWAII\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING VIDEO OF MAUI FIRE RESCUES\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH, RESCUE, DUNN, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVERGLADES PLANE CRASH RESCUE\par \par \uc2 FDA, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES, DAVIS, HALLOWEEN, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, on this Halloween, it's not just the children, it's the moms, in costume and in the fight to help other moms.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in Fairfield, Connecticut, it's not the zombies taking over, it's the Mombies. They're all dressing up for Halloween. But it's not just their costumes, it's their dance moves. Michael Jackson's "Thriller." They're doing this to entertain, but also to raise money for breast cancer research, hoping their moves to the Backstreet Boys' work. Dancing on Main Street for a good cause. Fifty moms strong, this started in 2016, growing every year. And right here tonight, in costume...\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE MEMBER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Founder Terry Davis, on the left with fellow mombies Joy Martini (PH) and Eileen Cress (PH).\par \par \uc2 TERRY DAVIS (FOUNDER CREATOR MOMBIES)\par \par \uc2 We're raising money for metastatic breast cancer through the Cancer Couch Foundation.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Many are breast cancer survivors themselves, and Joy is currently battling It.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE MEMBER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm a mombie and I'm also a breast cancer patient. And I couldn't be more grateful and more proud than dancing with these women.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Practicing in the hospital.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE MEMBER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Look at us. Look at us.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her nurses dancing with her. And tonight, just listen to how much money all of these moms have raised.\par \par \uc2 TERRY DAVIS (FOUNDER CREATOR MOMBIES)\par \par \uc2 To date, we've raised over $200,000.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Happy Halloween.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Happy Halloween. Tonight, the moms and their moves on this Halloween, raising more than $200,000 and counting.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mombies.org. Let's help them. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231103ejav0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RACHEL BILSON REVEALS SHE'S HAD MISCARRIAGES ACTRESS OPENS UP ABOUT HER PREGNANCY LOSS\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HUTCHINSON, MANHUNT, LEVESQUE, SHOOTING, SAUSCHUCK, CARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" PERSON OF INTEREST\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS INJURED IN ATTACK; URGENT MANHUNT UNDERWAY FOR SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GUN VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" PERSON OF INTEREST\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, SPEAKERSHIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS ELECT NEW HOUSE SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REP MIKE JOHNSON TAKES THE GAVEL AFTER WEEKS OF CHAOS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CIVIL FRAUD, TRIAL, FINE, GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TAKES THE STAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE FINES FORMER PRESIDENT $10,000 FOR VIOLATING GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , FORD MOTORS, DEAL, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  REACHES TENTATIVE AGREEMENT WITH FORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEAL COMES NEARLY SIX WEEKS AFTER START OF AUTOWORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CARD, SHOOTING, MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 THOMAS, ETHICS, WELTERS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE OTIS, MEXICO, HERSEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MONSTER HURRICANE SLAMS MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAT 5 STORM IS MOST POWERFUL EVER TO HIT COUNTRY'S PACIFIC COAST\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, FTX, TRIAL, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 UBER, WAYMO, GABLE, MACDONALD, DRIVERLESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UBER LAUNCHES DRIVERLESS RIDES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNERING WITH WAYMO TO OFFER AUTONOMOUS CAR OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 WEMBANYAMA, NBA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LEWISTON, BOWLING ALLEY, RESTAURANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 16 KILLED IN MAINE SHOOTING RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR "ARMED AND DANGEROUS" PERSON\par \par \uc2 CREDIT CARDS, INTEREST, FEES, ADVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE COST OF CREDIT CARDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS PAID $130 BILLION IN INTEREST & FEES\par \par \uc2 BILSON, ACTOR, MISCARRIAGE, PREGNANCY, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACHEL BILSON REVEALS SHE'S HAD MISCARRIAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS OPENS UP ABOUT HER PREGNANCY LOSS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're back with our "GMA" cover story. October is Pregnancy and Infant Loss Awareness Month. Rachel Bilson is talking about her own experience. Stephanie Ramos has the details. Good morning, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. The actress, Rachel Bilson, is opening up on her podcast, "Broad Ideas," about a difficult time in her life, sharing that she's suffered miscarriages, and she wants other women to know they are not known.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, actress, Rachel Bilson shedding light on pregnancy loss.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BILSON (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 We would like to acknowledge that we talk about things that could potentially be triggering. It's very open and honest and vulnerable and beautiful.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) During an intimate discussion on the latest episode of her podcast, "Broad Ideas," Bilson sharing that she has suffered from multiple miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BILSON (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 It's one of the biggest things I talk about is pregnancy and having babies, and I've\u160\'00\'A0had miscarriages, so I've had losses, never carried, you know, they were early on.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  estimates that up to 26 percent of pregnancies end in miscarriage, making it one of the most common forms of pregnancy loss.\par \par \uc2 DR. JESSICA SHEPHERD (VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Very important for women to understand that they are not the cause of a miscarriage. Now, what increases a risk for miscarriage is including people who have had miscarriages in the past, so if they've had two or more previous miscarriages. Also, age is a risk factor. Being 35 and older does increase the risk of a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Best known for her role as Summer Roberts in the television series, "The OC," successfully giving birth to her daughter, Briar Rose, back in 2014 and embracing the value of openly talking about the ups and downs that pregnancy can bring.\par \par \uc2 DR. JESSICA SHEPHERD (VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 The most important part is to have discussion and to have support when this happens. Even in those instances, there's always hope, especially when it comes to pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Bilson has spoken publicly about motherhood and co-parenting before, but this is the first time she's opened up about her own pregnancy loss, and, guys, it is so meaningful.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It certainly is. Stephanie, thank you for bringing that to us.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231128ejaq0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MEN WITH BREAST CANCER TWO MEN SHARE THEIR STORIES TO HELP REMOVE THE STIGMA\b0\par\par\uc2 851 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ADDRESSES THE NATION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ISRAEL, UKRAINE, TERRORISTS, DEMOCRACY\par \par \uc2 WARSHIPS, YEMEN, MISSILES, RYDER, \uc2 US NAVY\par \par \uc2 GAZA, HUMANITARIAN, AID, ISRAELI, ROADBLOCKS, DICHTER\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, TROOPS, CASUALTIES, AID\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, SPEAKER, JORDAN, VOTES, REPUBLICANS, DIVISION\par \par \uc2 POWELL, GUILTY, TRUMP, PROSECUTORS, MCAFEE, TIMMONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM MOVING IN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 KING, US ARMY, DMZ, CHARGES, DESERTION, MILLER, GATES\par \par \uc2 SCHOOL BUS, BAKER, HEMILICH, CHOKING, BELL, QUARTER,\par \par \uc2 SPEARS, "WOMAN IN ME", CONSERVATORSHIP, TIMBERLAKE, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 "BILLBOARD", POP SONGS, "I WANNA DANCE WITH SOMEBODY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ADDRESS, PUTIN, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, UKRAINE, WARTIME, AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 HOME, SALES, BUYERS, MORTGAGE, RATES, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 DASH DIET, COGNITIVE, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 IRWIN, ENDOMETRIOSIS, DIAGNOSIS, SYMPTOMS, "CROCODILE HUNTER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 AAP, "TODDLER FORMULA", LABEL, NUTRITION, RECOMMENDATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 JACKMAN, KIDMAN, ROLLING STONES, "HACKNEY DIAMONDS", CHER, "CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA POP NEWS\par \par \uc2 STORM, HURRICANE\par \par \uc2 HAPPY WAX, EL ARROYO, BUTTERSCOTCH BLANKEES, GELPRO, HUSH, PEACHSKINSHEETS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MARGOLIN, GALLANT, "BIG LITTLE FEELINGS", TODDLERS, QUESTIONS, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA: "BIG LITTLE FEELINGS" EXPERTS ANSWER YOUR QUESTIONS\par \par \uc2 BERGAMOTTO, "STAR WARS", HOME, TOYS, ACCESSORIES, PETS\par \par \uc2 "20/20", SMITH, MURDER, MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 UNITED STATES GRAND PRIX\par \par \uc2 PINK, BREAST CANCER, MALES, PIERCE, COVINGTON, STIGMA, GUCALP, SIGNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Together in Pink for Breast Cancer Awareness Month. We most often associate breast cancer with women. But thousands of men in the US receive a diagnosis each year. Whit Johnson here with that story. Hello, Whit.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEN WITH BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO MEN SHARE THEIR STORIES TO HELP REMOVE THE STIGMA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning. Breast cancer in men is rare, but the CDC says about one out of every 100 breast cancers diagnosed in the US is found in a man. And this morning we hear from two men who are not only fighting breast cancer, but the stigma that often comes with it.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Eric Pierce started experiencing aching bones and trouble sleeping in 2021, his primary doctor sent him to an oncologist.\par \par \uc2 ERIC PIERCE (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 They found it in my bones. So then, we went and got a mammogram and they found out that I had breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Diagnosed as stage IV, the now 66-year-old and grandfather of three, said his world turned upside down.\par \par \uc2 ERIC PIERCE (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It's like, what? I'm a male, how do I have breast cancer?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Brent Covington, the first sign of trouble was feeling a lump under his nipple that progressively got larger.\par \par \uc2 BRENT COVINGTON (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I showed it to my daughter, who's in the healthcare business. And she said, "That's a sign of breast cancer."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The now 52-year-old diagnosed as stage II.\par \par \uc2 BRENT COVINGTON (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Initially, it was, it was disbelief, not knowing that men could get breast cancer. So, it was, it was disbelief. It was shock.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This year, about 2,800 men will be diagnosed with some type of breast cancer, with about 530 of them dying from the disease. Some men, like Eric, say the diagnosis also comes with a stigma.\par \par \uc2 ERIC PIERCE (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It's like, what? Breast cancer? I'm a man. So, that's kind of embarrassing.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the warning signs for men are often no different than they are for women.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT ARE THE WARNING SIGNS COMPARED TO WOMEN?\par \par \uc2 DR AYCA GUCALP (BREAST MED ONCOLOGY/MSK/MALE BC SPECIALIST)\par \par \uc2 You could feel a lump in the chest wall. You can see changes in and around the nipple. But, a lot of the time, the, the mass can be small and the mass can also be painless. And so, there may be a period of time where the individual doesn't even notice that there's something going on.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As for Brent, he has this critical message for other men.\par \par \uc2 BRENT COVINGTON (MALE BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 If you feel a lump, get it checked out because you never know. But if you have been diagnosed with breast cancer as a male, have a positive strong attitude. That carried me and helped me endure the ups and downs. That got me through it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Brent is now going on four years of being cancer free. And Eric's doctors have put him on a hormone pill that's been showing promising results. Both men are eager to help raise awareness. And just like experts at the CDC, they are urging men who notice lumps or other changes to go see a doctor. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Important warning. Okay, Whit, thanks very much. Coming up country star Riley Green performs live.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231114ejak0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS TOGETHER IN PINK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, JORDAN, SCALISE, MCHENRY, GRAVES, MCCAUL\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, STABBING, CARSON, KENNY, HOLDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR BROOKLYN STABBING SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL ATTACK ON SOCIAL JUSTICE ACTIVIST CAUGHT ON CAMERA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2  , TRIAL, FRAUD, JAMES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STUDENT LOAN, IMMIGRATION, BORDER WALL\par \par \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE HEALTH CARE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKS END WITHOUT DEAL AFTER 75,000 WORKERS WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 SENA, ROSS, ABDUCTION, BROWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ACCUSATIONS ABOUT 9-YEAR-OLD'S SUSPECTED KIDNAPPER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEIGHBOR CLAIMS MAN HAD SUSPICIOUS ENCOUNTER WITH HER GRANDSON\par \par \uc2 GYMNASTICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN GIRLS!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. GYMNASTICS TEAM WINS RECORD SEVENTH STRAIGHT WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MUSIC VIDEO, "COCO LOCO"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, MURDER PLOT, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 FRANKE, HILDEBRANDT, CHILD ABUSE, KESTER\par \par \uc2 WONG, GYMNASTICS\par \par \uc2 MLB\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MALUMA LIVE, 8:30\par \par \uc2 SPEAKER, OUSTED, MCCARTHY, HOUSE, CONGRESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS ON CAPITOL HILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR NEW HOUSE SPEAKER RAMPS UP\par \par \uc2 WALL, IMMIGRATION, BIDEN, LAWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW MOVE TO BUILD BORDER WALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE WAIVES LAWS TO CLEAR WAY\par \par \uc2 UBER, PACKAGE, RETURN, RIDE SHARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UBER INTRODUCES PACKAGE RETURN FEATURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVERS WILL DROP OFF UNWANTED ITEMS\par \par \uc2 GREEN, ACTOR, ILLNESS, ADVOCACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "90210" STAR BRIAN AUSTIN GREEN'S HEALTH BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW HE ADVOCATED FOR HIMSELF TO GET BETTER\par \par \uc2 DISCOUNTS, SHOPPING, HOLIDAY, FORECAST, PANDYA, VAN ULLEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HIGH DISCOUNTS PROJECTED THIS SEASON\par \par \uc2 CLOONEY, "ONE NIGHT ONLY", FAT BEAR WEEK\par \par \uc2 BRAS, DEODERANT, CASES, JEWELRY, KNITWEAR, BANDS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now in honor of Breast Cancer Awareness Month, Tory Johnson is here with "Deals & Steals" Together in Pink. And we are having a pink party in studio with these beautiful breast cancer survivors. And all the deals that you see are from small companies dedicated to helping thrivers and their families. Scan the QR code to go right to them. It's wonderful, got to look you in the eye, wonderful to have you all here and doing well. Okay, what makes this so unique right here?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANAONO BRAS\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, we are starting with AnaOno, and this is all about supporting the chest an breast at any stage of breast cancer. So as they say, one breast, two breast, no breast, new breast, they've got a bra specifically for you because it's really all about sort of changing outcomes, unexpected outcomes with surgeries and treatments. And everything is designed with incredible soft fabric. You guys, feel this fabric, how unbelievably soft it is. It's designed with no wires, openings in the fronts, just really thoughtful designs both in bras, as well as loungewear, underwear, all slashed in half, starts at $7.50. Hopefully, you find something that works for you. Good brand.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FREEDOM DEODORANT\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next up, let's talk about Freedom deodorant.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, Freedom. So, I got to start off by saying Amber approved. I was texting her yesterday. She originally told me about this line, and so I texted her. I said, "Are you still using it?" She goes, "Of course I do."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh yes.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, coq au vin is hers. What's interesting is when this line was first started, the founder didn't know that just a little while later, she was going to be diagnosed with breast cancer. And she said, "I was then on a mission to create a product that mattered on what I put on my body." And so, it's not just, we think a lot about what we put in our bodies, but what we put on our bodies matters, too. So, this is 100 percent aluminum-free deodorant.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, it smells really good.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I said, "How do you know that it really, really works?" And she said, "We tested it on women in Arizona summer heat."\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That will do it.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Everybody came back odorless. That'll do it. Also another favorite of Amber's is their eucalyptus shower spray, turns the shower into a spa. This is a fabulous one. It works, and it starts at $6.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It has really helped her through her journey. And did we see them on survivors?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STG SCREEN CASES\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, we've got Denise, (PH) Shirley, (PH) Lori, (PH) all modeling our Save the Girls. So, this was started by a woman whose sister-in-law was diagnosed with breast cancer, and she would carry her bra, her phone in her bra, and she said, "Do you know what? I know you want your phone close. I don't like it that close." So, she created all of these bags that have just touchscreens so you can keep your phone really close without losing your phone, but you don't have to put it on your body.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's great.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's so smart.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They also have come up with these amazing cross-body straps.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The straps are so cute.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on, work it, work it girl. There you go.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Work it girl, so you can keep it really close. Save the Girls also has donated $50,000 to all kinds of breast cancer research organizations. Everything here slashed up to 60 percent, $10 to $30. These are fabulous. These are fabulous.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSTIC CUFF JEWELRY\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We love our jewels.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do love our Rustic Cuff. When the creator, Jill Donovan, was diagnosed with breast cancer, to every single treatment, she would bring these bracelets that said these words, hope, faith and love, one of the stacks that we've got here. And she would give them to all of the patients, who were also going through treatment. And she saw just, like, how simple, a simple piece of jewelry can connect people, can make people feel better. And we've got also options where you can customize with your own names like that. They support, also, they've donated almost $100,000 to Oklahoma Project Woman, that gives all kinds of support services for women with limited financial resources...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that, beautiful.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...from, everything from mammograms to treatment options. So, this company does a lot in their community. This is a great product. These start at $14.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOVE YOUR MELONS KNITWEAR\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this next product has really helped pediatric cancer.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, so breast cancer gets so much attention, but it's a great reminder now that there are other cancers that also need funding and support for patients. Love your Melon, these are fabulous and such a good name. They've donated more than 250,000 of these. We've got Nadine, (PH) Shirley (PH) and Denise who are donning theirs.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're so cute.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're so soft, so comfortable. These are fabulous. They've also given almost $10 million to pediatric cancer research and patient support. I mean, that is beautiful. We can help them up that today. These start at $17.50.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love your Melon.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love your Melon, baby.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RELIEF BANDS\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And finally, Relief Band. So, these were started to be used in a hospital setting to help with motion sickness. To help with the nausea that comes from chemotherapy, pregnancy, any other sort of, you know, place that nausea comes from. It's just a simple little pulse point that sends, it's really designed, it's completely natural and absolutely, it's fast acting and long acting, send these little pulse...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of great reviews on this.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such good reviews, sends these pulse points that tell your brain, "No more nausea." These are 50 percent off and free shipping.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Free shipping. All right. We've partnered with all of these companies on all these amazing deals. Head to goodmorningamerica.com to find all of these offers. Thank you, Tory.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, thank you, thank you, and thank you to our models.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our supermodels.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. They look beautiful. Stick around. We've got Maluma, Maluma is going to perform live. And we have a special surprise, as well, so come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSIS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231018eja500068\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER & FINANCIAL TOXICITY GOING INTO DEBT WHILE TRYING TO PAY FOR CARE\b0\par\par\uc2 976 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, GAETZ, GOOD, BURCHETT, ROY\par \par \uc2 SENA, ROSS, HOCHUL, ALLEN, KIDNAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING GIRL FOUND ALIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 9-YEAR-OLD RESCUED, SUSPECT IN CUSTODY AFTER URGENT 48-HOUR SEARCH\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FRAUD, TRIAL, JAMES, COHEN\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, CUELLAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONGRESSMAN CARJACKED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS REP CUELLAR ROBBED AT GUNPOINT NEAR DC RESIDENCE\par \par \uc2 PASSPORT, PROCESSING TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSPORT WAIT TIMES REDUCED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST DECREASE SINCE POST-PANDEMIC TRAVEL BOOM\par \par \uc2 IPHONE 15, APPLE, OVERHEATING, PARMAR\par \par \uc2 KIMMEL, WGA, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , STRIKE, SCHWARZENEGGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVE, "MY COUSIN VINNY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY SELECTION BEGINS IN SAM BANKMAN-FRIED TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTX\uc2  FOUNDER ACCUSED IN MULTI-BILLION DOLLAR FRAUD AFTER CRYPTO COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, SAFETY, COPE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, HOUSE, SPEAKER, OUSTER, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAETZ MOVES TO OUST MCCARTHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE SPEAKER FACING BACKLASH OVER DEAL\par \par \uc2 MISSING, GIRL, FOUND, SENA, ROSS\par \par \uc2 JAMES, BRONNY, BASKETBALL, CARDIAC ARREST, SURGERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEBRON JAMES GIVES UPDATE ON BRONNY'S HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REVEALS SON HAD SURGERY AFTER CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 JEFFRIES, \uc2 ABERCROMBIE & FITCH\uc2 , CEO, SEXUAL ABUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER \uc2 ABERCROMBIE & FITCH\uc2  CEO UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIKE JEFFRIES FACING ALLEGATIONS OF SEXUAL ABUSE\par \par \uc2 ELBA, THERAPY, ACTOR, SELF-CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDRIS ELBA ON HIS "UNHEALTHY HABITS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR OPENS UP ABOUT MENTAL HEALTH TOLL\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, FINANCIAL TOXICITY, RUSSO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & FINANCIAL TOXICITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOING INTO DEBT WHILE TRYING TO PAY FOR CARE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to our series, "Together in Pink," for Breast Cancer Awareness Month. This morning, something that few ever really hear about, the often overwhelming cost of care. Erielle Reshef is here with one woman's story. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you guys. As you know, breast cancer diagnosis can come with so many different variables, and one that's often overlooked is the financial burden. More than half of breast cancer patients say they have gone into debt to pay for their treatment, and experts call this financial toxicity, and they say it can take a devastating toll. One single mom is sharing her story.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Cindy Russo was diagnosed with breast cancer earlier this year, she knew the treatment would be grueling, but she never anticipated the disease would take a toll financially.\par \par \uc2 CINDY RUSSO (BREAST CANCER PATIENT)\par \par \uc2 It is so unbelievably overwhelming. It is beyond the biggest challenge ever.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's called financial toxicity, the harmful effect of cancer treatments on a person's quality of life.\par \par \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN (AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 We very much believe that people should be battling cancer, not bill collectors. Financial toxicity is associated with poor outcome for cancer patient.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOING INTO DEBT WHILE TRYING TO PAY FOR CARE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Recent studies show cancer survivors reporting financial hardship related to their care had a higher risk of death, and survivors are 2.7 times more likely to file for bankruptcy compared to those without cancer. The impact of financial toxicity, unmistakable.\par \par \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN (AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Can be in the form of skipping drug doses to save money or not filling prescriptions, borrowing money, refinancing the home or reducing spending on what we would consider to be essentials, like food and clothing.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since starting chemo in March, Russo filed for short-term disability, which pays just half of her salary. To help with her mounting medical debt, the mom of two has called her mortgage company, electric company and others to figure out a payment plan, the Long Island native struggling like so many single moms.\par \par \uc2 CINDY RUSSO (BREAST CANCER PATIENT)\par \par \uc2 It's all I think about every day. It makes it difficult to be motivated to do anything.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The average cost of cancer care and medications is more than $42,000 in the first year, and that doesn't include out-of-pocket costs. Early detection can help save your life and your money.\par \par \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN (AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 At the beginning of a cancer journey or a cancer treatment strategy, having that open conversation with your provider team and with financial assistance...\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And experts say there are things you can do to help. Ask your doctor if you can switch to generic drugs, work out a payment plan with your hospital and lean on your friends and family for help.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Cindy still has multiple radiation treatments ahead of her. In the meantime, her sister set up a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  page to help ease some of these costs. Of course, we're wishing her well, guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO FIND FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE AFTER A BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I know you touched on this at the end of your piece, but are there other things that people can do if they need some financial support during this time?\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There definitely are, and it's important to know the resources out there. You can reach out to the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 , which provides free transportation to and from cancer-related appointments. Also, your local \uc2 Department of Social Services\uc2  may be able to provide food, housing and general assistance. And some drug companies will provide help with insurance repayments or discounted medicine. So, it's important to know the resources and to be your own advocate.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, and ask. There are programs out there, but you have to ask. All right, thank you very much. This is often overlooked.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it is, and it's such a burden.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja30003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BUDDIES THROUGH BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSED YOUNG & NOW HELPING OTHERS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,400 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 SHAH, REASOR, BREAST CANCER, TREATMENT, REASOR, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BENTLEY, SHEPHERD, FERTILITY, BREAST CANCER, PORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE WOMAN'S JOURNEY FROM DIAGNOSIS TO FINDING A SURROGATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 KORSON, KNOLLMAN, FAYANJU, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 MORROW, DAGES, BREAST CANCER, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So moving to be out here in the sea of pink with these survivors and thrivers. Welcome back to "GMA" as we stand here together in pink. All these women here reminding us of an important message that no one has to take this difficult journey alone. Two thrivers who met in the thick of treatment are now spreading awareness.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUDDIES THROUGH BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIAGNOSED YOUNG & NOW HELPING OTHERS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When it came to breast cancer, Markeeta Morrow didn't think it was in the cards.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I've always been a person who was very into making sure that I took care of my body.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lauren Dages had an early scare that, she says, doctors initially told her was nothing, then came the diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It was shocking. I dropped to the floor and my world completely changed.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While routine breast cancer screening can start when a person is 40 years old, Lauren and Markeeta were both in their 30s when they learned they had triple-negative breast cancer, finding each other during treatment and supporting each other ever since.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It's really nice not to have to overly explain to someone or try to get them to really understand just how horrible it is.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 And you can even smile and kind of laugh about it.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Even though it's very traumatic.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One recent study found peer support significantly improved positive emotions among breast cancer patients. And in a time when more young women are being diagnosed with breast cancer, the two friends are calling out the need for women to be their own advocates.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It can happen to anyone at any age at any time.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 If you feel anything that's off at all, advocate for yourself. Don't worry about being annoying. Don't be worried about being too loud in the office.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While some research shows that there's no benefit to self-breast exams and it's no longer recommended for women to do it routinely, both women found their cancers this way.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 If you feel something that is abnormal, something that wasn't there last time, say something. Because No one is going to be a bigger advocate for you than yourself.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN HELPING EACH OTHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW FAST FRIENDS ARE PROMOTING SELF-EXAMS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Jessica Shepherd from VeryWell Health is back along with Lauren and Markeeta. So, you all are both self-exam advocates. Talk to us about Commit to One pledge, what it means and why it's so important to you.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 The Commit to One is basically choosing one day a month that you can remember when you're not on your menstrual cycle that you can do every single month and you can check for any changes in your breasts.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why is it so important to you, Markeeta?\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I think it's really important to me because that is how I found my lump. I was doing those self-exams. I've always done them. And I think that if we express to everyone, no matter your age, you should be in tune with your body, making sure you do what you need to do, and it can save lives.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, doctor, there's actually disagreement about this in the medical community. Why is that?\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah, you know, the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  really has no longer recommended the breast self-exam. But what we see clinically, even in my practice and my colleagues, is that we want women to be aware of their breast tissue. And having that, you can see in these stories, clearly, that's how they diagnosed. So, we still advocate for women to do this on a monthly basis.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, give us a demonstration, ladies, what we need to do.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN DAGES (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, normally you would do this with your shirt off. And you just go ahead and just raise your hand up above is your head. You take three fingers, place them on your breast. You're going to go ahead with those fingers and do a circular motion all around.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER ALL OF THE BREAST, ARMPIT & UP TO COLLARBONE\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 And what we're trying to do is look for anything that feels different, feels odd. You're going all the way around the breast. You're going to make sure you get into that underarm because you do have breast tissue there. We're going all the way up to the breast bone. Get up in there. Do the other breast, and then you're all done.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Get up in there.\par \par \uc2 MARKEETA MORROW (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Get up in there.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, some life-saving advice and tips. Thank you, ladies. And what other precautions should women be aware of?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST SELF-EXAMS DO NOT REPLACES THE NEED FOR A MAMMOGRAM\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, you know, we really have good research on lifestyle and preventative. So, that means healthy diet, really what you can get through your food. Limiting alcohol. These have been shown in research to decrease your risk of breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER PRECAUTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO DO A BREAST SELF-EXAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAKING THE 'COMMIT TO ONE' PLEDGE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we've been talking about diet. What kinds of diet, should other than limiting your alcohol?\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, cruciferous vegetables, this is going to be like your broccoli and your cauliflower. Those really have good antioxidants and have been shown to have the things that you need that are going to help you boost your immune system and fight off those cancers.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, doctor, Lauren, Markeeta, we thank you so much for being here, continuing to thrive. And we are just so grateful to have you present with us today. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a warm and touching feeling here this morning. We want to thank everyone who stood with us together in pink this morning. A great way to kick off Breast Cancer Awareness Month.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANNE HATHAWAY & MARISA TOMEI!\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Truly. And tomorrow on "GMA," we have Anne Hathaway and Marissa Tomei joining us live.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have a great day, everybody.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY ONE WOMAN'S JOURNEY FROM DIAGNOSIS TO FINDING A SURROGATE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,256 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 SHAH, REASOR, BREAST CANCER, TREATMENT, REASOR, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BENTLEY, SHEPHERD, FERTILITY, BREAST CANCER, PORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE WOMAN'S JOURNEY FROM DIAGNOSIS TO FINDING A SURROGATE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we are going to turn now to fertility. It is a second battle many women with breast cancer have to fight. Certain treatments can lead to infertility, giving some women yet another difficult situation and a set of new decisions to make when they're diagnosed.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At 38 years old, Sarrah Strimel Bentley, a former Broadway performer turned yoga instructor, was in a new relationship and a picture-perfect image of health until she found a lump the size of a walnut in her left breast.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I got the biopsy results back that, indeed, I had stage 2 invasive ductal carcinoma. And it was like time stopped. And, of course, I was terrified.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the same breath, her doctor recommending an appointment with a fertility specialist.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I had no idea that when you have breast cancer that, you know, your fertility would be affected. It was my dream for as long as I can remember to be a mother.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Studies have found that about half of young women with breast cancer say they'd like to have a child after completing the treatment. But some treatments, including certain types of chemotherapy, can affect fertility.\par \par \uc2 DR ELISA R PORT (CHIEF BREAST CANCER SURGERY MOUNT SINAI HEALTH SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 We try to be extremely proactive when a young woman is diagnosed with breast cancer about preserving her fertility.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sarrah undergoing two rounds of IVF with her then boyfriend James, resulting in a single embryo.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I feel so lucky that we have this chance to be able to make embryos before I go into treatment.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sarrah holding on to hope and her positive spirit through rigorous rounds of surgery, chemo and radiation. Through it all, her future baby remaining in sight, despite the challenges.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 My oncologist had told me that, due to my age, my type of cancer and the fact that we only had one shot, she said you need to have a surrogate if you want to bring this baby to life.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sarrah and her now husband James documenting their surrogacy journey every step of the way.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Surrogacy is not a straight line and it is not easy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Bentleys finally matching with Whitney, their surrogate.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Leading up to finding out that the embryo transfer was successful was the longest two weeks of my life. That call was either going to be the best day of my life or the hardest news.\par \par \uc2 HEALTH CARE PROVIDER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) it's positive.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I lost my mind.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God. Oh, my goodness.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 And the most incredible moment of my life.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the couple are eagerly awaiting the arrival of their baby boy.\par \par \uc2 HUSBAND (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It's becoming real, and we can't wait to meet the little guy.\par \par \uc2 SARRAH STRIMEL BENTLEY (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Just know that if you get diagnosed with breast cancer and you are a young woman and you think your life is over, it is not. I'm so, so thankful to be here.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are so excited for them and thankful for people like Whitney, who do this ultimate job of being a surrogate. And we want to bring in the other people doing the ultimate work. Dr. Jessica Shepherd, who is an OBGYN and chief medical officer for VeryWell Health. You're on the other side of it, saving lives.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT FERTILITY OPTIONS ARE AVAILABLE TO WOMEN WITH THE DISEASE?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's so nice to see you. This can be such a blow. I have friends who have gone through this, not only do you find out you have breast cancer, but you find out you may not be able to conceive.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How do you deal with that?\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I think the emotional toll that you see with these patients when they get this diagnosis is so overwhelming. And breast cancer is the number one cancer that's diagnosed in women. And not only that, 10% of these cancers are going to be diagnosed in women 45 years and less. So, we have a clear problem when we see fertility options and breast cancer diagnosis, what that really means. And so, it really requires a conversation, but knowing that there are options is clearly what you saw here in Sarrah's instance.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are the most important things to consider in that conversation about fertility, questions you should be asking your doctor?\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (CHIEF MEDICAL OFFICER VERYWELL HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Now, when you're considering what do I do? Where do I go from here when its concerning fertility is to know that there are options. And early diagnosis is key. But not on early diagnosis, it's what am I going to do and what are my options? So, when we think of surrogacy, when we think of cryopreservation, which is egg freezing or embryo, that really can tell a story for someone who doesn't know where they're going to go with this. So, emotionally, we want to capture that, but also knowing that there's options. And we have so much research that shows that these are great options.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Shepherd, thank you for doing what you do and advising us today. And coming up, we have a big surprise for one young thriver and her medical team. You do not want to miss this. It is a very uplifting story. Stay with us. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 YOUNG THRIVER SHARES HER BREAST CANCER JOURNEY HOW A CLINICAL TRIAL HELPED GET HER CANCER FREE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,486 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 SHAH, REASOR, BREAST CANCER, TREATMENT, REASOR, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BENTLEY, SHEPHERD, FERTILITY, BREAST CANCER, PORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE WOMAN'S JOURNEY FROM DIAGNOSIS TO FINDING A SURROGATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 KORSON, KNOLLMAN, FAYANJU, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are back now "GMA" with the story of a young thriver, Kate Korson, who was diagnosed with an incredibly rare breast cancer just before her 34th birthday. And now, she's here with her doctors to tell her story and to raise awareness about how important it is to get screened early. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUNG THRIVER SHARES HER BREAST CANCER JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW A CLINICAL TRIAL HELPED GET HER CANCER FREE\par \par \uc2 HAYLEY KNOLLMAN MD (ONCOLOGIST PENN MEDICINE)\par \par \uc2 Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kate Korson was just a week shy of her 34th birthday when she received her breast cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Breast cancer was never on my radar. It was overwhelming and gut wrenching.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the time, she was living on a small ranch in Colorado, caring for her rescued horses and a flock of birds when her world turned upside down., stage 3 triple-negative breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 How am I 34 with stage 3 breast cancer? Why? Why is this happening to me?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRIPLE-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Triple-negative breast cancer accounts for about 10% to 15% of all breast cancers. It's a very aggressive tumor type. Kate decided the only place for her treatment was \uc2 Penn Medicine\uc2  , where her mother was treated for colon cancer 17 years ago. From day one, Kate told her doctors she wanted to participate in a clinical trial just like her mom did.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 The benefits of a clinical trial are that you get the most cutting-edge treatment. You get the treatment that will be available in a few years. And for me, that was overwhelmingly successful.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a matter of months, Kate's tumor shrunk substantially and her doctors were able to stop treatment early and send her to surgery.\par \par \uc2 HAYLEY KNOLLMAN MD (ONCOLOGIST PENN MEDICINE)\par \par \uc2 Her participation in the clinical trial ended up meaning that she got half the length of time of the chemotherapy and had significantly less toxicity, meaning side effects.\par \par \uc2 LOLA FAYANJU MD (CHIEF OF BREAST CANCER SURGERY \uc2 PENN MEDICINE\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 We were really excited to see that basically all the tumor was gone.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her treatment journey is far from over. But thanks to the clinical trial, she's currently cancer-free. And Kate says, she couldn't have done it without the wonderful team at Penn.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 From day one, I have felt fully supported. I feel like I'm the luckiest girl, which I know is crazy coming from a woman with breast cancer, but it's really how I feel.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are so lucky to have Kate here in studio with us to share her message. Her doctors also here, Dr. Hayley Knollman also here and Dr. Lola Fayanju. Welcome. You are both from Penn Medicine Abramson Cancer Center. Welcome to "GMA."\par \par \uc2 LOLA FAYANJU (CHIEF OF BREAST CANCER SURGERY \uc2 PENN MEDICINE\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 Thanks.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Thanks for having us.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Kate, well, how does it feel for you, after all you've been through, you are here on "Good Morning America" and potentially saving someone else's life by doing this?\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It's - surreal. It's absolutely surreal. And this whole time that my priority is has been helping other people however I can. So, I, it feels like yesterday was the first day that I met you guys. Yeah. It's incredible.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Dr. Fayanju, I know that you talked about how you can never be too young to get breast cancer. What do you think, though, when you have a healthy 34-year-old woman like Kate who comes in and gets a diagnosis?\par \par \uc2 LOLA FAYANJU (CHIEF OF BREAST CANCER SURGERY \uc2 PENN MEDICINE\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 Well, the first thing I think is, was there an opportunity to potentially diagnose or prevent this type of thing from happening? And so, we really encourage young women to know early on with the help of their primary care physician or gynecologist, am I at high risk for breast cancer? Should I be getting genetic testing? Should I be getting screening at an earlier age? So, knowing your family history is incredibly important.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in my own family, Dr. Knollman, my mom was diagnosed with breast cancer. She is now cancer-free many years later. But it was such a blow when we heard this. And I wonder what you recommend patients do to stay mentally optimistic through what is going to be a big, big obstacle in their lives.\par \par \uc2 HAYLEY KNOLLMAN MD (ONCOLOGIST PENN MEDICINE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, absolutely. You know, when I first meet patients and we talk about treatment, whether that's chemotherapy or pills, you know, endocrine therapy, we talk about how we're going to be very aggressive with physical health and mental health, emotional health is also so important. So, I always talk with women about things like, you know, feeding their, their soul. Things like yoga, counseling, joining support groups. There are so many great resources for breast cancer community and especially women, young women with breast cancer as well.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, and people like Kate, you're out there making a difference in women's lives. And I know how important that is to women who are going through this. We've had it in our own staff here at "GMA," the women who have gone through it and found a purpose. But, Kate, we know your purpose and we want to celebrate that today because this incredible team, the \uc2 UPenn\uc2  team, was all part of your journey. And as a result, the physical and emotional toll that this has taken and the hard work you've all put in, Raising Cane Chicken Fingers heard about this story. They heard about your story. They were inspired to be part of this great work and the research, and they are donating $100,000 of net proceeds to UPenn Abramson Cancer Center in your name. Was any of you expecting (inaudible) this morning?\par \par \uc2 LOLA FAYANJU (CHIEF OF BREAST CANCER SURGERY \uc2 PENN MEDICINE\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does this mean for you, Kate?\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Amazing. I, like, all I wanted out of this was to help my, help other women, but also help my amazing doctors get the grants and do, keep doing the research. That is so important. And this is, this is amazing. Thank you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And thank you and thank all of you for the work that you do every single day to save lives and educate women.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, thank you so much. As Robin says, make your mess your message.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's exactly what you're doing right here. Thank you so much, Kate. And we've got a lot more ahead on gma. Hey, Ginger, what's coming up?\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Gio. So, I know that Kate's out there. She has no idea that the surprises are just getting started because, in here, we've got all of her friends and family. She has no idea that we were going to celebrate her even more. Such an incredible survivor. So much more to come right here on "Good Morning America." Please stick around.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we are back now on "GMA." And just moments ago, we surprised Kate, a breast cancer survivor, with incredible news that Raising Cane's Chicken Fingers is donating $100,000 of today's proceeds in her honor to the Penn Medicine's Abramson Cancer Center, where she went through her own cancer journey.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Kate, we know that you thought you were just here to talk about your story, and you are. But we have a lot of surprises ahead here because you shared how important your support system has been through all of this. And we spoke with some of them. They've carried you through, they helped pull you through the toughest moments. Take a look at this because they are showing up for you again.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, no.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Kate. It has been almost 15 years that we've known each other, and I could not be more grateful for that.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We just want to tell you how proud we are of you. You've been so strong and amazing through this whole cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA KELLOGG (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 We're so proud of how well you've handled everything that life has thrown at you this year. You really manage it all with grace and courage.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Kate's case is a great example of what, clinical research can provide for people. And I think that Kate can do anything that she wants. She has a really long life ahead of her.\par \par \uc2 MARJORIE ELWELL (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 I want to make sure you know how loved you are. That is why I'm here today alongside so many other people who love you.\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA KELLOGG (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 We just want to tell you we love you so much.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I love you so much, and couldn't live without you.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We love you.\par \par \uc2 RELATIVES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We love you.\par \par \uc2 CHILD (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Aunt Kate, I love you and I'm so proud of you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, so sweet.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep. So beautiful. Why don't you take a look over there. Come on. Come on over.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on over.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) These are all the people who love you, who've been there for you each step of the way and they wanted to be here this morning with you live on "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got your mom, your dad, your parents, your uncles, your aunts, your cousins, all of them right here for you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I hope everyone at home has a tissue out because this is such a moment to see.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, so beautiful. Marjorie, where's Marjorie?\par \par \uc2 MARJORIE ELWELL (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 That's me.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on over. Come on over. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Marjorie, there you are. Marjorie, okay. Marjorie, you traveled all the way from Colorado just to be here this morning. What does it mean for you? We can see what it means to you.\par \par \uc2 MARJORIE ELWELL (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 It means, it means so much to me. Kate is the type of friend that if I were in pain or dealing with a painful situation, she would take that pain and hold that for me, which is so incredibly special.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Adriana, you were part of this journey. Talk about pain. You were there helping Kate through all of that pain. What is it like to see her now thriving?\par \par \uc2 ADRIANA KELLOGG (BEST FRIEND OF KATE)\par \par \uc2 It's unbelievable. From day one, it was really clear that there was no other option besides beating this, and that she was going to be a force of nature. And it's been absolutely amazing to watch and be by her side.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Kate, we know, well, there you are. You're with (inaudible) over there, one of our senior producers. That's who we heard your story from. And we heard you really wanted to go to happy hour with your medical team, okay. So, your friends over at \uc2 Penn Medicine\uc2  , they wanted to surprise you with a special gift this morning here. You and members of your care team, they are getting tickets in a box suite to Wednesday night's \uc2 Phillies\uc2  game. That's all she wanted. You are such a \uc2 Phillies\uc2  fan.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Huge.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mom and dad, how do you feeling to see all of this? You've made such great sacrifices and had to go through something no parent wants to see and now here you are.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We're just thankful that, you know, she's in such good health and thankful for her doctors (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You give people hugs. We'll hold this for you.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I know, right? I will hold my people.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is nothing better than seeing all of you here together. The impact that you have all had on Kate's life, the impact she's had on all of your lives, we are so thankful and grateful for all of you. Kate, we hope you have a great time at the \uc2 Phillies\uc2  game.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Best wishes to all of you.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 08:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S CIVIL FRAUD TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT TO APPEAR IN COURT\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump set to appear in a New York court this morning. The former president's civil fraud trial about to get underway, bringing him face-to-face with the judge who found he inflated his net worth by as much as $2.2 billion. Trump now at risk of losing part of his business and some of his buildings.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAYLOR SWIFT MEETS THE \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "TRAYLOR" MANIA\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  defeats the \uc2 New York Jets\uc2  , all eyes on Taylor Swift cheering on Travis Kelce. How the superstar is helping attract new fans. Our reporter was at the game.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BRICK-AND-MORTAR STORES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Toys 'R' Us\uc2  comeback, opening again after filing for bankruptcy in 2017. When will the kid's favorite make its return?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCARE UP SOME SAVINGS!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Countdown to Halloween, just over four weeks away. This morning ways to save on everything to make the holiday less scary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER AWARENESS MONTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we're together in pink. Kicking off breast cancer awareness month, shining a light on the rise in young women being diagnosed with the latest on detection and treatment, from self-exams to how artificial intelligence is improving screening and breast cancer and fertility. One former Broadway performer sharing her journey. Plus, we're meeting one thriver and celebrating her medical team.\par \par \uc2 KATE KORSON (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I want to help people in the future who are faced with this. I want things to be easier for them.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The big surprise for them ahead as we say...\par \par \uc2 CANCER SURVIVORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we do say good morning, America. You may have noticed, we are all in pink this morning. And that's because October is breast cancer awareness month. And this morning, we are kicking off our coverage.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's right, Gio. And we are joined by thrivers from the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  . They've shown up today because breast cancer touches so many. One in eight women will be diagnosed at some point. And this morning, we are hearing people's stories and sharing the latest advancements in detection and treatment.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Some heartwarming stories coming up there.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we turn now to \uc2 Toys 'R' Us\uc2  , making a comeback, announcing that it will open up 24 flagship stores in the US as early as next year.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It also plans to open smaller shops on cruise ships and at airports. The first of those will open at stores at the Dallas/Fort Worth Airport next month. \uc2 Toys 'R' Us\uc2  once had nearly 1,700 stores worldwide, but it filed for bankruptcy protection in 2017. And it's remained closed and closed a lot of its stores here last year. And I know a lot of families, LD, you, you're going to be there with your son someday.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking forward to see Geoffrey. Remember, Geoffrey the giraffe?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:11, SCARE UP HALLOWEEN SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up on our "GMA Morning Menu," how to save this Halloween, from costumes to decorations, ways to avoid a frightening bill this year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:14, TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Can't wait for that. Also, this morning, together in pink. We are kicking off Breast Cancer Awareness Month with the latest advances and guidelines in detection and treatment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:20, BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, breast cancer and fertility. The options for young women diagnosed with the disease. One former Broadway performer shares her story. And we have a big surprise for one young thriver. And she's sharing her empowering message. It is all coming up right here on "GMA." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLING BREAST CANCER LATEST BREAKTHROUGHS IN CANCER RESEARCH & TREATMENTS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 SHAH, REASOR, BREAST CANCER, TREATMENT, REASOR, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to standing together in pink in our Times Square studio. Some of the ABC News family, from our props teams to stage managers, control room staff, we want everyone to know that we, too, stand with you. It's a journey some of us had to deal with personally, of course, impacting lives of family and friends. So, we know breast cancer isn't something that anyone should have to fight alone. And for Breast Cancer Awareness Month, we are supporting battling, surviving, thriving against the disease. We are kicking off latest our coverage with some of the latest treatments and trends in breast cancer advancements. And joining us now, Dr. Ami Shah and Dr. Erica Stringer-Reasor. Welcome.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST BREAKTHROUGHS IN CANCER RESEARCH & TREATMENTS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, ladies. Such an important conversation that we're having this morning and throughout the month. Dr. Shah, let's start with you. We know that the median age for diagnosis for breast cancer is 62. But in recent years, of course, we've started to see younger women being diagnosed. Tell us about those numbers.\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (HEMATOLOGY & ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, unfortunately, that's true. Breast cancer is, you know, the most common cancer in those under the age of 50. For all women, the rate of breast cancer is about 1 in 8 in their lifetime.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (HEMATOLOGY & ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 But it's that group under the age of 50 where we are seeing an increase in the rate. From 2010 to 2019 we saw about a 7%-increase in the rate of breast cancer. And we're not entirely sure why this is happening. For each individual in the majority of cases, we can't identify a specific risk factor or exposure. About 5% to 10% of breast cancers are linked to somebody's genetics. But the majority are not, which is why it's so important for all of us to have that awareness of breast cancer and to know when to seek additional care.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Dr. Stringer-Reasor, of course, minority women are disproportionately diagnosed as well. You have been named ambassador of hope. What have you seen in this role?\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA STRINGER-REASOR (DIR BREAST CANCER PROGRAM UNIV OF ALABAMA)\par \par \uc2 So, fortunately, we do notice that women younger than aged 45 and minority women continue to be under-represented in clinical trials and have worse outcomes. We also know that black women and white women have similar incidence of breast cancer. But if you are a black woman, you are at least 40% higher chance of dying of your disease. And this goes for all subtypes of breast cancer. We think that there are multiple contributing factors to this, namely the biologic factors, which include black women are diagnosed at later stages, higher (inaudible) of their tumor, and three times more likely to be diagnosed with triple-negative breast cancer, which is an aggressive form of breast cancer with limited treatment options.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK WOMEN & BREAST CANCER DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA STRINGER-REASOR (DIR BREAST CANCER PROGRAM UNIV OF ALABAMA)\par \par \uc2 Secondly, we also noticed that there is some bias-driven factors, which include systemic factors, as well as provider beliefs, and patients lived experiences of discrimination that leads to medical mistrust. Thirdly, there are some socioeconomic factors that play a huge role in this risk factor, including poverty. So, those that live in poverty have a higher risk of having lower access to care. Actually, lower access to good care. So, receive suboptimal treatments and late treatment actually, delays in their treatment.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA STRINGER-REASOR (DIR BREAST CANCER PROGRAM UNIV OF ALABAMA)\par \par \uc2 And lastly, if you are a minority woman, you are less likely to receive a survivorship plan in which we know improves lifestyle changes and encourages regular follow-up.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's just so important to understand why that's happening. And, Dr. Shah, we all know screening. It is so important for early detection. So, what are the current screening guidelines right now?\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (HEMATOLOGY & ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so actually one of the big organizations that make our recommendations for guidelines recommended lowering the age that screenings start from 50 to 40 because of that rising rate of breast cancer in young women.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER SCREENING RECOMMENDATIONS\par \par \uc2 DR AMI SHAH (HEMATOLOGY & ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST LURIE CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 They recommend a mammogram every other year starting at the age of 40, continuing until the age of 75. There are other organizations that recommend annual or every other year mammograms. And some people, based on their own risk factor, whether it's their genetics, a family history, dense breast tissue, a prior abnormal biopsy that may benefit from a supplemental screening with an MRI or an ultrasound. And so, it's important to talk to your doctor about what's the right screening strategy for you. So, we can catch as many breast cancers as possible in the earliest, most curable stages.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And on that note, Dr. Stringer-Reasor, what are the new breakdowns, you know, the new breakthroughs that we're looking at when we're talking about this treatment?\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA STRINGER-REASOR (DIR BREAST CANCER PROGRAM UNIV OF ALABAMA)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm. So, we recommend patients living a healthy lifestyle. We also encourage those that, when they have a healthy lifestyle, to exercise regularly and to also have a balanced diet, to lower their risk factors of breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIFESTYLE CHANGES TO LOWER BREAST CANCER RISK\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA STRINGER-REASOR (DIR BREAST CANCER PROGRAM UNIV OF ALABAMA)\par \par \uc2 We also encourage patients that have a higher risk factor of breast cancer to really know their bodies. And so, know what's normal and abnormal is in the body as well as establish care with a primary care physician. If you have a primary care physician and you have concern with your body, then you can be evaluated quickly. And then, lastly, 90% of all breast cancers are not hereditary link or don't have a family history. So, if you palpate an abnormal mass, if you feel or notice skin changes, like redness or dimpling, if you notice fluid, feel discharge from the nipple or asymmetry in the chest wall, we encourage you to seek medical care.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such important information. Dr. Shah and Dr. Stringer-Reasor, thanks so much for being here today and being there for your patients all the time. We really appreciate it. And those advances in AI will truly hopefully save a lot of lives as well.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, FRAUD, TRUMP, JAMES, MINTZ, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS, SHUTDOWN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM, FEINSTEIN, BUTLER, SENATE, ACTIVIST, LGBTQ\par \par \uc2 MISSING, SEARCH, SENA, HOCHUL, CAMPING, MAZZONE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 KAISER PERMANENTE\uc2  , NEGOTIATE\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, PAYMENTS, PAUSE, RESUME, INTEREST\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, FOOTBALL, CARDIAC ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL TIME OCTOBER HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, KELCE, CHIEFS, JETS, FANS, TROMBETTA, DEFRANCESCO\par \par \uc2 NASCAR, TRUCK, PLANK, SMITH, STRUCK, PIT STOP\par \par \uc2 BEYONC\u201\'00\'C9, "RENAISSANCE", CONCERT, FILM, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 BILES, GYMNASTICS, VAULT, CHAMPIONSHIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IN COURT; MCCARTHY UNDER FIRE; THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT; TOYS 'R' US COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 FUNDING, SHUTDOWN, MCCARTHY, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2  , SWIFT, KELCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "TRAYLOR" EFFECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAN FRENZY AS TAYLOR SWIFT MANIA & NFL FANDOM COLLIDE\par \par \uc2 TOYS 'R' US\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOYS 'R' US MAKING A COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAILER SAYS IT WILL OPEN UP TO 24 FLAGSHIP STORES NATIONWIDE NEXT YEAR\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 SHAH, REASOR, BREAST CANCER, TREATMENT, REASOR, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 BENTLEY, SHEPHERD, FERTILITY, BREAST CANCER, PORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & FERTILITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE WOMAN'S JOURNEY FROM DIAGNOSIS TO FINDING A SURROGATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 KORSON, KNOLLMAN, FAYANJU, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we head now outside to Ginger, who's sending a big hug from outside.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, I am. Oh, my goodness, Rebecca, the tears are flowing, as we've got celebration of Kate, every other thriver, all the health care workers and the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  with us here out in Times Square on a beautiful morning, albeit you can smell the smoke a little. But we thought we should talk about fall colors because it is such a gorgeous morning. You think, oh, well, where are they happening?\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Look at Salt Lake County in Utah, and they're in Huntsville, Utah. And some of those northern locations are seeing at or close to peak if you see some of the red on the map there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FALL FOLIAGE\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the far northern fringes. But even some colors showing up as far as the Ozarks. So, we'll be keeping an eye on that this next month.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But for now, let's go ahead and get a check a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a crowd out here this morning. Coming up, two young women who bonded during their breast cancer treatment and are now helping others show us the right way to do a self-exam. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231017eja20000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON "THICKER THAN WATER"\b0\par\par\uc2 4,453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: 20/20\par \uc2 TWNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, "THICKER THAN WATER", COLEMAN, EATING DISORDER, "SCANDAL"\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Being in water, moving through water, has always felt more natural to me than walking on land. When I am in the water, I am at peace. I feel most at home with myself, in my body. In the water, I could be free.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Kerry Washington, water has always been her safe space, an oasis from the stresses of her life. A life that, to all appearances, is filled with satisfaction and success. Leading lady of TV and film, married to a former NFL star, mom of three. But she now reveals a life also filled with soul-crushing secrets, shared for the first time in her new book, "Thicker Than Water."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Thicker Than Water." You are an author.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I am.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You ready to dive in? You ready to dive in?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah? What is it about water? That's the underlying theme.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It is. I love water. I think I must be part mermaid. I love the distance that water allows me from the world. I can still see it and hear it, but it's like in a slightly other dimension.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry's world has been, in many ways, a mystery. To outsiders, she's famously tight lipped about her personal life. But with her book, she brings to light a lifelong identity crisis, a search for self so intense that she dreaded the simple question, "How are you?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Often when I hear "How are you," I am overcome with blind rage. "How are you? Who are you? What do you want? How do you feel?" These questions have been unimaginably difficult for me to answer. More often than not, inside, I am undone.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I made sure when I saw you that I didn't say, "How are you," because I read...\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I know.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...you go into a blind rage.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 So, for a long time, when somebody would ask me how I am, it would set me into this panic mode, because I didn't know how to answer the question, and be true to myself, and also give them what they want to hear. And so, it would really be a stressful moment.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry's story begins in the Bronx, New York, as a much doted upon, only child of Earl Washington, a real estate agent, and Valerie, a college professor.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I want to talk about the young Kerry. Describe what a young Kerry was like.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 She was this ball of contradiction, right? Because she was filled with love, and energy, and art. But she was also afraid, and struggling, and searching.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said you lived among a family of performers, and the magic trick was in pretending.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Mmm.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What did you mean by that?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 We kind of had this appearance of being this kind of very successful, intelligent, elegant, family where everything was perfect, and that was not the case.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry writes about her parents' bitter arguments, overheard at night while she pretended to sleep. Their yelling and crying, fighting about money, about her father's drinking, about disappointments in the marriage.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 As they slammed doors and shouted obscenities at each other, I could feel the tension between them, vibrating through the wall. I developed panic attacks at night.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said that you felt that you had to be the one to fix it.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I thought, "Well, maybe if I'm a little smarter, or more successful, or prettier, or happier, or thinner, eventually" I thought, like, you know, "Maybe if I could be better in some way, it'll make things better for this family."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I talk in the book about feeling like there was something I didn't know, and feeling like there was some distance between my parents and I. And I want to be really clear, my parents are extraordinarily loving people. But in that love, there was this veil, there was this distance.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there were so many things that you, you reached out to, to try and help you.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 CREW MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Acting was one.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Acting was a lifeline.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I was so, yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In some ways?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I was so lucky to find acting. It became an escape, right, from any of the fear and the anxiety, I could jump into a character and not have to think about any of that. I could just be this other person.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That love of acting was developed, in part, at the Spence School, an elite private school in New York City.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're at the Spence School.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 We are.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is your old stomping ground.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 This is.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doesn't look like my high school.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It's...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, a little bit different from my school.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 This is, this is an extraordinary place.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At 13-years-old, Kerry was on stage as a fairy, with none other than another famous Spence alum, Gwyneth Paltrow. By high school, Kerry had her own starring roles, like Ophelia in "Hamlet."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I came offstage as Ophelia. And I looked at my mom, and she was crying. And that was, like, the moment that I understood the magic of acting. 'Cause I thought, "This woman who carried me for nine months, like, she knows exactly who I am. If even for half a second I could convince her that I was another person in another time, like, this is some powerful stuff."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Part of Kerry's acting training was as a "Peer actor educator" with the Star Theater, a group focused on promoting teen health, including teaching young people about safer sex, in the midst of the AIDS epidemic.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I have something I want to show you, because...\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Okay.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...there are a lot of people that they feel that they know when the first time you were on ABC. They thought it was with your show, "Scandal." That was not the first time you were on ABC.\par \par \uc2 PETER JENNINGS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This broadcast is about AIDS. I'd like to you to meet a young woman now whose name is Kerry.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh, dear.\par \par \uc2 PETER JENNINGS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She is going to play at this morning, another young woman named Jessie.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Eric is this guy I'm going with. He's so perfect. Curly brown hair.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER") (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 Green eyes, tall, built, 22.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 When he comes to pick me up at school, every girl's head turns.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 This is crazy.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I lost it with Eric.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness gracious.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 A friend of mine told me that she heard Eric had AIDS or HIV or something. How am I supposed to deal with this? I'm only 14. I mean, who can I talk to about this? I mean, what does all this mean? It's so confusing. I just I gotta get outta here.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my gosh. When the producers were planning the special, I did the monologue in this conference room at ABC, and Peter said, "You're gonna do that live on television." And I was like, "Okay."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it led to you getting a nickname, correct?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It did.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was it?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 In this period of time, because I was a peer educator, I always had condoms in my backpack, and I was "Condom Kerry."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Condom Kerry."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But while Kerry was educating her peers, she was concealing her own struggles.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said, "I was using alcohol, and sometimes food, and sometimes weed, and sometimes sex to alter my brain chemistry and allow me a dangerously destructive escape."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Uh-huh. I had to keep maintain this fa\u231\'00\'E7ade of, like, the overachieving, high school educator performing on prime time television. Like, my grades were good. I was the lead in the play. And then, after hours, I was acting out.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Next, Kerry reveals the depth of her pain.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you actually contemplated suicide?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And a surprise reunion you won't want to miss.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KERRY WASHINGTON "THICKER THAN WATER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A CONVERSATION WITH ROBIN ROBERTS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What is it like to walk these halls again?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It's wild. I feel old.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By the end of high school, Kerry Washington had secured a talent agent, was actively auditioning, and had developed a full-blown love of acting.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It was such a transformative time. This drawing room has all the class pictures.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I think I know you are over here I am told.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Am I?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's see.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 So, I would be '94. So, here. Aw, that's me.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh wow. Center stage even then. Center stage even then.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I wonder if we could find Gwyneth. What year was Gwyneth?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't know. We can't find Gwyneth, but I can find Mr. Coleman.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I love your hair.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We surprised Kerry with her beloved high school theater director, James Coleman.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So James, tell us about a little Kerry Washington.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Oh dear. Oh dear.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back in the day.\par \par \uc2 JAMES COLEMAN (FMR THEATRE DIRECTOR THE SPENCE SCHOOL)\par \par \uc2 You know, she was different. She had depth. She had resonance.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 He always challenged us to go deeper. I learned how to be a thinking artist here. I mean, I research, people make fun of me, I research my characters so intensely all the time. But that's because that was welcomed here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It started here. It started here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 George Washington University\uc2  was next for Kerry, where she'd earned a scholarship in acting. But her most challenging performance was hiding an eating disorder she describes as raging out of control.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 By the time I got to college, my relationship with food and my body had become a toxic cycle of self-abuse that utilized the tools of starvation, binge eating, body obsession, and compulsive exercise.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 The first time that I actually got on my knees and prayed to some power greater than myself to say, like, "I can't do this, I need some help," was with my eating disorder.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I would, when seeking to stuff my feelings, stuff my face, secretly binge eating for days at a time, often to the point of physical pain, sometimes to the point of passing out.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I could feel how the abuse was, was a way to really hurt myself, as if I didn't want to be here. Like, it scared me that I that I could, that I could want to not be here because I was in so much pain.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 That hopelessness and agony led to thoughts of suicide.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you actually contemplated suicide?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's how dark?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. It's so funny, 'cause, as I say that to you, I'm like, "And that'll be the headline." But the behavior was tiny little acts of trying to destroy myself.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry sought professional counseling, which she continued for years as part of a long journey of healing. And then, in 2001, she scored her big break when she co-starred in the teen blockbuster "Save The Last Dance."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SAVE THE LAST DANCE"\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 You need to watch where you sit, girl. Don't ever let me catch you at that table again. And it's Chenille.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The growing success brought a lack of privacy. In her book, Kerry reveals for the first time how she was recognized while having an abortion.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 The nurse looked down at me, smiled, and very gently said, "Do you know who you look like?" She said that I looked like Kerry Washington, that girl from the movies.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) People are gonna hear you talk about things and read about things that they've never known, like your abortion.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I thought, "We stay in our circles of shame because we don't talk about it." And so, I challenged myself to try to write about my experience having an abortion. To sort of let go of the shame about having an abortion and say, like, "This is what this happens. A lot of women do this. This is a form of healthcare. This is okay."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 And then, to also share that, I experienced a lack of privacy, and that and how hard that is. And I'm saying we have to value our right to privacy, and to free agency, and to choice.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She also reveals a childhood trauma, a boy who she says repeatedly touched her while she was in bed, asleep during sleepovers, without her awareness. When she finally discovered the violation, at age 10, she made a decision to protect him and not tell any parents.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes, he was the perpetrator, but I felt that he was not built to withstand the pain of facing the consequences of his actions, so I would hide my pain and cover the truth to keep him and everyone else comfortable.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How was that, reliving that trauma? That could not have been easy.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I mean, these were, like, the hardest writing days, right? But, I felt like the point is to remind myself and each other that we're not alone, and that little girl made the choice to not tell anyone. I have a great deal of compassion for where the choice came from and even a little admiration for that little girl.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 But I also adore her and feel so sad that she carried the burden of that on her own for so long. And so, I wanted to make a choice to tell a truth that she couldn't.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry kept silent about her private struggles as her stardom grew. Her reputation on the rise with roles in Oscar-winning films, "Ray."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "RAY"\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 You walk out that door, and I'm going to do something I should have done a long time ago, Ray, I'm going to take my boys, and I'm going to leave.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE LAST KING OF SCOTLAND"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "The Last King of Scotland."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 You must do it. You can do it from here.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The child must go to the hospital.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Please.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Django Unchained." And then, of course, "Scandal."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SCANDAL"\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Consider it handled, Madame President.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But there was another secret, one she never suspected waiting in the wings, a family secret that would rock her world.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It never occurred to me that that was gonna be what they were gonna tell me.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KERRY WASHINGTON "THICKER THAN WATER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A CONVERSATION WITH ROBIN ROBERTS\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 And you are?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Olivia Pope.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With "Scandal," ABC's hit primetime show, Kerry Washington became a household name.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you ready to break out the popcorn and pour the wine? Because you know, I remember visiting the set there at "Scandal."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes, it was so fun to have you there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is your office.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 This is my office. This is Olivia Pope's office, and this is the couch where you see me interrogate lots of new clients.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It is my name on that door, and I do not give up.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The program, which premiered in 2012.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 It's handled.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Earned rave reviews, fierce fandom, and broke barriers for casting the first black woman to lead a network TV drama in nearly four decades.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fans call themselves gladiators.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'll put my hand up. I was a gladiator. Do you have a message for gladiators today?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I'm very proud of the show, but we weren't a juggernaut of a success because of the show. It was because of the viewers, because people tuned in, because people were ready for her. And I have the life that I have today because of them.\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Ms. Pope, the President would like a moment with you.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Please tell the President I'm busy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her role as DC fixer "Olivia Pope," inspired and influenced by real life crisis manager Judy Smith.\par \par \uc2 JUDY SMITH (LIFE CRISIS MANAGER)\par \par \uc2 She instinctively understood what I did and what it was about. She just wanted to know everything, and it was a level of trust because she wanted to get it right, and she knocked it out of the park.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry creating lasting bonds with her castmates she considered "Found family," including co-star and friend Bellamy Young.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We talked to Bellamy, and she wanted to share this message with you.\par \par \uc2 BELLAMY YOUNG (ACTRESS "SCANDAL")\par \par \uc2 Ker, I just want to tell you that I love you so much. And watching you apply your loving, anthropological, dramaturgical, investigative prowess, the same one you use for all the characters that I watch you play so beautifully on screen, to see you apply that to yourself, was such a radical act of compassion. I celebrate the kindness that led you to share all with us.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 That's so rude, that's so rude that she did that and didn't tell me. Yeah, it's friends for life. Friends for life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After seven seasons, living in Olivia Pope's world.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Ladies and gentleman, our final episode. Episode 782.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kerry writes, she was then left to search for her own truth.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 So, I thought, "Do I even know who that authentic self is? If I am no longer Olivia Pope, who am I?"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It was during that time, Kerry learned new information from her parents that she says changed everything.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 2018, wrapping up "Scandal," you get a text that turned your world around. What was that text?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 The text was, "We need to talk to you." We're not a family that has, like, regular, serious talk, family-meeting kinda stuff. So, already, my Spidey sense was like, "Mmm, something's up." I texted my husband, and I said, "I need to go meet up with my parents." When I got there, my dad was sitting, and my mom kind of smiled at me. And I went and sat down with them.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 But they told me that my dad is not my biological father, that I was born from a sperm donor. And I was shocked. It was amazing, because I was at once shocked, like, completely shocked. At the same time, it felt like some sort of weird confirmation. It was like they took glasses off of me, and cleaned them, and handed them back to me.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Things just started to make sense in a different way. I was weirdly excited. Like, I wasn't mad. I, at first, at first, I wasn't mad. I didn't feel betrayed. I wasn't sad. I just was like, "I'm so curious." 'Cause I think I knew, in that moment, that, like, in some way, this was my call to adventure.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But it took them all that time.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I know, if my dad could have taken it to his grave, he would have. I also know that's because, for him, there was nothing to tell, that my dad made the decision early on that I was his, and he was mine, and nothing will ever shake that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have you attempted to locate your biological father?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I have. I am in the process of attempting...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And still in the process?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 ...to find my donor, yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How does your father feel about that?\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I think he's open, and curious, and, you know, maybe not thrilled but, accepting and supportive.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That bombshell revealed after Kerry agreed to participate in the PBS show, "Finding Your Roots" with Henry Louis "Skip" Gates Jr.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "FINDING YOUR ROOTS"\par \par \uc2 HENRY LOUIS "SKIP" GATES JR. ("FINDING YOUR ROOTS")\par \par \uc2 Welcome to "Finding Your Roots."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It turned out a DNA test would be required, alarming her parents.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 I said, "Skip, I don't know. My parents are so resistant now, and I don't know why. Like, can you get on the phone with them and maybe talk them through this?" And so, he got on the phone with them. And my mom was like, "Hey, what if, hypothetically, what if there was a situation where a sperm donor was involved? Like, do you think that that would show up in a DNA test?" And he said, "Absolutely."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 And she was like, "And would we have to talk about that on the show?" And he said, "Yes." And they said, "I don't think we're gonna do the show." And he was like, "Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait. You don't have to do the show. But you should consider telling her."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 And that was the greatest gift that he gave my family. Because when my dad told me, I realized that every time that I have said, "I love you," to my dad, that there has been this little part of his brain, conscious or unconscious, that has had to have said, "She loves me because she thinks I am her father."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Right? So, I'm saying, "I love him," from his perspective, on the condition of a lie. The moment that he told me, I realized that I had the opportunity to, for the first time, love my father unconditionally, that he got to hear me say, "I love you, even though I know."\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 That healing that my family got to do, to say, "Yes, I now know that you've lied to me for four decades, and I love you." That is an extraordinary gift for our family.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're not supposed to make me cry. I'm supposed to try and make you cry. That was beautiful, Kerry.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Next.\par \par \uc2 KERRY WASHINGTON ("THICKER THAN WATER")\par \par \uc2 Look at you guys all matchy, matchy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We go home with Kerry, for an emotional conversation with her parents.\par \par \uc2 VALERIE WASHINGTON (KERRY'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 What's the difference between it's a secret or it's none of your business?\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document TWNT000020230929ej9o00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE BREAK DOWN\b0\par\par\uc2 896 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, POLL, ECONOMY, VOTERS, IMMIGRATION, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ABC/WP POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARNING SIGNS\par \par \uc2 2024, BIDEN, POLLS, VOTERS, FINANCE, ECONOMY, AGE, ABORTION, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BREAK DOWN\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's dig into this more with our political director Rick Klein here with The Breakdown to help make sense of this poll, and dive into the numbers. And Rick, the economy is clearly at the top of voters' minds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE: YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PERSONAL FINANCIAL STANDING\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Martha, these numbers are simply staggering for the sitting president. Forty-four percent of people in this poll say they are not as well off as they were at the start of the Biden administration two and a half years ago. Those are the worst numbers that we've seen in our ABC News/"Washington Post" polling. It's a question we've been asking going back to the Reagan administration.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And when, when you dive into the big questions around the economy, we know President Biden has been out there trying to make the case, unemployment is low. He's been talking about how inflation has been easing, but people aren't buying it. You covered some of the reasons why, gas prices, food prices, grocery prices and the like. Right now on the big picture in the economy, 74 percent of the country, that's about three-quarters of Americans who say the economy is either not so good or downright poor.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and it's not just the state of the nation or the policies that are giving people pause on President Biden. It seems to be the man himself.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOO OLD FOR SECOND TERM?\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Martha, let's talk about age because we know for sure that the country certainly is. President Biden would be 82 years old on Inauguration Day, 2025. That's how old he is. He's not getting any younger, and of course, perceptions around his ability to perform in the job are not getting any better. Right now, three-quarters of Americans, 74 percent say that he is too old to effectively serve in a second term. That compares to about 50 percent who say the same around \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And it's not just Republicans or Independents who are skeptical over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2024 NOMINEE PREFERENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT ABORTION RULING\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is a question we asked, should Biden be at the top of the ticket? Sixty-two percent of Democrats and Democrat-leaning Independents said they think that someone else should be the presidential nominee, although the party is deeply split on who that someone else should be. Now, if you're looking for a potential good sign, a positive sign for Democrats in this poll, opposition to the Supreme Court's decision on Roe versus Wade, overturning abortion rights at the national level remains very, very strong, 64 percent opposition. Of course, it was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's three - Supreme Court justices who authored that opinion and made it possible.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and of course, abortion played a big role in last year's midterms, but most of these numbers paint a bleak picture for President Biden's reelection chances, Rick.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP-BIDEN 2024\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and, Martha, maybe the most startling number in our poll is this, the, the hypothetical matchup, a rematch of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  versus \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Our poll with, with the "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " pegging this at 51 percent to, for, for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That is a nine-point edge. Now, that's only a couple of points difference from our last poll in May, but it is significantly different than most recent polls. It is an outlier compared to other polls we've seen recently.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our partners at FiveThirtyEight put together an analysis for us. They find an average of recent polls having this more in the one to two-point range with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  typically having the edge. Whether you believe that or not, look, there's a good chance that there's people just trying to send a message in the polling right now, given the other frustration we've seen. We know in this poll there's some, some quirks, some oddities around the number of Black voters and Hispanic voters, the younger voters who seem to be supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and get this, 'cause it's pretty hard to believe, but we asked people whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should be constitutionally disqualified from running for office and among people who said yes, one in five, about eighteen percent said they'd vote for Trump anyway. So that might just be sending a message that's more anti-Biden than it is pro-Trump. But regardless, the, the weaknesses that we are seeing for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his approval rating across the board are very real. They're alarming to Democrats even if no one thinks this is ultimately gonna be a nine-point race.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rick Klein, thanks for that.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230929ej9o00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-ON-ONE ONE-ON-ONE WITH GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE\b0\par\par\uc2 962 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG, JOHNSON, STELLY, SANDERS, BIDEN, HIGHWAY\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, ABORTION, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  remains the runner-up in FiveThirtyEight's latest polling average of Republican presidential hopefuls. But he's also been losing ground. So, how does he stop the Trump train from pulling away? ABC's Linsey Davis sat down with DeSantis in Texas today for an exclusive interview.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A number of your opponents have been really critical of your six-week abortion ban in Florida. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who's in Iowa today, has called it a terrible mistake. He says that you've gone too far. Can you trust that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  still has the views with regard to abortion that reflect the base of the GOP party?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, when you provide pro-life protections that says when a baby has a heartbeat, that there's protections, that is not something that pro-lifers think is terrible. They think that that is a noble and just thing to do. Of course, there've been many other states that have also done that. He claimed to be pro-life. He spoke at the March for Life and was waxing eloquently about how everybody counts. For him to then attack people like Iowa, South Carolina, Florida, all these other states, I thought was a big mistake. But, look, I mean, I think he's taking positions that I think are different from what he took in 2015 when he first came onto the scene. And I do think he's a different candidate today than he was back then. And I think the one back then was probably closer to where Republican voters want to be than the latest iteration.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said he claimed to be pro-life. Do you think he is pro-life?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, you tell me. I think that if you have something where you have a baby that has a detectable heartbeat, if you're pro-life, you would want to say that there should be protections there. And if he's saying that that's a terrible thing, I know most pro-life voters would think that he's wrong.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're governor of Florida, you're a congressman from Florida, you're arguably the state's biggest cheerleader. Why is it that you suppose that the Florida Republican congressional delegates, the majority at any rate, support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who's been indicted four times, over you?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I have almost the uniform support of the Florida legislature, who's in Florida. So, those are the guys I work with. We've been able to deliver huge wins for Florida. We've really set the standard for the nation. Right now, our economy's ranked number one in the nation, according to CNBC. Education, number one, according to \uc2 US News & World Report\uc2 . We have businesses flocking to the state. People are flocking to the state. And I think those folks who we work with daily basis, almost 90-some-percent of them come to the conclusion that what I've been able to do, the leadership, if I could do that in Washington, it'd be good for the country.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You know, I've never really been a guy that got along in DC. I don't like the way it operates. I think we need a house-cleaning up there. There will not be business as usual when I become president. There will be changes the way things are done business. And, you know, that doesn't necessarily sit well with everybody. And that's true with people in both parties up there.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But how does that work, as president, if you say, you know, I've never really gotten along with the people in DC?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, because there's a culture that's developed, I think, that has put the interests of DC ahead of the interests of the American people. And you look, right now, five of the eight wealthiest counties the United States are suburbs of Washington, DC. How does that happen? It isn't like they have abundant resources there or they're producing much of anything. They're producing a lot of debt, a lot of spending. People that are politically connected to the government are doing better. Meanwhile, Americans outside that area are basically bearing the costs with all these highest prices that the spending and inspiration have fueled.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 So, what I represent is really saying, you know what, it's time that we, the people, come and that we're leading the charge up in DC. It's not just about the people in DC. It's about what you can do for folks throughout the country. And there's a lot of people that are struggling. If we can't have in this country people that are working hard, trying to raise kids, if they can't afford to buy a home or buy a car or even afford groceries, if America doesn't work for those people, we are not going to be successful as a country.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Linsey.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE HUNGER GAMES"\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Up next, the return to Panem. "The Hunger Games" are back on the big screen and we're got the action-packed sneak peek.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230922ej9k00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DESANTIS ON ABORTION BATTLE ONE-ON-ONE WITH GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE\b0\par\par\uc2 770 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GARLAND, HEARING, VAN DREW, JORDAN, SCHIFF\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, MASON, FORESTAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MURDER SUSPECT ACCIDENTALLY FREED\par \par \uc2 FENTANYL, O'SULLIVAN, TARANTINO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING NEW FENTANYL BUST\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION CRISIS, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SURGE AT THE BORDER\par \par \uc2 SALAZAR, LINDSEY, CLINKUNBROOMER, GASCON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHARGES IN DEPUTY'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION, DESANTIS, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESANTIS ON ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back here in the US, and to the race for the White House. On the Republican side, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a 40-point lead over his Republican challengers, including Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Trump now attacking DeSantis over Florida's six-week abortion ban, calling it a terrible mistake. ABC's Linsey Davis sitting down with Governor DeSantis today, asking him about the issue of abortion and about Trump's criticism.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE WITH GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A number of your opponents have been critical of your six-week abortion ban in Florida. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who's in Iowa today, has called it a terrible mistake, he says that you've gone too far. Can you trust that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  still has the views with regard to abortion that reflect the base of the GOP party?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (R-FL) (2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, when you provide pro-life protections that says when a baby has a heartbeat, that there's protections, that is not something that pro-lifers think is terrible. They think that is a noble and just thing to do. Of course, there have been many other states that have also done that. He claimed to be pro-life, he spoke at the March for Life and was waxing eloquently about how everybody counts. For him to then attack people like Iowa, South Carolina, Florida, all these other states, I thought was a big mistake. But, look, I mean, I think he's, he's taking positions that I think are different from what he took in 2015 when he first came onto the scene. And I do think he's a different candidate today than he was back then. And I think the one back then was probably closer to where Republican voters want to be than the latest iteration.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey Davis with Governor DeSantis. Linsey joins us tonight from Odessa, Texas, where Governor DeSantis was speaking today. And Linsey, Governor DeSantis standing behind Florida's six-week abortion ban. The question, of course, on the national level, would he support this move for the whole country?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, David, you're right. He does stand behind it, but he is not committed to pursuing it on a federal level. We should note that while Trump is critical of DeSantis' policies, he's often quick to take credit for appointing those three conservative Supreme Court justices who ultimately helped to overturn Roe versus Wade, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Linsey Davis live in Texas tonight with the interview. Linsey, thank you. And I should point out that Linsey will have much more of her exclusive interview with Governor DeSantis on ABC News Live Prime. That starts at 7:00 PM. Eastern on ABC News Live and on Hulu. Thank you, Linsey.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UAW STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GM SENDS 2,000 WORKIES HOME\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the newest ripple effect from the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike against America's big three automakers.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) GM now shutting down a plant in Kansas City, Kansas, tonight, laying off nearly all of its 2,000 workers. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  warns a new wave of strikes could be announced Friday unless they receive a substantial offer from the automakers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL RESERVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTEREST RATES LEFT UNCHANGED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One more note on the economy tonight. The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  leaving interest rates where they are, deciding not to raise rates this month, but saying one more hike could come this year.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Fed also projecting stronger growth now and lower unemployment than they first thought, and they now forecast fewer rate cuts than they expected to make next year.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back here tonight, the breaking news after a family of four was found dead in their home, a mother, father, and two young sons. The investigation taking a dramatic turn today. And news about that Patriots fan who died after that fight at Gillette Stadium. What a preliminary autopsy now shows tonight.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230922ej9k00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW STUDY ON BREAST CANCER BY COUNTY HOW WHERE YOU LIVE CAN IMPACT YOUR HEALTH\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN-US PRISONER DEAL\par \par \uc2 PRISONERS, RELEASED, IRAN, ASSETS\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, DEPUTY, AMBUSH, CLINKUNBROOMER, LUNA, LACKEY\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2 , STRIKE, AUTOMAKERS, WORKERS, NEGOTIATIONS, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, CATASTROPHIC, LIBYA, DAMS, \uc2 UN\uc2 , MISSING\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL SECURITY, OVERPAYMENTS, LORI, COOPER, PAYBACK, WALSH\par \par \uc2 SANDERS, COLORADO, FOOTBALL, OVERTIME, VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "WHEEL OF FORTUNE"\par \par \uc2 CONGRESS, DEADLINE, SPENDING BILLS, HOUSE, SENATE\par \par \uc2 BRAND, INVESTIGATION, SEXUAL ASSAULT, DOCUMENTARY, PERRY\par \par \uc2 CASH, UNCLAIMED, FLORIDA, RAYS, GRAHAM, SILVERMAN\par \par \uc2 SOCCER, MAHONEY, DRAKE, GOAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIVE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 IRAN, DEAL, PRISONER SWAP\par \par \uc2 AMBUSH, SEARCH, CLINKUNBROOMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT ION KILLING LOS ANGELES SHERIFF'S DEPUTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES SEARCH FOR SUSPECT WHO GUNNED DOWN OFFICER IN APPARENT AMBUSH\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES SOAR TO 2023 HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. NATIONAL AVERAGE NOW TOPS $3.88 PER GALLON\par \par \uc2 CHILD CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PRICE OF PARENTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LENDING TREE: ANNUAL CHILD CARE COSTS UP NEARLY 20% FROM 1016-2021\par \par \uc2 MOONVES, "BUT FIRST GOD"\par \par \uc2 SEACREST, "AMERICAN IDOL", "WHEEL OF FORTUNE"\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, DEATH RATES, GEOGRAPHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY ON BREAST CANCER BY COUNTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW WHERE YOU LIVE CAN IMPACT YOUR HEALTH\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a new study on US breast cancer death rates, which shows that where you live could be a factor. Our ABC News chief medical correspondent Dr. Jen Ashton joins us now with more.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, my friend.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning. So, tell us about this study.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, it's interesting we just came off weather and looking at the map because this study is really about geography. It's about county-level social behavior.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, this study looked at different counties across the country and the social variables. Things like obesity. Things like access to mammography. And if you take a look at the map of the country, what's fascinating, those darker pink or red, that's where the highest rates for breast cancer mortality are. So, you see a large distribution across the south, the Carolinas, Virginia, Louisiana, Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what's interesting is we've talked about this a lot before, Linsey. We are looking at the same disease, in this case \uc2 breast cancer now\uc2 . The modern way of looking at it across different genders, across different races, across different ethnicities. And now, different parts of the country, geography.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what would you recommend for those who live in an area with higher rates? How can they lower their risk?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT YOU CAN DO TO TAKE CONTROL OF YOUR HEALTH\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you hear this headline and you think, well, I can't move, right, most of the time nor is that necessarily appropriate. But what I think is appropriate is there are a list of things.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOWERING BREAST CANCER RISK FACTORS\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If you look at that and say, boy, I'm in that area, maybe I'm obese. Maybe I don't have great access to mammography. Here are the things that I can do to lower my risk. So, keeping your weight in a healthy range is very important, staying physically active. And that doesn't necessarily mean having to go to a gym. Minimizing alcohol intake. Again, if you look at the map and you say, gosh, I live in that area, I should not be drinking alcohol, which is a known risk factor, and then not smoking. And then screenings I think is really, really important.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is something that is the gold standard. And we've seen in this country, as mammogram rates drop, mortality, death from breast cancer is going up.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And before I let you go, just because there often is some variation with the guidelines for screening, what's the current guideline for mammograms?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE CURRENT GUIDANCE FOR MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the latest from the US Preventive Service Task Force and, again, ACOG and the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  has their slight differentiation. But for the average risk woman to start mammogram screening at age 40, and then every other year to age 75. But remember keyword, average, 80% of women are average risk until they get that diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Ashton, thank you do much.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up, the very funny Leslie Jones is here live. You will not want to miss it.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231004ej9i0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EXTREME HEAT AND PREGNANCY STUDY: POTENTIALLY LINKED WITH SEVERE MATERNAL COMPLICATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE LEE INTENSIFYING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL HEAT\par \par \uc2 LEE, WINDS, EAST COAST, INTENSITY, TRACK\par \par \uc2 STORMS, LIGHTNING, RAIN, HAIL, POWER, HEATWAVE\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SEARCH, CAVALCANTE, RESIDENTS, BIVENS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, G-20, SUMMIT, CHINA, UKRAINE VIETNAM\par \par \uc2 CONVICTED, NAVARRO, JURY, HOUSE, JAN 6TH\par \par \uc2 AUTOWORKERS, STRIKE, GM, FORD, \uc2 STELLANTIS\par \par \uc2 CAVE, RESCUE, DICKEY, SICK, NOVOSEL\par \par \uc2 ONE CHIP, CHALLENGE, TEEN, DEATH, PAQUI\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, GAUFF, KEYS, PROTESTS, SHELTON, DJOKOVIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCORCHING TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MASTERSON, SENTENCED, ASSAULT, MUELLER, HOLLEY\par \par \uc2 FRANKE, CHILD ABUSE, 911, ARREST, YOUTUBE, FOSTER, DCFS\par \par \uc2 RODDICK, US OPEN, GAUFF, SHELTON, DJOKOVIC, ALCAZAR, FOUNDATION\par \par \uc2 CROSS COUNTRY, RUNNERS, SPORTSMANSHIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATEGORY 5 STORM: MONSTER HURRICANE\par \par \uc2 LEE, HURRICANE, EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 PREGNANCY, HEAT, EXHAUSTION, COMPLICATIONS, MATERNAL\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we now turn to a warning about those high temperatures for expectant mothers. A new study finds excessive heat exposure during pregnancy could be linked with severe maternal complications, and Doctor Jennifer Ashton is here with the details. Great to see you, Doctor Jen.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You too.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you really don't think about this until it happens to you. I had a scare like this a few years ago in a pregnancy. Break down the study for us.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this was really interesting because you're looking at the area where obstetrics and environmental health, the climate, actually overlap. This study done in California used zip codes, then compared them to delivery records in the hospital and found that there was an increased risk of complications like sepsis, hemorrhage, clotting disorders that went up 27 percent when women were exposed to prolonged high temperatures, particularly in the end of their pregnancy. We're talking about 95 degrees and higher for three days or more. So, again, time to connect those dots, as Ginger and I always say, between what's going on in our climate and environment and our medical health.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I was towards the end of my second trimester, so that makes sense. What are some of the signs here for that heat exhaustion?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE SYMPTOMS TO WATCH OUT FOR AND WHAT TO DO IT YOU'RE OVERHEATING\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I think we have to remember this is a spectrum of severity, so you start with heat exhaustion, which is kind of the more moderate kind, midway in terms of the effects, heavy sweating, cold, clammy skin. You can have nausea, vomiting, tiredness or weakness, dizziness, and fainting. If that is not rectified or treated, it can then progress to heat stroke. That is the more severe, so you're talking about high core temperatures, 103 degrees or higher, hot, red, or dry skin, that's the key, your body loses its ability to sweat, nausea, vomiting, confusion, loss of consciousness, or change in mental status. That is a true medical emergency, that person needs to be treated in an emergency room.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And obviously, when you're pregnant, there are a million things to think about. What do you tell your patients as an OB/GYN?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, I think the key is prevention because these things can happen quickly and unexpectedly. So if you can, not put yourself outside in that environment, stay in in air conditioning. If you do have to go out, literally, bring an ice pack from your freezer, keep it in your armpits, around your neck and minimize your time in that heat.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such great advice. Doctor Ashton, as always...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...thank you, and we'll see you on "GMA3."\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230919ej980000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COMMON PAINKILLERS & BIRTH CONTROL PILL NEW STUDY FINDS LINK TO BLOOD CLOTS\b0\par\par\uc2 861 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HEAT, SAFETY, SCHREIBMAN\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE LEE, TRACK, WEATHER, HEAT WAVE, STORMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNRELENTING HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANOTHER DAY OF HIGH TEMPS FROM TEXAS TO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, CAVALCANTE, HOLLAND, DEPAUL, DRUMMOND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR ESCAPED MURDERER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS RELEASE NEW SURVEILLANCE VIDEO OF KILLER'S DARING ESCAPE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, INDICTMENT, GUN CHARGES, GARLAND, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNTER BIDEN FACES INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPECIAL COUNSEL PLANS TO BRING GUN CHARGE IN WAKE OF FAILED PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO EX-TRUMP LAWYERS TO BE TRIED TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DA: GEORGIA ELECTION TRIAL TO TAKE FOUR MONTHS, 150 WITNESSES\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, GREECE, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY FLOODING EMERGENCY IN GREECE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNDREDS RESCUED AFTER ANOTHER DAY IF RECORD RAINFALL\par \par \uc2 MISSILE STRIKE, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING ATTACKS AS BLINKEN VISITS UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA CLAIMS IT SHOT DRONES NEAR MILITARY HEADQUARTERS\par \par \uc2 RECALL, AIRBAGS, ARC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE AIRBAG RECALL PUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REGULATORS: MORE THAN 50 MILLION AIRBAGS AT RISK OF EXPLODING\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, KEYS, OSAKA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN STARS GET SET FOR U.S. SEMIFINALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MADISON KEYS ADVANCES, JOINING COCO GAUFF & BEN SHELTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, MCGRATH, CARNIVAL CRUISE\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, BROOKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO POLICE OFFICER SAVES TRAPPED DRIVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNCONSCIOUS MAN PULLED FROM FIERY CRASH\par \par \uc2 AIRFARES, BERG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLY THE CHEAPER SKIES!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRFARES TO THE LOWEST PRICES IN NEARLY TWO DECADES\par \par \uc2 SPRINGSTEEN, CHIANG, PEPTIC ULCER\par \par \uc2 RAY THE MASCOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WATCHING THE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 HEAT, NORTHEAST, RECORD, WEATHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNRELENTING HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANOTHER DAY OF HIGH TEMPS FROM TEXAS TO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 KILLER, CAVALCANTE, ESCAPE, PRISON, FUGITIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR ESCAPED MURDERER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS RELEASE NEW SURVEILLANCE VIDEO\par \par \uc2 SNAPCHAT, TEENS, PROTECTION, SOCIAL MEDIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNAPCHAT'S NEW TOOLS DESIGNED TO PROTECT TEENS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APP ADDING SAFEGUARDS TO LIMIT INTERACTIONS\par \par \uc2 PAINKILLERS, BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BLOOD CLOTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Time for our "GMA" cover story. A new study looks at the increased risk of blood clots while taking painkillers and birth control pills. Dr. Jen Ashton here to break down the study. What does it tell us?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so, huge study, you guys, done in Denmark, over two million women, just published in the "\uc2 British Medical Journal\uc2 " looking at what we call a class effect between two known huge classes of medications, hormonal contraception and nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory painkillers. We know that they both come with an increase clotting risk. What wasn't known is amongst women who take both of them together what that risk was. So, take a look because the risk was stratified based on the dose of the hormones that these women were exposed to.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, highest risk were combined, were combined estrogen and progestin patch, a vaginal ring, which contains high dose estrogen, higher dose estrogen containing pills and then what we call third generation or fourth generation progestins and anti-androgens like cyproterone. So again, that's the high risk group. Then they went to medium and low risk categories. Amongst those medium risk categories, other combined birth control pills, which are the kind of pills that most women in this country would be on, a Depo-Provera injection, which is a high dose progesterone injection, and then lowest risk, progestin-only pills, certain types of implants, normally containing progestin, and then progestin-containing intrauterine devices. So, very interesting risk stratification based on the type of hormone.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the idea of clotting is not new. We've, we've talked about it. But specifically, what birth controls are we talking about here in this study?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So again, it really depends because when you talk about hormonal contraception, the list I gave is pretty extensive. If you're on any type of hormone for contraception, you want to ask your gynecologist or your health care provider. But in terms of the nonsteroidals, which is also interesting, this pain category, which could be prescription or over the counter, we're talk about things like ibuprofen, naproxen, those things also with associated risk when taken for about a week.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, no specific makers, though? Okay, okay, got it.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Correct.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as far as pain relievers go, are there any that have a higher risk for clotting?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I think those nonsteroidal anti-inflammatories. We're not talking about things like acetaminophen. Again, even though the relative risk was increased, the absolute risk still in the range of about two in 10,000, which is incredibly low, you guys. And as we say in gynecology all the time, the risk of a clot in pregnancy, way higher than this. But this is personal for me, you guys, because daughter had a clot on the pill and nonsteroidal. So, it's just about awareness, you know, the four words, talk to your doctor.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such important awareness. Dr. Ashton, thank you.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230918ej970000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,345 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 JACKSONVILLE, HATE, SHOOTING, DOLLAR GENERAL, WATERS, PITTMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARCH ON WASHINGTON\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRUMP, VOTERS, WASHINGTON, MACE, KNOTTS, CLYBURN, MURPHY, ALBRIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC MUGSHOT\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, DEBATE, BIDEN, POLLING, TRUMP, RAMASWAMY, RICHMOND, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE ROAD TO 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATES HOLD FEISTY FIRST PRIMARY DEBATE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRUMP, DEBATE, ABORTION, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE/FMR US PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 What has taken place here is a travesty of justice. We did nothing wrong. I did nothing wrong, and everybody knows it. I've never had such support.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Have you seen \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's mugshot yet?\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Boo.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Mr. President, are you worried at all about...\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 No. I, I did see it on television.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What did you think?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Handsome guy. Wonderful guy.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and President Biden reacting to Trump's booking at the Fulton County Jail. Let's bring in our Roundtable, former DNC Chair Donna Brazile, "The Dispatch" senior editor, \uc2 Sarah Isgur\uc2 , "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " editorial writer and columnist \uc2 Charles Lane\uc2 , and we welcome "Atlanta Journal Constitution" political columnist Patricia Murphy who we met in Georgia this week. Thanks for flying up here and joining us, Patricia. It's great to have you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm gonna start with you though, Chuck, and turn to the developments in Georgia this week. This is the first time in our nation's history we've seen a presidential mugshot. I know we worry about making things seem normal. That was decidedly not normal. Just reflect on that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BOOKED IN FULTON COUNTY JAIL WITH HISTORIC MUGSHOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA ELECTION CASE DEFENDANTS\par \par \uc2 CHARLES LANE\uc2  (WASHINGTON POST EDITORIAL WRITER AND COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Ex-presidential, but yes. It is a shocking, stunning development, and I mean, it's become now routine apparently that a president, this ex-president will be indicted 'cause this is number four. And I think what strikes me the most about it is how much it has benefitted him politically in the short run in his own world. He raised money off this, Martha. He made, he raised more money in one day off this mugshot moment than he did about the first indictment in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES LANE\uc2  (WASHINGTON POST EDITORIAL WRITER AND COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 So, the other, I think it was $4.2 million this time. So, the other thing we're learning here is that this has not only lost the power to shock certain people, it has become a rallying point for him. And in my mind, it raises the question, the point of this exercise in part is to deter future wrongdoing. And yet, in his mind, he's, and in reality he's being rewarded for it. So, now I'm looking toward a 2024 when perhaps if he does lose a primary, he'll cry fraud about that, having not been deterred here. We are in for a very strange year that we've never had before, the, the likes of which we've never really had before.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We sure are, Sarah. And, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did say basically fundraising, blaming the Justice Department, that, that is his default mode with these indictments.\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I mean, but what we're seeing, if you, you know, look at these focus groups, you'll see Republicans say that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been so self-evidently a bad president that there's no way he can win in 2024. And when you ask the Democratic focus groups, they'll say it is so obvious that we cannot have an indicted felon as president, so \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can't win. And I think part of the problem that we're seeing with these repeated indictments, they're very broad.\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Even some lawyers I don't think can follow all of the different sort of charges and what they exactly mean. They should've gone for the narrow rifle-shot approach here, the documents case, maybe the fake electors, and instead we have something much more broad that I think is psychically making Democrats very happy on the left. But in reality it's exactly what, what Chuck said, which is, it is helping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in this primary. It's why he didn't have to go to the debate. He's getting all the media and attention he needs.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Donna?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first of all, I'm about to lose my entire season tickets to the \uc2 NFL\uc2  because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . So, I want my money back. We're about to see week after week starting tomorrow of repeated criminal trials, or, setting a date for his criminal trial, setting a day for all of the civil action that will take place. So, while in the short-term \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is able to appeal to the congregation within the Republican Party, I think most Americans are turned off, turned off by someone who is using his criminality or all of these charges as, you know, a way to raise his profile, to raise money.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is not funny. When you go after the United States, the peaceful transfer of - power, when you take documents and don't return them, these are serious charges that he is facing. And at some point, someone in his inner circle, I don't know who, will be able to look him in the eye and say, sir, with all due respect, you're gonna be in court for the next six months, and you're going to miss the \uc2 NFL\uc2  season as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP FRONTRUNNERS SAY VOTERS WILL BE JUDGES OF TRUMP'S ALLEGED CRIMES\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll, we'll, we'll wait for that moment, Donna. Patricia, you're in Georgia obviously and, and covering politics. Give us a sense of what it was like down there this week. We obviously talked about politics, but talk about the Fulton County Jail.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP, 18 OTHERS ARRESTED IN FULTON COUNTY, GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 PATRICIA MURPHY (ATLANTA JOURNAL CONSTITUTION POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 It was totally surreal. I was at the Fulton County Jail when he was driven in through those very heavily armored gates, and this in Georgia does not feel like it's just one of four indictments. They're not all blurring together when it comes to this indictment. We all lived through the 2020 election. We lived through the recounts. We had many Georgians receive death threats because of all of the things that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , and others said about especially about the Fulton County election workers.\par \par \uc2 PATRICIA MURPHY (ATLANTA JOURNAL CONSTITUTION POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 We saw that Trump plane come in for rallies. He said it was rigged and stolen before the election happened. It really turned Georgia politics into complete chaos for the last three years. It's never stopped. So, to see him go through the Fulton County Jail on charges he cannot be pardoned from by a president, can't be pardoned by the Governor, this is very, very serious. When he drove through those gates, I said it was like half of a Trump rally because he had all of his Trump supporters there, and a little bit like a funeral, this long procession, and you could've heard a pin drop. Everybody knew this was no joke. This was deadly serious.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and Sarah, I wanna to turn to the debate and, and your reaction to the debate, whether it made any difference and you heard \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 . You heard Cedric Richmond. Did it move the needle at all really? You can go to as many polls as you want.\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. I mean, you talk to for instance, the DeSantis folks or what \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  was saying, and they're gonna say the same thing. This isn't a national contest we're having, we're focused on Iowa, New Hampshire, that's where we're gonna turn the tide, and if we can beat Trump in Iowa and New Hampshire, this polling all changes on a hat. That is true. However, when you talk to the campaigns kind of behind the scenes, what they're gonna tell you is, yeah, like, this debate didn't change anything.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATES HOLD FEISTY FIRST PRIMARY DEBATE\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was never gonna change anything. There's nothing we can say to make \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  not 30 to 40 points ahead of all of us. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can though. He is fully capable of changing the dynamics of this race. And so, yes, we're sitting here with basically a debate over who's gonna be number two because at some point, maybe, you know, an asteroid hits and that's the actual conversation.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ASSESSING THE FIRST REPUBLICAN PRIMARY DEBATE PERFORMANCES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IS ABORTION ISSUE A LIABILITY FOR REPUBLICANS IN 2024?\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and Donna, let's not forget the issues, and, and abortion was a big issue on the stage that night. Democrats are obviously gonna pull that and use that as a tagline.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, and, and you, you heard a lot of different positions, but the bottom line is the Republicans wanna ban abortions. Fine. Let, let American women have the last say on that issue. You know, this is a race for the bottom, a, a race for second or third place, a race to stick around for another month or two. But what I saw at the, watching the debate, and by the way, this is my Republican red. I wanted to pay homage to you, Sarah.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What, what I saw was a bunch of candidates that really don't know how to move beyond \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . So, this shopping spree will continue for the number two position or the number three position, but nothing came out of that debate that scared me.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and Charles, some Republicans may be worried about Trump's general election vulnerabilities. Patricia said that in our piece, as a matter of fact, that some are looking for other people. Is he really vulnerable?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SKIPS FIRST REPUBLICAN PRIMARY DEBATE\par \par \uc2 CHARLES LANE\uc2  (WASHINGTON POST EDITORIAL WRITER AND COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think if you look at polls, which unfortunately that's all we really have to go on, he's trailing slightly to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I, my gut tells me that with I think it's above 50 percent of the public also telling pollsters they wouldn't vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which is very different from the GOP primary electorate, you'd have to say he is, of course Trump is vulnerable. But if there is a third party that chips into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's vote, that could change. And a lot depends, I think, also on who Trump picks as a running mate.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANY VOTERS UNSATISFIED WITH BIDEN-TRUMP REMATCH POSSIBILITY\par \par \uc2 CHARLES LANE\uc2  (WASHINGTON POST EDITORIAL WRITER AND COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 But I, I have the impression watching that debate that you have these a certain group of candidates like \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , others, practically begging their primary electorate to kind of come to their senses, you know, understand, like, Nikki Haley was saying, look, we don't have 60 votes for an, an abortion ban so let's do something more moderate, and they are being tuned out by this primary electorate, which is absolutely still devoted to Trump.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and Patricia, I, I want to ask you about something you said in the piece and down there. You called \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a depreciating asset. What are you seeing of, of the President's chances there, and, and in the Black vote in particular?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NYT/SIENA POLL: BIDEN LOSING KEY SUPPORT FROM BLACK VOTERS\par \par \uc2 PATRICIA MURPHY (ATLANTA JOURNAL CONSTITUTION POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policies have been very popular particularly among the Democratic base. We've had billions of dollars flood into the state of Georgia. We've seen a lot of policies that Georgia voters, particularly Democrats, wanted out of him. However, his age I do think is an issue. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also has not really been presented as a viable alternative if something, God forbid, happens. So, he is a depreciating asset. I think about him a little bit like a car that's been driven off the lot. He has a lot of miles on his tires.\par \par \uc2 PATRICIA MURPHY (ATLANTA JOURNAL CONSTITUTION POLITICAL COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 However, in a general election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is like a car bomb that's gone off in the Republican Party. Our own Republican governor has to go back and tell Republican voters, these elections are secure. This election was not stolen. Our nominee needs to look forward, not back. He's talking about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . So, Republicans are worried about the apparatus of the election, that their own Republican voters have been convinced by the former president that they can't trust those ballots and then also just about his politics.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Thanks to all of you. I know you'll all be back.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, the latest on that jet crash mystery and the fate of the man who led a short-lived mutiny in Russia. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, 60 years since \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 .'s famous "I Have a Dream" Speech at the March on Washington. Pierre Thomas looks back at the watershed moment in the push for racial equality.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230831ej8r00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REPUBLICANS FACE OFF IN FIRST PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE EIGHT GOP CANDIDATES CLASH OVER FOREIGN POLICY, ABORTION & TRUMP\b0\par\par\uc2 1,070 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, RAMASWAMY, PENCE, SCOTT, DESANTIS, HALEY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we're going to begin with the debate. There's an arena in, there it is, the arena in Milwaukee where the eight GOP presidential hopefuls took the stage last night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS FACE OFF IN FIRST PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EIGHT GOP CANDIDATES CLASH OVER FOREIGN POLICY, ABORTION & TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It was a heated debate covering a wide range of topics, including the candidate who was not there. Rachel Scott in Milwaukee with the highlights for us. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning to you. With Donald Trump sitting this debate out, his closest rival, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , was bracing for an onslaught of attacks. But in the end, it was the political newcomer, entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  who became a top target.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, a heated and combative Republican debate. Eight candidates facing off for the first time and not holding back.\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm the only person on the stage who wasn't bought and paid for.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TIM SCOTT (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Going back and forth being childish is not helpful to the American people to decide on the next leader of our country.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 This is exactly why Margret Thatcher said, if you want something said, ask a man. If you want something done, ask a woman.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the candidate drawing the most attention and criticism, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . The 38-year-old entrepreneur and fierce defender of Trump, recently seeing a rise in the polls.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  DRAW FIRE FROM GOP RIVALS\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm not sure I exactly understood \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 's comment, but I'll let you parse that out. For me, it's pretty simple, that's something a US president can do with focus and I'll deliver on it.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, let me explain to you. Let me explain it to you, Vivek, because I can. I'll go slower this time. We don't need to bring in a rookie, we don't need to bring people without experience.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Listen. Listen.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It was Ramaswamy's first debate.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You have no foreign policy experience and it shows. It shows.\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And you know what, the foreign policy experience that you all have...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The businessman trying to address his lack of political experience early on.\par \par \uc2 VIVEK RAMASWAMY\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Who the heck is this skinny guy with a funny last name and what's he doing in the middle of this debate stage? I tell you, I'm not a politician.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That line later called out by former New Jersey Governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I've had enough already tonight of a guy who sounds like ChatGPT stand up here. And the last person in one of these debates who stood in the middle of the stage and said, what's a skinny guy with an odd last name doing up here was Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the candidate who earned the center spot on the stage, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , did not stand out from the rest of the pack.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Our country is in decline. This decline is not inevitable. It's a choice. We need to send Joe Biden back to his basement.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The sparring on stage ranged from foreign policy, to clashing over abortion restrictions.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But just to be clear, governor, would you sign a six-week ban federally?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm going to stand on the side of life.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR DOUG BURGUM (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I am on the record, and I stand behind that we should not have a federal abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We need to stop demonizing this issue.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But there was some consensus. Nearly every candidate agreed former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  did the right thing on January 6th. DeSantis, ready to move on.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I kept my oath to the Constitution that day. There's no more important duty, right?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We've been through this. We've answered this so many times.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 So, answer the question.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I've answered this before.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, yes?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Why are we, Mike did his duty. I've got no beef with him. But here's the thing, is this what we're going to be focusing on going forward? The rehashing of this?\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm relieved.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) About an hour into the debate, the focus turned to the candidate who was not on the stage, the front runner, former President Donald Trump, now facing four indictments and 91 charges.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Would you still support him as your party's choice? Please raise your hand if you would.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Almost all of the candidates eventually raising their hands.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Whether or not you believe that the criminal charges are right or wrong, the conduct is beneath the office of president of the United States. And, and, you know, this is the great thing about this country. Booing is allowed, but it doesn't change the truth. It doesn't change the truth.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Christie was booed multiple times for going after the former president. Trump skipping this debate entirely, releasing a prerecorded interview instead. As his rivals look to get back out on the campaign trail today, Trump will be expected to surrender to authorities in Georgia. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's exactly right, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230905ej8o00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW CDC REPORT ON MATERNITY CARE RAISING AWARENESS ABOUT POTENTIAL MISTREATMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 673 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; TRUMP SURRENDER LOOMING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO FIRST REPUBLICAN DEBATE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, SURRENDER, GIULIANI, WILLIS, MEADOWS, DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, GOP, DESANTIS, RAMASWAMY, CHRISTIE, TRUMP, MCDANIEL\par \par \uc2 HAROLD, RAIN, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 HEAT, ALERTS, TEMPERATURES, SCHOOLS\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, RECOVERY, DNA, GREEN, ERICKSON\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, IRIZARRY, VIDEO, POLICE, GARCIA, DIAL, OUTLAW\par \par \uc2 TRAPPED, RESCUE, CABLE CAR, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RETAIL, THEFTS, ORGANIZED, PROFITS, FELDMAN, CONSUMERS\par \par \uc2 EXPLOSION, FARLEY, GAS LEAK, GREENE, MEIER\par \par \uc2 CORCORAN, HOUSING, MORTGAGES, RATES, FED, BUYING, SELLING\par \par \uc2 GIRAFFE, SPOTLESS, ZOO, BRIGHTS, NAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIVE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT, GEORGIA, ELECTION, CONSPIRACY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SET TO SURRENDER IN GEORGIA ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT SAYS HE WILL TURN HIMSELF IN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, REPUBLICAN, POLITICS, PRESIDENT, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST REPUBLICAN DEBATE HOURS AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EIGHT GOP CONTENDERS TO SQUARE OFF\par \par \uc2 HEAT, MIDWEST, WEATHER, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME HEAT HITS THE HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 104 MILLION AMERICANS IN 22 STATES ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY, "RICH MEN NORTH OF RICHMOND", SINGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE MAN BEHIND MUSIC'S SURPRISE #1 HIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW OLIVER ANTHONY WENT UNKNOWN TO CHART-TOPPER\par \par \uc2 CDC, REPORT, HEALTH, MATERNITY, PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CDC REPORT ON MATERNITY CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAISING AWARENESS ABOUT POTENTIAL MISTREATMENT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go to Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George, thank you. Now to a new CDC report about the perceptions women have about their treatment during pregnancy, and the results were not good. Dr. Jen Ashton joins us now to break it all down. Okay, so explain why the CDC is raising alarm about this?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think first of all, just big picture view, we have a national embarrassment in our maternal mortality rate. We are facing a crisis here in this country, with the rate of women dying during childbirth that has been increasing for 20 years, racial disparity there, as you see with other situations, with Black women at higher risk, facing three times the rate of death compared to white women during pregnancy. And some women feel and perceive discrimination in their care during pregnancy and delivery. And this may discourage them from speaking up, from seeking help, and that's part of what this study really got to.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, what do you think is the biggest takeaway for women but, in particular, minority women, as you mentioned?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT WARNING SIGNS TO LOOK OUT FOR\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Listen, I think no one knows your body better than the person who is in that body, right, so women need to feel empowered, to speak up, to have their conversation with their health care provider, whether it's a doctor or a midwife. And you should find a doctor or a midwife that you feel very comfortable with. This is a major life event. Bringing a friend or family member with you is always is good idea. And never, never, never hesitate to speak up if you feel uncomfortable, if you feel something isn't right, or if you have questions.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some medical providers are criticizing this study. Why?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I mean, the methodology with this study is getting a lot of kind of side-eye view here, in terms of how it was conducted, recall bias, surveys on women five years after their pregnancy ended, not a nationally representative sample. But again, it focused on perception. Perception is important, and when you're talking about this crisis, communication is at the hub of it. At the end of the day yesterday, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  did issue a statement saying, and I quote, "to improve maternal health outcomes, it's imperative that pregnant and postpartum patients feel comfortable communicating with members of their healthcare team." \uc2 ACOG\uc2  knows we need to do better at this.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Got to talk to the doctor, ask questions. All right, Dr. Jen, our thanks to you, as always.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230831ej8n0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL RULING SETS UP SUPREME COURT BATTLE FEDERAL APPEALS COURT SEEKS TOUGHER RESTRICTIONS ON MIFEPRISTONE\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, SEARCH, GREEN, MARSHALL, TREU, CASTILLO\par \par \uc2 EVACUATION, WILDFIRE, CANADA\par \par \uc2 INDICTMENT, TRUMP, WILLIS, PENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRETARY OF STATE CALLS AMERICAN DETAINED IN RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCE: BLINKEN REASSURES PAUL WHELAN U.S. IS WORKING TO FREE HIM\par \par \uc2 WHEELAN, BLINKEN, RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 AIR SCARE, ENGINE, FIRE, KLEINECKE, SOUTHWEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR SCARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLAMES SEEN SHOOTING FROM SOUTHWEST PLANE JUST AFTER TAKEOFF\par \par \uc2 MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL RULING SETS UP SUPREME COURT BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL APPEALS COURT SEEKS TOUGHER RESTRICTIONS ON MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the latest court ruling about the popular abortion pill mifepristone and what it means for access to the drug. Faith Abubey joins us with the very latest. Good morning, Faith.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And good morning to you, Linsey. This court's decision is an extraordinary challenge to that \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved abortion drug that's now been on the market for more than 20 years.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A federal judge siding with a conservative plaintiff, saying that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decision in 2016 to expand the use of mifepristone to ten weeks gestation and then, in 2021, further relaxing regulation making it more widely available and accessible went too far and ignored some safety concerns.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the Biden administration is now firing back, making it clear that it strongly disagrees with the ruling.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Vice President adding that this is just another step towards a nationwide abortion ban and that "this lawsuit is a threat to a woman's freedom to make decisions about her own body." Now, we know this ruling doesn't take effect right away, but it does now set the stage for another Supreme Court battle over abortion. The drug maker, meanwhile, is saying that it's confident in the pill's safety and effectiveness and also promises to fight the injunction. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Faith Abubey, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230825ej8h0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,200 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 MAUI, HAWAII, WILDFIRES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC DEVASTATION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GARLAND, CHUTKAN, WEISS, TRUMP, BHARARA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SCANDAL ELECTION"\par \par \uc2 RASKIN, BIDEN, WEISS, SPECIAL COUNSEL, MCCARTHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GARLAND APPOINTS SPECIAL COUNSEL IN HUNTER BIDEN CASE\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, 2024, RUBIO, RNC, DEBATE, PLEDGE, TRUMP, CHUTKAN\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM FEBRUARY 6, 2016\par \par \uc2 2024, IOWA, STATE FAIR, PENCE, HALEY, DESANTIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 2024, DEBATE, DESANTIS, TRUMP, VOTERS, POLLS, PENCE, BIDEN, GARLAND, WEISS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. Let's bring in our Powerhouse Roundtable, former DNC Chair Donna Brazile, "National Review" editor and "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " contributing columnist \uc2 Ramesh Ponnuru\uc2 , "New Yorker" staff writer Susan Glasser, and we want to welcome our newest ABC News contributor, Rachel Bade, also, of course, the co-author of the "Politico Playbook."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN CANDIDATES STORM IOWA STATE FAIR\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Rachel, let me start with you because you were just out in Iowa. I think you'd just landed maybe even this morning, but, but very (inaudible) recently. What's your sense? Anybody able to break through all the Trump noise, any of the other candidates?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I mean, it's interesting because, you know, in light of all these negative headlines that the DeSantis campaign has, sort of, been experiencing lately, they've been, sort of, clinging to this bright spot. And that is Iowa. He's actually polling better there than he is nationwide. He's seen as more likable, more trustworthy than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in that state. And yet, when you're at the fair on Saturday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  comes in on the day that DeSantis is there, and all of a sudden, you know, crowds are swarming him and he is sucking up all the headlines.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I will say, you know, from the point of DeSantis' campaign, they're very much looking at Iowa as this, sort of, "Field of Dreams" sight, type mantra. "If you build it, they will come." They're really focused on creating this, sort of, hyper local campaign, visiting all 99 counties, appointing county-level chairs in all 99 counties and trying to, sort of, woo local leaders. They were telling me and there's a belief that if you look at Republicans who won the state of Iowa previously, a lot of them were barely polling in the, the single digits at this point in the campaign, and would end up coming in to win Iowa, Ted Cruz, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 . And so, there's a feeling amongst the DeSantis people...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rick Santoro? So, but...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...that it's not over, it's not over yet. So, we'll see.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, Donna, you've, you've worked Iowa from the other side.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Does that sound like wishful thinking coming from...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First of all, I missed those fried cheese - curls. I missed the pork chop on a stick, the fried butter and the fried dill pickles.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fried butter. Not familiar with that.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, I, I just want to put it all on the table that I enjoyed my time at the fair. Look, President, former President Trump, as the judge calls him now, Mr. Trump, he, he brought the sunshine. He brought Floridians on the, on his plane. He created that circus that we saw yesterday. And you're right, there was no more oxygen left for Mr. DeSantis. I don't know if Mr. DeSantis can recover some of the momentum he had earlier this year when everyone thought, I say everyone but not me, that he was going to be the best alternative.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We still have Tim Scott who's rising in, in Iowa. You still have, I think, this unknown factor of what might happen over the next two months that could also spell disaster. But, for right now, I think everybody's waiting for the debate and I know I am.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP PRESIDENTIAL PRIMARY\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Ramesh, does he show up? Trump, that is.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think the normal political calculation for somebody in his position, with such a huge lead in the national polls, is not to show up. What's the upside? Except that Trump has always had such a keen sense of drama, and the drama of keeping everybody guessing and then showing up and showing that he's not intimidated, you could see how that might appeal to him.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 538 POLLING AVERAGE: TRUMP MAINTAINS COMMANDING LEAD\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Does, does he pay a price if he doesn't show up?\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Well...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I know that you need, usually if you're way ahead, don't take any risk.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But is there a risk in not showing up?\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 The other candidates presumably start making the argument that he feels entitled and that he feels afraid, and traditionally that kind of thing does have some effect. Whether it has an effect against Trump is a, is an open question.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That seems like a weak way to go after Trump considering everything else that's there.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, I mean, you know, and, and, and if, Susan, if he does, let me ask you what I asked \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 . If he doesn't sign that pledge, does \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  really say no, we're gonna leave the frontrunner out of the debate?\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 Well, since \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  and the RNC have been essentially an arm of the Trump campaign, both in 2020 and so far in 2024, you know, when in doubt, when it comes to, you know, sort of this Republican Party, it's become so Trump-ified, imagine that they'll find a way around it.\par \par \uc2 ROUNDTABLE PANELIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , by the way, you know, I believe in the past he said that he would sign the pledge but then disregard it and doesn't plan to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But, you know, again and again and again, Jonathan, this is his story. The story is the Republican Party finding a way to justify the unjustifiable. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you know, there's nothing that man doesn't love more than a camera. So, our default setting has got to be that he's gonna find his way in the middle, right?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEN DAYS UNTIL 1ST REPUBLICAN PRIMARY DEBATE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He might show up. That he might show up. But, you know, Christie, I thought was interesting, Rachel, in saying that, you know, he thought he made a mistake and the others made a mistake by not taking Trump on in 2016 early. Actually, Christie waited another four or five years to do so. But, I mean, what, what is your sense? Are, are, are they finally gonna, gonna, gonna take him on? Or is this...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, is he gonna, like is he actually going to show up? I mean...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, you're seeing Pence. I mean, you made a very interesting point. Pence is going nowhere in the polls. His fundraising's in trouble, barely made the debate stage. But, is he campaigning for something else?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I mean, it was really interesting to watch Pence, because the Vice President, you know, after January 6th and for several months, you know, after Trump left office, he didn't want to talk about what happened that day. And, you know, at the fair, we very much saw Pence lean in on talking about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and how he was wrong about the 2020 election, and how he didn't have authority to just throw out, you know, Electoral College votes.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I watched as a number of people came up and shook his hand, thanked him for doing that. He also got heckled for doing that. But, he, he brought it up unprompted and he was very much taking shots at Trump on this. And sort of the, the observation my colleague and I had at Politico was that, you know, this doesn't really help him with GOP voters. So, is he running for something else? Is he running for legacy? And we asked him about that, and he said, you know, "I'm running to win."\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, of course...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you gotta wonder because, you know, it certainly...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...wouldn't help him in the polls.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took on the Republican establishment in 2016, and I don't think the establishment, and maybe you know better since you understand the Republican establishment. They haven't been able to really get their sea legs back. I don't know if the Republican Party will ever be a, quote, unquote, "a mainstream party" again like it was before when you understood conservatism, Conservative values.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But now you have a, a indicted defendant out on bail who is leading the party, who is basically running on a platform of retribution, and that is gonna define not just the presidential race, but I think all of the down ballot races as well.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, explicitly running on retribution.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 If I, you know, getting it back to the Pence point, I understand everybody thinks it is, you know, so many Republicans either think that Trump won in '20 or think it's rude to point out that he didn't win in 2020. But, I do think that the other candidates have to make that case if they're serious about winning because what is your argument left? If Trump actually won in 2020, counterfactually, you know, and it was stolen from him...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, and why, yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Then of course, that's the top issue and you can't say he's a loser. You can't say he's not electable because he, in that alternate reality, won two presidential races already.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and meanwhile, we have what happened in Ohio which should be a big warning sign...\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...for, for, for Republicans, right? The, this, this, this, you know, Ohio, big victory for the abortion rights movement, big defeat for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO VOTERS KEEP 50% THRESHOLD TO CHANGE CONSTITUTION\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think part of...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In a Republican state.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 That's right. Look, part of this is the incredible distortion field where we are, we are all somehow living in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's alternate reality, right?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 We are talking about well, it's a great benefit to him according to, you know, big story in the "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " today that he's been indicted criminally, what, three times and it looks like a fourth coming up this week, because we're living in this warped distortion field of a Republican primary in which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is stampeding. It's a minority of a minority in the country. And so, then you have something like these series of abortion rights referendums in the wake of the Roe versus Wade decision. And you realize that in this country...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Changes Ohio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IS ABORTION ISSUE A LIABILITY FOR REPUBLICANS IN 2024?\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 ...even in deep red states, there are solid majorities that don't think, you know, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should be the president again, who defeated him in the popular vote in 2016 and in 2020, who support by actually record numbers abortion rights. And yet, we live in this world where it's somehow good that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a criminal defendant, but somehow bad electorally for the President that his son is being investigated for something that as far as we know does not directly concern Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Let me, let, let me ask you about that, Donna. Does, so, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , this, elevating this to a special counsel, I mean, the White House cannot be happy with Garland about this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GARLAND APPOINTS SPECIAL COUNSEL IN HUNTER BIDEN CASE\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first of all, let me just say this, I mean, no one is above the law, not even the son of a president of the United States. We need to stress that.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You don't see Democrats out here attacking \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . You don't see Democrats out here, you know, saying the Justice Department is weaponized against the Bidens. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been under investigation for five years. I, I can tell you, that must, that, that, that is painful. That's painful not just to the President, but for people who love the Biden family, because he has been under attack. He signed the plea deal a couple of months ago and it fell apart. It collapsed once the judge took a look at the writing and said, I don't like all of these commas, or, you know, I'm not a lawyer, so I don't want to pretend to be one.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, the fact is he's now going to go through this arduous...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, like you said, it's almost five years and it's gonna go on longer now. So...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Five years. Five years and there's no evidence - linking Hunter's business dealings to the President. The Republicans have tried everything in Congress. They've tried everything, but this is warmed over leftovers and I do believe at the end of the day, if they can get that deal back on the table, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  will be able to, finally be able to live his life again.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, so - Republicans called for the Special Counsel, now are denouncing the Special Counsel. I understand they say Weiss shouldn't be the guy, but is there, is there another reason behind this, Rachel?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS BLAST NEW SPECIAL COUNSEL, AFTER CALLING FOR ONE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why Republicans are upset by the Justice Department doing something they asked the Justice Department to do?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the hypocrisy on it is, it's peak Washington right there. But, yeah, I mean, it's, publicly Republicans are saying they don't trust the guy who was named specifically. But...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David Weiss.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, of course, but there's other reasons. I mean, this really blows a hole in their top talking point when it comes to the White House and that is this idea of, you know, weaponization...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...of the Justice Department, you know, saying that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's being treated differently than President Trump. Now the Biden family has more, you know, special counsels than Trump does himself.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this is a man who's been indicted what will be fourth, the fourth time potentially this week. And the other reason is that Republicans really wanted to do a quick impeachment of Joe Biden. They were (inaudible) been planning on it. This really complicates that plan because usually...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you go back to when Democrats flipped the House in the 2019, there was a belief, you know, they were gonna impeach Trump at some point. But, the mantra on the Hill was like, okay, we don't touch this until the Special Counsel finishes his work.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mueller.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, Robert Mueller.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, that's right.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This just could very much, since it's just starting, could drag out into next year which means that any impeachment push they have is potentially going to stall. Moderate Republicans are not gonna wanna vote for an impeachment inquiry if there is an ongoing special counsel investigation into this.\par \par \uc2 RAMESH PONNURU\uc2  (NATIONAL REVIEW EDITOR/WAPO CONTRIBUTING COLUMNIST)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What, what do you make of McCarthy raising the impeachment? I mean, was he ever serious about it?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP EYEING HUNTER CASE AS GROUNDS FOR BIDEN IMPEACHMENT\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 You know...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Or...\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 You know, he has to be serious about it because he is being led around by the nose, essentially, by a faction of any five House Republicans. And I think, you know, he has flirted again and again, whether it's with shutting down the government or the impending, you know, crisis we may have with government spending in September. Same thing with impeachment. He has a radical sort of fringe that's able to threaten essentially to depose him at any moment.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN GLASSER (THE NEW YORKER STAFF WRITER)\par \par \uc2 You know, I can't even keep straight what the, what the message is from Kevin McCarthy at this moment. I can't tell you is he, wait. Is he for impeachment right now or he's for it maybe. I...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. On that, Ramesh, we'll get you next week on this one.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, another potential indictment looms for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Georgia. Our Aaron Katersky is there at the courthouse. And we speak with one of the likely key witnesses in that case, next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230818ej8d00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HALLE BERRY GETS REAL ABOUT MENOPAUSE STAR ON WHY SHE'S PUSHING BACK AGAINST THE STIGMAS\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 EVACUATIONS, MACON, SCOTT, WILDFIRES, WEINTRAUB, KENT, MAUI\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, EVACUATION, TRAVEL, MAUI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAVELERS STUCK AT MAUI AIRPORT AMID DEVASTATING BLAZES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, THREAT, ROBERTSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT KILLED IN FBI RAID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UTAH MAN WAS BEING INVESTIGATED FOR MAKING THREATS AGAINST PRESIDENT BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FEINSTEIN, HEALTH, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATOR FEINSTEIN'S HEALTH SCARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 90-YEAR-OLD LAWMAKER BRIEFLY HOSPITALIZED AFTER FALL\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS DUE OUT THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 MLB, LORENZEN, WILSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEEL GOOD PHILLIES!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTON WILSON HITS HOME RUN IN FIRST MLB AT BAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAITI, DORSAINVIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN HOSTAGE FREED IN HAITI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSE & DAUGHTER SAFE AFTER KIDNAPPED NEARLY TWO WEEKS AGO\par \par \uc2 MURDER, TUPAC, DAVIS, KNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS IN TUPAC MURDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEWLY-OBTAINED POLICE VIDEO SHOWS RAID AT HOME NEAR LAS VEGAS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, BERG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LANDING BIG TRAVEL SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY NOW IS THE TIME TO BOOK FLIGHTS FOR FALL\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, "1989"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 FIRES, MAUI, HAWAII, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY HAWAII WILDFIRE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 36 KILLED AS BLAZES DEVASTATE MAUI\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, INTEREST, ECONOMY, RATE HIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS DUE OUT THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 BERRY, ACTOR, MENOPAUSE, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLE BERRY GETS REAL ABOUT MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR ON WHY SHE'S PUSHING BACK AGAINST THE STIGMAS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a lovely morning outside in New York City. Welcome back. It is time now for our "GMA" cover story, Halle Barry talking about menopause. The Oscar-winning actress says she's embracing the change and rejecting the stigmas that comes with aging. Bravo. Erielle Reshef has details. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you. Bravo indeed. Berry says that she is smack dab in the middle of menopause, and she wants to challenge the preconceived notions about this stage of life and empower more women to not only accept it but celebrate it.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning Oscar-winning actress Halle Berry pushing back forcefully against harmful stigmas associated with menopause.\par \par \uc2 HALLE BERRY (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I am challenging everything I thought I knew about menopause, like your life is over, you are disposable, society no longer has a place for you, you should retire, you should pack it up. I'm challenging all of those stereotypes.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 56-year-old star telling "Women's Health" magazine she is solidly in her womanhood, embracing this season of life and encouraging more women to proudly do the same.\par \par \uc2 HALLE BERRY (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm my best self now that I reached 56 years old. I have the most to offer.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Berry emphasizing the importance of openly talking about menopause so more women feel comfortable sharing their own experiences, something doctors say is essential to normalizing what can be sensitive changes.\par \par \uc2 DR. NITA LANDRY (OB-GYN)\par \par \uc2 As we start to have these very important conversations, it allows us to demystify it. We're able to communicate about what we're experiencing so women don't feel as alone. When you're having those conversations, you can really start to empower yourself through education.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Berry also urging women to own wherever they are in life.\par \par \uc2 HALLE BERRY (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Take your time and figure yourself out. You don't have to be rushed. You don't have to be forced. It's not a race.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLE BERRY ON FACING MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS TALKS EMBRACING THIS SEASON OF HER LIFE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Berry credits exercise with helping her feel in touch with her body. She says it's not about how you look but feeling strong and comfortable in your own skin. And she also says breaking this taboo surrounding menopause starts with women being comfortable talking to other women about it. We know that's true, guys.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Good for her. I love to hear this.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I love that so many people are talking about menopause now, honestly.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, Erielle, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230821ej8a0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH STAKES OHIO ELECTION VOTERS REJECT GOP BALLOT INITIATIVE IN WIN FOR ABORTION RIGHTS\b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A WINNER\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, WINNER, JACKPOT, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 JACKPOT, TICKET, MEGA MILLIONS, PUBLIX\par \par \uc2 FIRES, MAUI, EVACUATIONS, DESTRUCTION, TEXAS, MALLINGER\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, OHIO, GOP, REJECT, ABORTION, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thanks, Ginger. As you said, not over yet. Well now to the special election results in Ohio overnight that could determine the future of abortion rights in that state. Erielle Reshef has the latest. Good morning to you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES OHIO ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS REJECT GOP BALLOT INITIATIVE IN WIN FOR ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you guys. A consequential vote for sure. Ohioans delivering a major win for abortion rights, voting down a Republican ballot initiative called issue 1, that would have raised the threshold to pass constitutional amendments to 60% rather than a simple majority. That would have made it harder to pass a measure expected to appear on the ballot in Ohio in November to protect abortion in the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The White House hailing this vote as a win for choice, saying Ohio voters rejected "A blatant attempt to weaken voters' voices and further erode the freedom of women to make their own health decisions." Anti-abortion advocates slamming the outcome, calling it a sad day for Ohio, blaming it on money from outside liberal special interest groups and inaction from the Ohio business community.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But big picture here, the measure on the Ohio ballot in November will be the nation's latest referendum on abortion rights since the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe V. Wade last year. Similar initiatives in California, Michigan and Vermont, enshrined abortion protections into their state constitutions. Experts say results in Ohio could be a bell weather of how contentious and how top of mind this issue is for voters nationwide in 2024. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej890002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS ON WHEELS BIG SAVINGS ON PRODUCTS FROM MASSACHUSETTS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE 