MINANCE OF WOMEN IN GENRE\par \par \uc2 PICKLEBALL, CITYPICKLE, SPORTS, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING NATIONAL PICKLEBALL DAY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. We are celebrating National Pickleball Day. It is one of the fastest-growing sports in the country with almost five million players nationwide. And this morning, our Lori Bergamotto is getting in on the action.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "THE GOLDBERGS"\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN TOBOLOWSKY ("THE GOLDBERGS")\par \par \uc2 Pickleball, the sport of kings.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) From TV shows to competitions, and, yes, the Kardashians, too, pickleball is indeed here to stay.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just in the past year, nearly 50 million Americans have picked up a paddle to play pickleball. No wonder it's America's fastest growing sport.\par \par \uc2 MARY CANNON (CITYPICKLE)\par \par \uc2 Two years ago, we had to explain what pickleball was. Now, pickleball is on the tips of everybody's tongue.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) CityPickle co-founders Erica Desai and Mary Cannon helping to bring the pickle craze to the Big \uc2 Apple\uc2  masses.\par \par \uc2 ERICA DESAI (CITYPICKLE)\par \par \uc2 We like to say whether you're eight or 88, you can play pickleball. It's something you can learn in a very short time and have a really good time playing.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Lydia, (PH) I hear you're a certified pickleball coach. Tell me the three things I need to know.\par \par \uc2 LYDIA (PICKLEBALL COACH)\par \par \uc2 First thing is the serve must always be underhand. Second, stay out of the kitchen. And the third, potentially most important, is to have fun.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love fun so let's play. Okay, ready? And I do love fun. So, it was so much fun. Pickleball is truly a sport for all ages, from kids to parents to grandparents. Everyone is headed to the courts. And the market, the pickleball industry is growing alongside of the sport, the market expected to nearly double, into the billions, by 2030. I'm here at CityPickle, you guys, in Central Park, having way too much fun. And we're going to show you all of the gear that you need. We're going to start by reminding you that everything is shoppable, so scan that QR code at the bottom of your screen. And I'm going to interrupt this game that Lydia, our model, is playing. Come here with our "GMA" intern, Daniel, (PH) over there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIUPIPO PICKLE PADDLES\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Lydia is using one of the most important things you need in pickleball, which is the paddle. And this is top rated on Amazon, nearly 14,000 positive reviews. It is super lightweight, and it has an inner core that's very lightweight, but it increases your strength when you're hitting, right? So, that's great.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FRANKLIN SPORTS X-40 PICKLEBALLS\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, We can't play pickleball without the actual pickleball. So, this one is from Franklin Sports. It is the pickleball to get, you guys, super affordable, dent resistant, long lasting. Get that at Amazon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FRANKLIN SPORTS PICKLEBALL ELITE PERFORMANCE SLING BAG\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now, when you've got all your gear, you need somewhere to tote it. So Rowan, I'm going to steal Brandon, (PH) your partner, away. But Brandon is toting one of these great bags that we found at \uc2 Kohl's\uc2 . It's from Franklin Sports. Brandon, go ahead and open that up. It fits six paddles, it fits a ball pouch, and there's even a spot for your cell phone or whatever else you need.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPANX GET MOVING DRESS\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's not all, you guys. It wouldn't be a segment that I'm doing unless there's fun pickleball fashion. So, Lydia is sporting what I think is one of the best exercise dresses out there. This is from \uc2 Spanx\uc2 . You guys, it smooths everything without suffocating, right? Doesn't it feel so comfy?\par \par \uc2 LYDIA (PICKLEBALL COACH)\par \par \uc2 Feels great.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She looks fantastic. And look, it even has, like, nice pockets right there. She can put that pickleball right in there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SKECHERS VIPER COURT PICKLEBALL SHOES\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we can't forget about shoes. So, let's talk about Brandon's shoes. These are from \uc2 Skechers\uc2 . You guys, they're made with Goodyear on the bottom, Goodyear rubber on the bottom, on those outsoles, for a great grip, super comfortable, removable insoles. So, we've got everything you need. Rebecca, when are we booking a court?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am so ready to play, Lori. I'm also very hungry for a pickle right now. I don't know if you have any of those out there. Anyway, great stuff, Lori. Thank you to our models, and thanks to all of you. All these pickleball items are shoppable right now using the QR code on the bottom of your screen or by heading to goodmorningamerica.com.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MICHAEL OHER LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE "WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,690 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED BAHAMAS MURDER-FOR-HIRE PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA MOM ACCUSED OF CONSPIRING TO KILL HUSBAND SET TO BE RELEASED ON BAIL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NATIONAL MONUMENT, TRIBAL, MINING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN DECLARES NEW NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTECTING TRIBAL LAND NEAR GRAND CANYON FROM URANIUM MINING\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, STEIDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CRITICALLY INJURED IN SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 : WOMAN BITTEN ON LEG AT ROCKAWAY BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, OWEN, BOAT, DOCK\par \par \uc2 FRIEDKIN, BURSTYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING OSCAR WINNER WILLIAM FRIEDKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR BEHIND "THE FRENCH CONNECTION" & "THE EXORCIST" DIES AT AGE 87\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, BULLOCK, ALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANDRA BULLOCK'S HEARTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNER BRYAN RANDALL DIES AFTER PRIVATE THREE-YEAR BATTLE WITH ALS\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, HERRERA, ROHRBACH, \uc2 FEDEX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO DELIVERY DRIVER REUNITED WITH MAN HE SAVED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDEX WORKER PULLED MAN FROM WRECKAGE OF BURNING CAR\par \par \uc2 STORMS, EAST COAST, DEATH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE SUMMER STORMS TURN DEADLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED AS WEATHER SLAMS EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ZELLE, SCAM, BANK, APP, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS\par \par \uc2 "POLTERGEIST GIRL", MURDER, DOCUMENTARY, BOYER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 ANDI, ROBOT, HEAT, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE DANGER OF EXCESSIVE HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USING TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STAY SAFE\par \par \uc2 NOTEBOOK, CREAM, JEWELRY, CARDS, DECANTER, PRETZEL\par \par \uc2 OHER, "WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHAEL OHER LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do welcome you back to "GMA." And I'm here with the bestselling author, former \uc2 NFL\uc2  player and Super Bowl champion, whose early life inspired the Oscar-winning movie, "The Blind Side." Now, Michael Oher has a new book out. It is called "When Your Back's Against the Wall." Michael, it's good to see you again.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Great to see you, as well. Thanks for having me back, pleasure.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I told you I read it cover to cover.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 I hope you liked it. Did you enjoy it? Awesome.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I did like it. What was there not to enjoy? I learned so much more about you because, you know, you're already a bestselling author with the first book. But this one is about legacy. You keep talking about that. Is that what's so important to you with this?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 It is. It's very important. And I took my time. I put a lot of hard work into it. And, you know, when I finished my \uc2 NFL\uc2  career, I just didn't feel comfortable with where I left off. And I felt that I had so much more to give to generations behind me. And, you know, finally to put some things in there to let people know a little bit more about my story and just the road that's been traveled has been tough for me for so long. And just to continue to overcome those obstacles and to be right here today, it's a journey that I enjoy, and it gives me the pleasure to continue to give back.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know because you work. You have worked from day one in your life. I mean, no one can take that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 I wouldn't wish it on anybody.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, but you, but you've done that. But you allude to, in the book, and what you were just talking about, the end of your \uc2 NFL\uc2  career. Didn't go out the way you wanted to because of the concussion. And you reached this really dark place. And here you've already gone through so much adversity. How was that time that you said was so challenging after football? How was that different from the adversity you had faced earlier in your life?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Well, all of my young adult life, teenage, I could control that every day. Here was something I couldn't control at all. And, you know, I built my foundation on just being positive and through every struggle, and I couldn't control that. And I had to start building good days on top of good days again. I really went back to the foundation and that hopeful attitude again, and, you know, it was able to help me get to a good point. And I think the most important thing is that I'm being vulnerable and telling myself that you need some help, and you can't do it alone any more, when I've been alone for all my life. So, having that tight circle and close family friends that helped me get through those tough times and still to this day, we're still working on it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's like a playbook. This is like a playbook for life. And you talk about positivity, and there's one you put, this is a quote that you say, be relentlessly positive, relentlessly positive. You know, that's tough for some folks.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 It is because you can't be positive 100 percent of the time, every single day. You need routine. You need consistency and discipline, too, and with that positivity, you, for me, you stack those hopeful days on top of hopeful days, and you look toward the future. And that's what really got me to where I am and knowing that one day, as long as, if I can get somewhat, 100 percent capacity thinking and physically, I can eventually get back to where I was.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Another difficult one, but one I agree with, patience, patience. And had you not been patient, you might not have found your wife, Tiffany, because you gave her, you slipped her your cell number when you all were in college, and it took her a while to call. You had to be patient.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Patience is everything. With patience, it brings greatness. But with that, I think, you know, it changed my life for the better, and it gave me something I didn't have as a kid. And that's a beautiful family with four kids, a wife. And what this book taught me with that is I'm still learning, I'm still growing, and with any, with every great thing, it takes time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and what I really appreciate throughout the book, you talk about your foundation because people say, "Oh, you're a miracle. You're a miracle." And you say, no, no, no. You don't want to be seen as a miracle. Explain to people what you mean by that and what you hope to achieve now with your foundation.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Well, I shouldn't be a miracle and no kid that's, I talk about socio-disadvantaged youth. We shouldn't be miracles, and we should have opportunities and resources to go out here and live a normal, young adult, child life, teenage, and go out and be successful. And with the foundation, what I'm doing is partnering with schools and placing success coordinators inside the schools, something I lacked as a young kid for a long time. I wish I had. You know, life would have been smoother mentally for me. So, what we're doing with that is giving kids an opportunity, not athletes...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 The first kids that's starting this fall are girls, and I believe in them more than anything to get the job done because, you know, I'm an athlete. I'm a big guy, football, you know, I can probably, you know, help take care of myself, but you give the ones who are overlooked a shot.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're a big guy? No, no, you're filling up that chair. You're filling up that chair.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Food and beverage won't let me be great, so I'm always chasing a diet.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, no, no. Hey, Michael Oher, thank you so much. Thank you for your transparency, thank you for your authenticity and really making a difference with your foundation, with your school, and making others know it shouldn't be deemed as a miracle, not a miracle.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you are, you are great. Michael's book, "When Your Back's Against the Wall."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL OHER ("WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL")\par \par \uc2 Awesome.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it is awesome. It is out now, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS HOW CRIMINALS ARE STAYING ONE STEP AHEAD\b0\par\par\uc2 1,000 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED BAHAMAS MURDER-FOR-HIRE PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA MOM ACCUSED OF CONSPIRING TO KILL HUSBAND SET TO BE RELEASED ON BAIL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NATIONAL MONUMENT, TRIBAL, MINING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN DECLARES NEW NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTECTING TRIBAL LAND NEAR GRAND CANYON FROM URANIUM MINING\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, STEIDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CRITICALLY INJURED IN SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 : WOMAN BITTEN ON LEG AT ROCKAWAY BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, OWEN, BOAT, DOCK\par \par \uc2 FRIEDKIN, BURSTYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING OSCAR WINNER WILLIAM FRIEDKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR BEHIND "THE FRENCH CONNECTION" & "THE EXORCIST" DIES AT AGE 87\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, BULLOCK, ALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANDRA BULLOCK'S HEARTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNER BRYAN RANDALL DIES AFTER PRIVATE THREE-YEAR BATTLE WITH ALS\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, HERRERA, ROHRBACH, \uc2 FEDEX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO DELIVERY DRIVER REUNITED WITH MAN HE SAVED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDEX WORKER PULLED MAN FROM WRECKAGE OF BURNING CAR\par \par \uc2 STORMS, EAST COAST, DEATH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE SUMMER STORMS TURN DEADLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED AS WEATHER SLAMS EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ZELLE, SCAM, BANK, APP, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We want to turn to our "GMA" cover story. It's really different than the story we just talked about, the new warning about a popular scam targeting people that use the popular cash app, Zelle, and the text messages that look like they're from your bank. Professor Erielle Reshef has the details. Good morning, Professor Reshef.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW CRIMINALS ARE STAYING ONE STEP AHEAD\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Professor of Scam U here, yes. These can be so realistic, and really anybody could fall for this scam. You've probably received a bank alert about a suspicious charge. Well, these scammers are one step ahead, urging customers to ignore those warnings, and their scheme is so convincing, one victim we spoke to says she lost more than $5,000.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a warning about an infamous scam once again targeting users of the \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  app, Zelle, costing them thousands.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL ADLER (SAYS SHE LOST $5\par \par \uc2 We looked at each other, and we were like, "This, this\u160\'00\'A0might be a scam."\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fraudsters call or send realistic-looking text messages that appear to be from \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , urging customers to ignore alerts about fraudulent charges or suspicious money transfers.\par \par \uc2 SANDHYA BROWN (FTC)\par \par \uc2 It's very pernicious what they do. Not only are they posing as your bank, they claim to be reaching out to protect you from fraud. And the fact that they're protecting you from fraud is a reason for you to trust them and follow their instructions.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That's what happened to Rachel Adler, who says she lost $5,500 after she received a text asking her if she'd made a $432 charge at a \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2  in Texas. When she replied no, she immediately received a call. She thought she was talking to a representative from \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL ADLER (SAYS SHE LOST $5\par \par \uc2 He sounded very kind. He was, seemed to be very educated, patient, caring, all of these things.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But turns out it was a scammer, the man telling her someone was using digital money transfer service Zelle to withdraw money from her account.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL ADLER (SAYS SHE LOST $5\par \par \uc2 "Did you make two Zelle transfers, one for $2,000 and one for $1,500?" And I said no.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then Adler says the man instructed her to wire money back to her account, but turns out all that money went straight to crooks.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL ADLER (SAYS SHE LOST $5\par \par \uc2 Then I noticed that at the top of the account, the $2,000 I had just Zelled to myself was now a debit.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It didn't stop there. The man warned her she'd get a text from \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  about a suspicious transfer but to disregard it. And sure enough, she did.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL ADLER (SAYS SHE LOST $5\par \par \uc2 Those were the things he was preemptively saying, "You're going to receive a text from the bank, and you don't have to pay attention to it because we're handing it on this phone call right now."\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  saying they prioritize client protection and will never ask a client to send money to themselves or anyone.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really important to keep that in mind. And experts tell us scammers rely heavily on urgency in these situations. So, if you receive an alert like this, call your bank through the number on the back of your debit or credit card and talk to a real bank representative. That way, it is easy to get looped into this. But just take a minute, call that legitimate number.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because it seems so legit.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Always double check. Thanks, E.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CELEBRATING THE WOMEN OF HIP HOP HONORING THE RISE & DOMINANCE OF WOMEN IN THE GENRE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,016 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED BAHAMAS MURDER-FOR-HIRE PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA MOM ACCUSED OF CONSPIRING TO KILL HUSBAND SET TO BE RELEASED ON BAIL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NATIONAL MONUMENT, TRIBAL, MINING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN DECLARES NEW NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTECTING TRIBAL LAND NEAR GRAND CANYON FROM URANIUM MINING\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, STEIDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CRITICALLY INJURED IN SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 : WOMAN BITTEN ON LEG AT ROCKAWAY BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, OWEN, BOAT, DOCK\par \par \uc2 FRIEDKIN, BURSTYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING OSCAR WINNER WILLIAM FRIEDKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR BEHIND "THE FRENCH CONNECTION" & "THE EXORCIST" DIES AT AGE 87\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, BULLOCK, ALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANDRA BULLOCK'S HEARTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNER BRYAN RANDALL DIES AFTER PRIVATE THREE-YEAR BATTLE WITH ALS\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, HERRERA, ROHRBACH, \uc2 FEDEX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO DELIVERY DRIVER REUNITED WITH MAN HE SAVED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDEX WORKER PULLED MAN FROM WRECKAGE OF BURNING CAR\par \par \uc2 STORMS, EAST COAST, DEATH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE SUMMER STORMS TURN DEADLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED AS WEATHER SLAMS EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ZELLE, SCAM, BANK, APP, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS\par \par \uc2 "POLTERGEIST GIRL", MURDER, DOCUMENTARY, BOYER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 ANDI, ROBOT, HEAT, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE DANGER OF EXCESSIVE HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USING TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STAY SAFE\par \par \uc2 NOTEBOOK, CREAM, JEWELRY, CARDS, DECANTER, PRETZEL\par \par \uc2 OHER, "WHEN YOUR BACK'S AGAINST THE WALL"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MICHAEL OHER LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 WOMEN, HIP-HOP, CELEBRATION, GLORILLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING THE WOMEN OF HIP HOP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HONORING THE RISE & DOMINANCE OF WOMEN IN GENRE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also this week, we are celebrating 50 year of hip-hop. This morning about the women at the top of hip-hop. Kelley Carter sat down with Grammy-nominated rapper, GloRilla. Good morning, Kelley.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. You know, women have been around in hip-hop since the dawn of the genre, but now we're in this incredible rap girl renaissance. And I sat down recently with hip-hop's next superstar, GloRilla. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From Latto and Cardi B to Megan Thee Stallion to Ice Spice, recently teaming up with rap legend Nikki Minaj, women are running hip-hop.\par \par \uc2 SPEEDY MORMAN ("360 WITH SPEEDY")\par \par \uc2 Women in hip-hop are really having a moment right now. To see women combat the idea there can only be one popular female rapper at a time.\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 I came in at a point in time where it was time for women to start dominating. I'm cheering every female rapper on. Keep going, keep doing it. We got this.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Unapologetic, authentic and confident, these rappers are trailblazing a path made possible by the lady emcees that came before them. GloRilla is...\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 GloRilla is that girl.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That girl. Okay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLORILLA TALKS THE WOMEN OF HIP HOP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAMMY NOMINEE ON HER BREAKOUT HIT & NEW MUSIC\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) GloRilla, one of hip-hop's newest talents, bursting onto the scene with her Grammy-nominated female anthem, "FNF."\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 You could say GloRilla but makes sure, Grammy-nominated.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why do you think this song resonated with fans the way that it has?\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 A lot of us, we go through the same stuff. And that's what I represent, really, because I've been in toxic situations, and it was just, you know, the feeling of being free, everybody likes the feeling of being free.\par \par \uc2 SPEEDY MORMAN ("360 WITH SPEEDY")\par \par \uc2 GloRilla being who she is but also, like, kind of embracing that tough exterior that she has, you know, like she has the rugged voice. Like, she has a presence about her, and she's never shied away from that.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Memphis native following that up with a second smash hit, a remix, "Tomorrow 2," featuring Cardi B.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who have been some of your favorites to work with so far?\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 My cousin, Cardi. (Inaudible) never going nowhere. "Tomorrow 2," that's my favorite feature of all time. I was like, "Oh my God, she just killed these..."\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Always gracing award show stages and festivals, GloRilla is currently preparing for her debut album.\par \par \uc2 GLORILLA (RAPPER)\par \par \uc2 I'm excited about it. I plan on going number one. I got to make another song that's going to have all the girls screaming and another anthem.\par \par \uc2 KELLEY L CARTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, GloRilla and I bonded over her love of her hometown which, of course, is Memphis, Tennessee. And that is why people love her so much, that authenticity. Can't wait to see what's next for her. Guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She got a big feature ahead of her. Thanks, Kelley.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She sure does. And coming up, Lori Bergamotto hits to the court for National Pickleball Day and reveals on the best gear, as well.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNDERSTANDING THE DANGER OF EXCESSIVE HEAT USING TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STAY SAFE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,034 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED BAHAMAS MURDER-FOR-HIRE PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA MOM ACCUSED OF CONSPIRING TO KILL HUSBAND SET TO BE RELEASED ON BAIL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NATIONAL MONUMENT, TRIBAL, MINING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN DECLARES NEW NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTECTING TRIBAL LAND NEAR GRAND CANYON FROM URANIUM MINING\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, STEIDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CRITICALLY INJURED IN SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 : WOMAN BITTEN ON LEG AT ROCKAWAY BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, OWEN, BOAT, DOCK\par \par \uc2 FRIEDKIN, BURSTYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING OSCAR WINNER WILLIAM FRIEDKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR BEHIND "THE FRENCH CONNECTION" & "THE EXORCIST" DIES AT AGE 87\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, BULLOCK, ALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANDRA BULLOCK'S HEARTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNER BRYAN RANDALL DIES AFTER PRIVATE THREE-YEAR BATTLE WITH ALS\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, HERRERA, ROHRBACH, \uc2 FEDEX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO DELIVERY DRIVER REUNITED WITH MAN HE SAVED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDEX WORKER PULLED MAN FROM WRECKAGE OF BURNING CAR\par \par \uc2 STORMS, EAST COAST, DEATH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE SUMMER STORMS TURN DEADLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED AS WEATHER SLAMS EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ZELLE, SCAM, BANK, APP, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS\par \par \uc2 "POLTERGEIST GIRL", MURDER, DOCUMENTARY, BOYER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 ANDI, ROBOT, HEAT, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE DANGER OF EXCESSIVE HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USING TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STAY SAFE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the dangerous heat. There are an average of about 700 heat-related deaths in the US each year, and Ginger is in Arizona taking a look at new technology to help us stay safe in this warming world. Good morning to you, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Morning to you, Robin. You know, Phoenix is not only one of the fastest growing but fastest warming cities in America. And they keep seeing their heat decks go up. That's why \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2  is utilizing this. It's called Andi. It's a thermal mannequin, first of its type, that can go outside, that can help stimulate different people, medication, all these different things so that we can know when humans go from uncomfortable to deadly.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Phoenix, Arizona, is still baking after having the hottest month ever for any US city on record. Heat is the number one weather killer, more than tornados, hurricanes and floods. And in Phoenix, it's especially deadly when they don't cool off at night.\par \par \uc2 ARIANE MIDDEL (ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 We have the buildings holding onto that sunlight. It creates this solar oven in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, here at \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2 , they are using this. It is called Andi. It is a mannequin/robot where they can simulate really any human and how they act around heat and how heat impacts them, especially the all-important threshold of what drives somebody to heat stroke.\par \par \uc2 ARIANE MIDDEL (ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 Andi stands for Advanced Newton Dynamic Instrument, and he's the first one to be able to go outdoors.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The researchers can even simulate different age, weight and skin colors to see how all demographics react to heat.\par \par \uc2 ARIANE MIDDEL (ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 Andi is like a human. Andi can breathe, sweat. He has a skin temperature, so when you touch him, his kind of, skin is warm. You can see how heavy he's sweating right now. So, if we were to put a human through this, you could see how much water they would be losing. Andi could have a different body mass index. Andi could have a different size. Andi could be overweight. Maybe Andi takes medication. So, Andi can mimic all these body types.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They also measure blood distribution and metabolic heat distribution. In future, they hope to detect which organs shut down first and how fast. We dressed Andi to test how different it would be running in a T-shirt versus shirtless.\par \par \uc2 ARIANE MIDDEL (ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 There is less, less sweat. So, that means it's essentially accumulating in his chest.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The takeaways here, shade is important, we know that, but they say if you put an umbrella over Andi or over yourself, you can take down the heat load of more than 30 degrees Fahrenheit, which can be the difference between life and death, especially with time, as it passes. Hydration is key, but there are some body core temperatures that rise so quickly or accumulate heat that you have to have the right type, with electrolytes and even salt. And finally, make sure you don't wick your sweat away. Some of that performance material we work out in takes the sweat away from our body. We need that sweat to evaporate and cool us.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then finally, we worked with the ICF, it's a climate group that simulates what it might look like by 2050 if we keep heating the way we are, with high-emission scenario. We would add 35-plus days of 110-plus, which would make this summer look a whole lot more like average, rather than an outlier.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's the big picture. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,062 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED BAHAMAS MURDER-FOR-HIRE PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA MOM ACCUSED OF CONSPIRING TO KILL HUSBAND SET TO BE RELEASED ON BAIL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, NATIONAL MONUMENT, TRIBAL, MINING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN DECLARES NEW NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTECTING TRIBAL LAND NEAR GRAND CANYON FROM URANIUM MINING\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, STEIDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CRITICALLY INJURED IN SHARK ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NYPD\uc2 : WOMAN BITTEN ON LEG AT ROCKAWAY BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BRAWL, OWEN, BOAT, DOCK\par \par \uc2 FRIEDKIN, BURSTYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING OSCAR WINNER WILLIAM FRIEDKIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIRECTOR BEHIND "THE FRENCH CONNECTION" & "THE EXORCIST" DIES AT AGE 87\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, BULLOCK, ALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANDRA BULLOCK'S HEARTBREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTNER BRYAN RANDALL DIES AFTER PRIVATE THREE-YEAR BATTLE WITH ALS\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, HERRERA, ROHRBACH, \uc2 FEDEX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO DELIVERY DRIVER REUNITED WITH MAN HE SAVED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDEX WORKER PULLED MAN FROM WRECKAGE OF BURNING CAR\par \par \uc2 STORMS, EAST COAST, DEATH, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE SUMMER STORMS TURN DEADLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED AS WEATHER SLAMS EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ZELLE, SCAM, BANK, APP, WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT SCAM TARGETING ZELLE USERS\par \par \uc2 "POLTERGEIST GIRL", MURDER, DOCUMENTARY, BOYER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the story of a mother who has spent three decades behind bars for killing her thee-year-old daughter. There are still questions about her conviction. Juju Chang here with the story. Good morning, Juju.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, George. You know, this decades-old murder mystery is back in the spotlight thanks to a devoted group of student sleuths. They're convinced it's a wrongful conviction that punished a (inaudible) because of her troubling and scandalous reputation. But now, there's new hope.\par \par \uc2 OPERATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 This is a free call from...\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINA BOYAR ("DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 Christina Boyar.\par \par \uc2 OPERATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 ...an incarcerated individual at Pulaski State Prison.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Christina Boyar has spent 30 years behind bars for the murder of her three-year-old daughter, Amber.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did you kill your daughter?\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINA BOYAR ("DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 No, ma'am, I did not. I did not kill my daughter.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For decades no one believed her, but now she has new supporters in her corner. They call themselves Team Christina.\par \par \uc2 OPERATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Grace, Lizzie and Sara are three amazing women. I love you.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These young women reinvestigated Christina's case for a class at Georgetown, convinced she was wrongfully convicted.\par \par \uc2 LIZZIE PORTERFIELD (RE-INVESTIGATED CHRISTINA'S CASE)\par \par \uc2 Christina wasn't there the day and the time that Amber received the injury that ultimately killed her.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In "Demons & Saviors," a new Hulu series, Team Tina looks at details of the case that seem stranger than fiction.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOTHER CONVICTED OF KILLING 3-YEAR-OLD DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SERIES EXPLORES DECADES-OLD MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINA BOYAR ("DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 When I was a 14-year-old kid, things started happening in my home.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A series of bizarre events, the alarm clock, the TV going haywire.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINA BOYAR ("DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 The lights turned on and off. There goes the glasses flying across the room.\par \par \uc2 CONTRIBUTOR (DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 The home of Tina Resch and her adopted family has become, for them, a house of horrors.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She was a media sensation, until she wasn't, caught on camera knocking over a lamp herself. Christina ran away. She says the only good thing that happened was the birth of her daughter, Amber. But then, in April 1992, Christina found herself in the spotlight once again, arrested along with her new boyfriend, David.\par \par \uc2 CONTRIBUTOR (DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 She's being charged with murder and cruelty to her daughter. Mrs. Boyar did tell Channel 2 news exclusively...\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINA BOYAR ("DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 I didn't murder my daughter.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Facing the death penalty at just 22 years old, Christina plead guilty. The students say Christina's troubled past was used against her.\par \par \uc2 LIZZIE PORTERFIELD (RE-INVESTIGATED CHRISTINA'S CASE)\par \par \uc2 The prosecution took what happened with Christina as an eighth grader and said, "Well, she's really manipulative, and if she can do that, then she can do murder, and she can kill her child."\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the prosecutor in the case says the students have it all wrong.\par \par \uc2 CONTRIBUTOR (DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 The case was strong against Christina Boyar, very strong. Whether or not a bunch of students in \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2  think it's unfair, that doesn't faze me at all.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I think the subtext is that you guys are na\u239\'00\'EFve, that you've been manipulated.\par \par \uc2 CONTRIBUTOR (DEMONS & SAVIORS")\par \par \uc2 Give her an Oscar. She's maintained the same story for 32 years.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now the students argue if we're being manipulated, show us how. They traveled repeatedly to Georgia, even presenting new evidence to the current prosecutor, asking him to reopen Christina's case. Now, "Demons & Saviors" is a collaboration, a new docuseries from ABC News Studios and Latchkey Films, and it's streaming now on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 . Guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to see those students going at it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's fascinating, Juju. Thank you for bringing that to us.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TE