DOCUMENTARY, BOYER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW QUESTIONS IN "POLTERGEIST GIRL" MURDER CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTINA BOYER CLAIMS SHE DIDN'T KILL DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 ANDI, ROBOT, HEAT, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDERSTANDING THE DANGER OF EXCESSIVE HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USING TECHNOLOGY TO HELP STAY SAFE\par \par \uc2 NOTEBOOK, CREAM, JEWELRY, CARDS, DECANTER, PRETZEL\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej880000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, ASSASSINATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE ON RESIDENTIAL AREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST EIGHT KILLED, DOZENS INJURED IN RUSSIAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CHALLENGES EVIDENCE LIMITS IN ELECTION CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM SEEKS NARROWER PROTECTIVE ORDER\par \par \uc2 OHIO, ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSAL COULD IMPACT ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, George, now to Ohio, where voters are facing a decision that could determine the fate of abortion rights in that state and have political impact heading into the 2024 presidential election. Stephanie Ramos is tracking that for us. Good morning, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. In November, voters in Ohio will decide whether to pass a constitutional amendment to protect the right to an abortion.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, though, voters decide on a question known as issue one, which could have a major impact on whether the right to an abortion becomes part of the state Constitution later this fall. Today's question on the ballot is to raise the standards to pass a constitutional amendment. Ohio is the only state with abortion access on the ballot this year. The measure is largely seen as an abortion fight. If the threshold is raised, it would make amendments set to appear on the November ballot that would make abortion protections into the Constitution more difficult to pass.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And early voter turnout in Ohio has surged for today's special election with more than 578,000 people voting by mail or in person since early voting began June 23rd. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) High-stakes. Okay, Stephanie Ramos, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej8800008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HUGE TURNOUT FOR HIGH-STAKES ELECTION ABORTION RIGHTS AT STAKE IN OHIO CONSTITUTION VOTE\b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GINGHER, HEAT, TRACK, TRAVEL, STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, BANCULLI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHARK ATTACK OFF NYC BEACH\par \par \uc2 ASSAULT, ALBERT, OWEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ASSAULT CHARGES IN DOCK BRAWL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: GEORGIA DA READY TO PRESENT\par \par \uc2 OHIO, JACOBSON, SPECIAL ELECTION, ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUGE TURNOUT FOR HIGH-STAKES ELECTION\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the huge turnout in Ohio for a special election and abortion rights could be at stake. On the ballot, a measure to make it harder to amend the state's Constitution. That measure rushed before voters ahead of a November ballot to change the Constitution to protect the right to an abortion. ABC's Alex Presha is in Columbus.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS AT STAKE IN OHIO CONSTITUTION VOTE\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a massive turnout at the polls in Ohio for a special election that could determine the fate of abortion rights in the state.\par \par \uc2 VOTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The Constitution is under attack, and we want to protect the constitution in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the ballot, a Republican-led measure that would make it harder to change the state's Constitution come November when voters consider an amendment to protect abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TO CHANGE OHIO CONSTITUTION\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Right now, a simple majority is needed to change the Constitution. But if the proposal, called issue 1, passes, any change would need a 60% supermajority.\par \par \uc2 VOTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It was important to protect my rights, especially as a woman and, you know, the abortion protection. So, I wanted to vote no today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO SPECIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before polls even opened, nearly 700,000 early voters had cast their ballots in what's being seen as the latest referendum on abortion since the Supreme Court overturned Roe vs. Wade. Ohio's ban on abortion after six weeks has been put on hold by a judge.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) has got to go.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For months, both sides have held rallies, door knocked, and spent millions on ads to get voters to the polls.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM CAMPAIGN AD\par \par \uc2 POLITICAL AD VOICEOVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Vote yes on Tuesday, August 8th, to protect parents' rights, unborn children, and the Ohio Constitution.\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 This is our decision. Not yours. Get out of our bedroom.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I won the last election. I'm not going anywhere.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What happens here in Ohio, Mary, could be a sign as to how abortion plays in the 2024 election. There are several conservative states that are expected to have similar abortion rights amendments on their ballots. Mary?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The whole country keeping a close eye on this tonight. Alex, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY WORKERS STAGE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Los Angeles today, thousands of city workers walking off the job, striking for 24 hours, marching at city hall and at the airport, saying wages aren't keeping up with the city's high cost of living.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hotel workers have also staged intermittent walkouts and, of course, the actors and writers are still on strike. Mayor Karen Bass pledging the city will not shut down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REINSTATES LIMITS ON 'GHOST GUNS'\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Supreme Court today temporarily allowing the Biden administration to enforce regulations aimed at stopping the spread of so-called ghost guns, firearms made with at home kits that do not have serial numbers.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The court voting 5 to 4 to put on hold a decision by a Texas judge striking down the regulations, while the Biden administration appeals that decision possibly all the way to the Supreme Court. Ghost guns are showing up at more and more crime scenes, and they are nearly impossible to trace.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEAR GRAND CANYON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN CREATING NATIONAL MONUMENT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And President Biden has designated nearly a million acres around the Grand Canyon as the nation's newest historic monument.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The designation will protect lands important to several native tribes and ban new uranium mines.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Today, marks an historic step in preserving the majesty of this place. First among American landmarks, sacred to tribal nations, revered by every American. It speaks to the soul of our nation.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President is visiting three western states, promoting his work to create jobs and protect the climate.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And when we come back, news tonight about the wife charged in an alleged murder-for-hire plot in the Bahamas. Why today's bail hearing did not go as banned. And breaking late today, rapper Tory Lanez sentenced for shoot Megan Thee Stallion, her message to the judge.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230810ej8800006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM'S NEW PASSION PROJECT MAJOR NEW INITIATIVE AIMED AT ERADICATING HOMELESSNESS IN THE UK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,175 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES, DAMAGE, KILLED, FUNKHOUSER\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, MUTINY, PRIGOZHIN, PUTIN, REVOLT, BLINKEN, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RUSSIA, ZELENSKYY, PRIGOZHIN, PUTIN\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, MUTINY, PRIGOZHIN, MERCENARIES, POWER\par \par \uc2 DERAILMENT, CLEANUP, RIVER, SULFUR, ASPHALT, WATER\par \par \uc2 POLICE, MURDER, CHARGES, PEREZ, MCMANUS, PACKARD\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, ALERT, 5G, RADIO ALTIMETER, DELAYS, CANCELLATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM CENTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PRIGOZHIN, MERCENARIES, PUTIN, REVOLT, REMNICK, FARKAS\par \par \uc2 SUB, DISASTER, DAWWOOD, DEBRIS, COAST GUARD, TITAN, STANLEY\par \par \uc2 SEMAGLUTIDE, PILL, RYBELSUS, STUDY, WEIGHT LOSS\par \par \uc2 BET AWARDS, HIP HOP, LABELLE, TURNER, WINNERS\par \par \uc2 PARTON, LOOKALIKES, IRELAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 PRIGOZHIN, MUTINY, RUSSIA, \uc2 WAGNER GROUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURMOIL IN RUSSIA AFTER ATTEMPTED MUTINY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUTIN'S GRIP ON POWER QUESTIONED IN WAKE OF MERCENARIES REVOLT\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, HOMEWARD, FERGUSON, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE WILLIAM'S NEW PASSION PROJECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR NEW INITIATIVE AIMED AT ERADICATING HOMELESSNESS IN THE UK\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to Prince William's new passion project, ending homelessness in the UK, a cause important to both him and his late mother. Lama Hasan is in Kensington Palace in London with the latest. Good morning, Lama.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, good morning to you, Linsey. And what a big morning it is for Prince William as he kicks off his massive five-year project to help the homeless. The Prince says this is an issue he wants to focus on and it's an issue he wants to fight for.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Prince William launching a major new initiative. Homeward is a five-year plan to prove that it is possible eradicate homelessness in the UK.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAM (PRINCE OF WALES)\par \par \uc2 Over the next five years, we have a unique opportunity to develop innovative new solutions and scale the tangible impact. This will inspire belief throughout the UK and beyond that homelessness can be ended for good.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Prince has pinpointed six locations for this initiative, which he says will bring together experts, key players and donors and, through collaboration, get people especially the young off the streets.\par \par \uc2 VICTORIA MURPHY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Prince William would have been aware that he was likely to be criticize for the optics of raising this. He's a land owner, a landlord, he keeps multiple properties. But I think he's prepared to accept that because he really wants to use his profile to bring this issue to light.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE WILLIAM TAKES ON HOMELESSNESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAUSE CHAMPIONED BY HIS LATE MOTHER PRINCESS DIANA\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Homelessness is one of the most important causes to William. At the age of 27, the Prince even spent a night on the streets to highlight the plight of the homeless. And for his 40th birthday, he took to the streets selling a magazine that supports them.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM CAMPAIGN AD\par \par \uc2 WILLIAM (PRINCE OF WALES)\par \par \uc2 I've done everything I can to kind of raise the profile of homelessness, and I want to do a lot more and a lot more needs to be done.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Prince's commitment to this cause instilled in him by his late mother, Princess Diana, who herself championed it.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, this is a cause that's so close to his heart. Prince William even has plans to build social housing on land owned by the Duchy of Cornwall that's the spoiling estate that he got from his father when he became second in line to the throne which, of course, would be significant. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SARAH FERGUSON REVEALS BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUCHESS OF YORK RECUPERATING AFTER UNDERGOING SURGERY\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Lama, switching gears here for a moment. Sarah Ferguson, the Duchess of York, has shared that she was recently diagnosed with breast cancer. What's the latest on her condition?\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Linsey, we know that the Duchess of York is back at home in Windsor recovering from her operation. And according to her spokesperson, she is surrounded by her family. Now, speaking candidly in her podcast, the duchess revealing that she had a single mastectomy after being diagnosed with an early form of breast cancer during a routine mammogram screening recently. She was otherwise symptom free. The 63-year-old is receiving medical treatments. The doctors have told her that the prognosis is good after having her surgery, which they say is successful. The doctors saying that that her experience underlines the importance of regular screening and is now urging people to get checked and to get screened. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, those screening so important and life-saving often. Lama, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:13, GROUNDBREAKING NEW STUDIES\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," three ground breaking studies on diabetes, obesity and the new drugs to treat them including one that's a pill, not an injection. Dr. Ashton is here to talk about it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21, THE RIGHT STUFF: BEST CAMPING GEAR\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also, this morning, Lori Bergamotto is here with the right stuff with everything you need for a camping trip this summer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:40, PATTI LABELLE & DULE LIVE LIVE!\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, Patti Labelle fresh off her performance last night at the BET Awards joins us live with Dule Hill to talk about "The Wonder Years." And Lara is in Houston for "Rise and Shine. Lara, good morning once again.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30, BREAKFAST BATTLE IN HOUSTON!\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit, good morning. So, we've got Marcus from The Breakfast Klub going head-to-head against JC and Sarah from Dandelion for the best chicken and waffles in all of Houston. We're also going to talk to some incredible female entrepreneurs. That will explain why I'm wearing roller states. And Toro, he's here to make sure I don't fall down. That's all coming up on "Good Morning America" live from Houston Texas. Don't go anywhere. We're going eat real well this morning.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA." A beautiful shot of Times Square here in New York City.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOW ME THE MONEY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And coming up this week, we are helping you find unclaimed money and surprising some people who didn't know they had thousands of dollars that belonged to them. It's going to be a good week.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, a little more sophisticated than the change in the couch.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, we're going to step a knot from there. All right, you can check it out this week starting on Wednesday. For now, let's get it over to Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right, thanks, Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230717ej6q0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION CLASH NORTH CAROLINA'S NEW BILL\b0\par\par\uc2 1,790 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, AUDIO, DOCUMENTS, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, GOP, FLYNN, WHITE, GRAY, GRAUNKE, STEIN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Aaron. Turning now to praise and protests one year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade. The issue now front and center in North Carolina with new and tougher restrictions just days away. And the battle over reproductive rights already looming large over the 2024 race for the White House. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 KELLY FLYNN (PRESIDENT & CEO A WOMAN'S CHOICE)\par \par \uc2 We're planning the doomsday scenario. What do we do? How do we serve our patients?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For the past year, North Carolina has been a safe haven for people seeking abortions in the south. That's about to change.\par \par \uc2 KELLY FLYNN (PRESIDENT & CEO A WOMAN'S CHOICE)\par \par \uc2 A lot of patients are calling because they're confused. Is abortion still legal? Can I even come in? I have no idea what's going on, because it seems like the laws are changing almost on a weekly basis.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On July 1st, the state will become the next to decrease abortion access, dropping from 20 weeks to 12.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 If abortion is outlawed, it means that I even as a resident physician wouldn't have access to training for those procedures.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At this point are you leaning toward possibly moving out of the state?\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's become a race against time for people like Kelly Flynn, who oversees three abortion clinics in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 KELLY FLYNN (PRESIDENT & CEO A WOMAN'S CHOICE)\par \par \uc2 It's been very, very stressful. It's also been very scary. It's taken a toll on everyone emotionally and mentally. We work a lot of hours. And, again, it's constant change that everybody has to be compliant with.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade a year ago with the Dobbs ruling.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Rise up for abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion access in America has shifted dramatically.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I honestly cried tears of joy.\par \par \uc2 NEWSCASTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 As soon as this opinion comes down, abortion is outlawed in many states in this country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2021, Texas had the most restricted ban, after six weeks. Now 15 states have stopped performing nearly all abortions. The ending of Roe quickly caused a massive increase in abortions in states with more permissive laws. The biggest jump between April and August of 2022 was North Carolina, where 37% more abortions were performed.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In some states, the rules around restrictions are murky, tying the hands of worried medical providers, fearing lawsuits or even possible jail time, and putting some women's lives at risk. The clinics Kelly oversees, had been overwhelmed with patients from states like Texas, Georgia and Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 KELLY FLYNN (PRESIDENT & CEO A WOMAN'S CHOICE)\par \par \uc2 There was a couple that came in from Florida. They were past the 15-week mark, so they couldn't be seen in Florida, and they had a fatal abnormality and knew that her pregnancy wouldn't survive.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At least 300 bills to restrict access to abortion have been introduced across the country since the start of the year, including North Carolina's pending care for woman/children and families act.\par \par \uc2 JOYCE KRAWIEC (REP) (STATE SEN NORTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 We have the opportunity to save many lives. We have the opportunity to provide women and families options that they haven't had before, to show them that children are not burdens, they are the greatest joy of your life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new law bans nearly all abortions after 12 weeks, and unless it's an emergency, the law requires a consultation at least 72 hours before a surgical abortion to discuss potential risks and other options. It does include exceptions through 20 weeks in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Through the 24th week if there are life limiting fetal anomalies. And places no restrictions if the mother's life is at risk. But it would prohibit these later abortions from being performed in any facility other than a hospital.\par \par \uc2 KRISTI GRAUNKE\uc2  (LEGAL DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  OF NORTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 Can you imagine having to wait 72 hours. You're in pain. You're maybe at risk of losing your life if you don't get this care. Just the profound impact that that will have, particularly on victims who live in rural areas.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But authors of the bill point to nearly 160 million in funding for things like foster care, child care access, maternal health care, and other programs aimed at helping pregnant mothers.\par \par \uc2 LISA S. BARNES (REP) (STATE SEN NORTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 This proposal focuses on the health and safety of women and children. We know that oftentimes women feel like they don't have options when they're faced with an unplanned pregnancy. But we want them to know that they do have options.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democratic Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  vetoed that bill in May, but the Republican majority in the state's general assembly overrode his veto.\par \par \uc2 NORTH CAROLINA HOUSE MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The House has overridden the Governor's veto and the bill becomes law, notwithstanding the Governor's objections. So be notified.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ripple effects are already visible in states that passed bans after the fall of Roe last year.\par \par \uc2 NEWSCASTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The new KFF survey shows a majority of OB/GYNs believe the overturning of Roe V. Wade is linked to an increase in maternal deaths.\par \par \uc2 NEWSCASTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Many obstetricians are leaving the area out of fear of breaking the law, which is also making it harder to recruit.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 Association of American Medical Colleges\uc2 , also saw a 10% drop in applications for residency in states that ban abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How do you feel than? This is a state that you call home, a state that you love.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 It's tough. I thought that I was going to have the choice of whether or not I wanted to move and continue my training. And now it looks like I nearly have to make that decision. It's almost forced my hand.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Callie White is one of those residents. She's studying to be an OB/GYN and practicing as a doula, but now is considering a move out of state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is it a difficult decision for you to make?\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 Yes. I don't think that I can in good conscience continue my training if it doesn't involve abortion care, just for the safety of my future patients.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Even as the North Carolina law is just a few days away from going into effect, opponents are trying to halt its progress. A lawsuit filed by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and North Carolina Dr. Beverly Gray, claims the bill's requirements for abortion care are unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 DR. BEVERLY GRAY (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 Litigation is the next step to say hey, we're going shine a lot on some things that are unclear about this bill.\par \par \uc2 KRISTI GRAUNKE\uc2  (LEGAL DIRECTOR \uc2 ACLU\uc2  OF NORTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 It fails to provide clear notice of what you can or can't do. That becomes a constitutional concern. It becomes a due process concern. And so we'll be asking the court for relief on the basis that as written now, the statute is so unclear that providers can't determine and patients can't determine what it's safe to do or not.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Something the attorney general of state, \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , agrees with.\par \par \uc2 JOSH STEIN\uc2  (DEM) (NORTH CAROLINA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 There are many provisions in it that inherently contradict other provisions. In one instance it says medication abortion is valid until 12 weeks. Another time it says 10 weeks. It is an incredibly sloppily drafted legislation.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Attorney General Stein is listed as one of the defendants in the lawsuit because it's his job to defend state laws in court.\par \par \uc2 JOSH STEIN\uc2  (DEM) (NORTH CAROLINA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 The law is clearly unconstitutional in my view, and because of that, I can't defend it. The law imposes unreasonable and unnecessary burdens on women and providers.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While the lawsuit runs its course, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is asking a federal judge to issue a temporary restraining order blocking the law. As these cases play out around the country, politicians continue to beat the drum on abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 FMR VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The cause of life is the calling of our time, and we must not rest and must not relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law in every state in this country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in North Carolina, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  giving a speech at her own event, marking the one-year anniversary of Roe's fall.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We, all of us, are now called upon to advance the promise of freedom. Including the freedom of every woman to make decisions about her own body, not the government telling her what to do.\par \par \uc2 PEDESTRIAN (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You know, even though I'm personally against abortion, I think that a woman has a right to choose.\par \par \uc2 PEDESTRIAN (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I feel like we as women have the rights and the brains to make decisions for our bodies, and we should be trusted to make those decisions with our health care providers.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 That's what this country is about, it's freedom, the pursuit of happiness, going back all the way to our constitution.\par \par \uc2 DR. BEVERLY GRAY (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 I think every single patient that I care for is unique, and the set of circumstances that they bring when they see me are unique. It's impossible to truly and thoughtfully legislate health care in that way.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDY'S RETURN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel. Coming up, Indy's return. Superstar Harrison Ford returns for a final appearance as "Indiana Jones." Why he's saying goodbye to the legendary role.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230628ej6q00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NIGHTLINE\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 This is "Nightline."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news. ABC News has obtain an audio recording of former President Trump appearing to acknowledge that he held on to a sensitive military document after leaving the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION CLASH\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, abortion clash.\par \par \uc2 KELLY FLYNN (PRESIDENT & CEO A WOMAN'S CHOICE)\par \par \uc2 We're planning the doomsday scenario. What do we do? How do we serve our patients?\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 North Carolina, once a safe haven for women.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Just days away from banning most abortions after 12 weeks.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE WHITE (MEDICAL STUDENT WAKE FOREST UNIVERSITY)\par \par \uc2 I don't think that I can in good conscience continue my training if it doesn't involve abortion care.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A year after the Supreme Court struck down Roe V. Wade, the issue still taking center stage across the country.\par \par \uc2 FMR VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The cause of life is the calling of our time.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The freedom of every woman to make decisions about her own body.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDY'S RETURN\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Indy's return.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Indy.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Give them hell, Indiana Jones.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The beloved fedora wearing adventurer back for one final crack of the whip in "The Dial of Destiny."\par \par \uc2 ASHAN SINGH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 At any point were you like, I'm too old for this?\par \par \uc2 HARRISON FORD (ACTOR "INDIANA JONES AND THE DIAL OF DESTINY")\par \par \uc2 Only in the morning when you first get up and you sound a little creaky.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So after more than four decades of playing "Indiana Jones," is Harrison Ford ready to retire?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "Nightline" will be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230628ej6q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CANDIDATES SPAR OVER ABORTION RIGHTS FIRST ANNIVERSARY OF RULING ALLOWING STATES TO BAN ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, PRIGOZHIN, MUTINY, FARKAS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR, MUTINY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE: MONITORING SITUATION IN REAL-TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN MET WITH TOP ADVISORS, SPOKE WITH ALLIES\par \par \uc2 MUTINY, RUSSIA UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 WAGNER GROUP\uc2  LEADER END ATTEMPTED MUTINY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETREAT ORDERED 150 MILES FROM CITY, NO CHARGES FOR LEADER O GROUP\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 PENCE, HARRIS, TRUMP, ABORTION, ELECTION, BOWERS, HALEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES SPAR OVER ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST ANNIVERSARY OF RULING ALLOWING STATES TO BAN ABORTION\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To politics now and to the presidential campaign as Republicans and Democrats use the divisive issue of abortion rights to rouse their followers.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President Harris, as you see here, as well as Republican candidates delivering speeches on the anniversary of the Supreme Court ruling that allows states to ban abortion. ABC's Em Nguyen has more.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, one year after the fall of Roe vs. Wade, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the Faith & Freedom Coalition in Washington, celebrating the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I got it done and nobody thought it was even a possibility.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The issue taking center stage on the 2024 campaign trail. His former vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , also rallying, pressuring his rivals for the Republican presidential nomination to support a 15-week federal abortion ban at minimum.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We will never rest and never relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley telling voters there is a place for federal law on abortion, an about-face from last month when she said that goal was unrealistic.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Let's make sure no state laws say that if a woman has an abortion, she's not going to go to jail and we're not going to give her the death penalty.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the issue of abortion had galvanized Democratic voters in 2022 and some abortion rights advocates think it will again.\par \par \uc2 MILLIE BOWERS (PRO-ABORTION RIGHTS)\par \par \uc2 There are a lot of women within this country. We are silent, but we're powerful.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEAR OR TOTAL ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, 15 states have enacted laws for near total or total abortion ban. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in North Carolina admonishing the spate of laws restricting abortion.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 How dare they attack basic health care?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAY 2023 ABC NEWS POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 78% OF AMERICANS SAY THE DECISION TO HAVE AN ABORTION SHOULD BE LEFT TO A WOMAN AND HER DOCTOR\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the most recent poll by ABC News, 78% of Americans say the decision whether to have an abortion should be left to a woman and her doctor, including 58% of Republicans.\par \par \uc2 VOTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And it should be what everyone's focused on.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And some protesters tell me, if a presidential candidate's views on abortion don't align with theirs, it's a deal breaker, underscoring just how much this issue is again dominating the campaign season. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Em Nguyen, our thanks to you this morning. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230711ej6p0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,269 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, WAR, UK, RU, PRIGOZHIN, REVOLT, PUTIN, ZELENSKYY, WAGNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIAN REVOLT\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, WAR, 2024, SPEECH, TRUMP, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 2024, HARRIS, CHRISTIE, TRUMP, DESANTIS, BAIER, ABORTION, PENCE\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (FMR UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Thanks to the Supreme Court decision of exactly one year ago, we gave those who have long been fighting for pro-life cause negotiating power. For the first time ever, you have tremendous negotiating power. Now, with Roe v. Wade, you had none.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 How dare they attack our fundamental rights. The \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  must pass legislation to restore the protections of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, the debate over abortion is as hot as it has ever been. Let's talk about all and this week's politics with our Roundtable, former DNC Chair, Donna Brazile, former RNC Chair and Trump White House Chief of Staff Reince Priebus, "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " congressional - reporter Marianna Sotomayor, and NBR, NPR White House correspondent Asma Khalid.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Reince, let me start with you and what we heard from Christie.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 Sure.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, a blunt takedown of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Is Trump ever gonna actually get on a debate stage with that guy?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAKING STOCK OF THE 2024 PRESIDENTIAL RACE\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 Well, I will tell you, those are the kinds of interviews that will entice President Trump to get on the debate stage, and Governor Christie knows it.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 And that's what he wants, and I think it'll happen. And I think, you know, we're, we're in the world of middle finger politics in America, the world of Wrestlemania politics, the world where, you know, attention - is what everyone is seeking in order to get support, in order to get those 40,000 donors, in order to get votes in these states. But I'll tell what you the campaigns are talking to me about. There are two things.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 One, qualifying for the debate stage, which is what everyone's trying to do. Governor Christie's found a lane and he's doing well in that lane of qualifying for the debate stage. But then, there's the second thing, which is, how do I understand how delegates are awarded in this party because delegates choose the nominees. And if you look at understanding the delegate rules, which is what all these candidates are doing, that's why they're focusing on Iowa, New Hampshire, South Carolina, but then there is a national play here because then comes 17 states on a winner take all.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 And that's why when you look at the polling today, Trump is still ahead by 30 national, at least 20 in those early states. Those state rules and those candidates are watching that very closely today.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Donna?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First of all, the twice impeached, twice indicted former president of the United States do not need a debate stage. Let's clear the, the air out of the balloon. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, usually when you're 40 points up or 30 points up you don't debate.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, you, why, would you debate? And look, I'm now taking a position that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken, which is, why would I give these other cats, I'm not calling them dogs because, of course, I have a dog and I know none of my, my dog would not want to be compared to them. But why would you give these cats an opportunity to take you down or to hit you when you're that high in the polls?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I see no reason why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should agree to debate because he has the lane to himself. This is his nomination to lose. And the only thing he will do by debating is to elevate the people who are now in the, quote, unquote, "in the hole."\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 Right. But you're assuming, you know, you're, you're, you're - talking as a political strategist. I understand that. But from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's viewpoint, number one, he looks back at 2016 and he says, number one, I won all those debates.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 Number one. And, number two, I'm, I'm gonna keep winning and I'm gonna take these guys down.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I mean, on one...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 That's how he sees it.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, on one hand, of course he loves the spotlight. But he also does hold back when the fight is right to him. He's - much better attacking people from afar than, than...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...than taking the fight directly to somebody. What, what, what's the expert - I mean, you heard Christie make the case that, that, that he's gained traction with this, Marianna? Do you, do you think that, do you think he really can?\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 He said he gained traction in New Hampshire. That's just...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 ...one state of many...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 Especially when you're pointing out just all of those states that come after those early states.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 I mean, are there people, he made the argument for character, and there definitely are voters, especially that we heard around the midterm saying, listen, I, I am a Republican. At the end of the day, if it comes to voting for Trump, okay. But the biggest thing that they always point out is character, that he's unreliable. You just don't know what he's gonna say or do next. If they could change something about Trump, that would be it. But we just, we, we know and we've seen that that's just not necessarily something that's gonna completely tank his chances.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL HURD JOINS CHRISTIE, HUTCHINSON AS 'ANTI-TRUMP' CANDIDATES\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 I also think that the more crowded this field becomes, it really does advantage \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We saw during the 2016 election, and it seems like almost exactly the same playbook now, you've got what, a dozen Republicans who are in the field. That just chips away, I mean, if they each get a percent or two, maybe, right? I mean, that benefits \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But I think we're gonna talk more about this, I'm sure, abortion. But over the weekend, there was the Faith and Freedom Coalition Conference. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was welcomed like the hero for having given the court...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "We want Trump. We want Trump."\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 Right? I mean, and so, then you have this large constituency, a key constituency of the Republican Party, that is more loyal today to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than it was, I would think, even four years ago.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the other candidates are tied up in knots with how to deal with him. I wanna play a, a bit of sound. This is what, this is what \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said when he was asked if he would commit to supporting Trump, if Trump were the nominee.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Regardless of his attacks, will you a - a 100 percent pledge to support Trump as the GOP nominee?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP-FLA) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 So, what I would say is this. When you are saying that Cuomo did better on COVID than Florida did...\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Really.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP-FLA) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 ...you are revealing yourself to just be full of it.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I mean, that's wild, because not only did he not say yes that he would support the nominee if it were Trump, regardless, is, he goes on to, and, and it went on and on and on to attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I mean, is that gonna work? It's not as blunt or as maybe effective as \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , but you know. And ultimately, he says, of course he's gonna support whoever can beat Biden.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 Right. I mean, it's this, all of these candidates are trying to find a way where they can attack Trump without naming him. That's something that we saw over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 And it's a very difficult line for them to play. Because again, they know that this is Trump's base, that Trump does animate them, that his policies are something that a lot of these voters rely on. So, going after him could be pretty difficult for all of these candidates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP REMAINS EARLY FRONTRUNNER IN REPUBLICAN PRIMARY\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And, and the policies, you hear this line often, I, I support Trump's policies, from Republicans, but I just don't like the drama, those that are critical. But I wanna play this from, from Bret Baier's interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on, on the question of criminal justice reform.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP: MONDAY\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But she'd be killed under your plan.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (FMR UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Huh?\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 As a drug dealer.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (FMR UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 No, no, no. Under my, oh, under that? It would depend on the severity. It would depend on the severity.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But here you wrote this ad (inaudible), and she's technically a former drug dealer. She - she had multimillion-dollar cocaine ring...\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (FMR UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Any drug dealer look, she...\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, even Alice Johnson in that ad?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (FMR UNITED STATES PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 No. And starting now, yeah. But she wouldn't have done it if it was death penalty.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I mean, so he's talking about Alice Johnson, who he pardoned and bragged about in a Super Bowl ad, and now, well, maybe she'd be executed. I mean, is there really a coherent Trump policy?\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 I don't know that it matters whether it is a coherent Trump policy because I - I would say there's a constituency within the Republican Party that doesn't like the drama. But there's a constituency, and I've met them. I'm sure we all have gone out and talked to voters like this...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 ...who really like the bravado, who like the style and the character. And so, when you've got a dozen Republicans running, I would say enough will likely like the style. And I don't know how much the policies really matter.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. I...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He sounded like a human pretzel because he couldn't get his words right. He couldn't put it together in his big mind of his, the genius that we never saw. But he didn't know what he was talking about. Let me tell you something. If I was Trump lawyer or counsel, I would've said, "Baby, you don't need to do those shows."\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, they've been saying that for a long time.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, they're not - he's not listening.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAP, ABORTION ACCESS RESTRICTED POST-DOBBS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. So, so I wanna get, we had the one-year anniversary of Dobbs, and, and we've seen a dramatic impact in the United States when it comes to an abortion policy. Take a look at the, the map of the US. We now have effectively illegal abortion in, in 14 states. We have, you know, we, and Florida's not even on there in this, regard, in terms of states that will have a six-week abortion ban 'cause Florida's ban is not in effect yet. But this is a dramatic change in abortion policy in this country, just a year after this decision.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 538: SUPPORT FOR ABORTION RIGHTS RISING AFTER DOBBS\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Three hundred, can you imagine? It's been a total mess, I think, in, in giving this issue to the state. First of all, we should trust women, and women of faith, to make this decision with their family. But to lose access, especially women in several of those states that you just put up, they are afraid to go to the emergency room even when they are sick because they're afraid that they will be turned away, and they have been turned away. And women in certain states have to drive several days just to get to the next available clinic.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS GRAPPLE WITH ABORTION DEBATE AHEAD OF 2024\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is a decision that should be made between women and their doctors and their families. And the politics that I've been hearing especially after watching the Faith and Freedom Conference, I said, I need, I need an exorcism now because I heard so many lies, so many lies about women and, and how women make this decision. This is why President Biden has recommitted himself to fighting for women's access to have the full range of reproductive health care. This is why the Vice President, who's a great vice president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , has said, you know, that she will also fight for women's access and including access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, Asma, on the politics of this, the country's divided on abortion. But the extreme positions on either side, including what, where we see Republicans going, is, is not a majority position in the country.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 That's right. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, how worried are Republicans about how this will play out? It hurt them in 2022. It seemed to.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I mean, I think there seems to be some disagreement amongst Republicans about how popular of a position this is, right? We saw \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  over the weekend calling for a nationwide abortion ban and encouraging his fellow Republican, 2024 contenders, to join him in having a 15-week abortion ban. Look, I think the politics have just fundamentally shifted.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 When Roe was the law of the land, it was far easier for Republicans to point at that and say we don't want that, and then Democrats had to be on the defensive. Now that equation has entirely flipped and, you know, Democrats are very eager. This White House thinks this is a very politically popular position for them to be in heading into 2024 because they don't have to articulate what they're for. They can just...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Reince?\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (NPR WHITE HOUSE ESPONDENT)\par \par \uc2 ...point at the Republicans.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 There's a 70 percent place on this issue, and that's that Americans support a 15-week first-trimester abortion ban. Part of the problem is, in a lot of these battleground states...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ban on abortion after the first trimester.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 After the first trimester. A lot of these battleground states, they have no, they, they...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, that's not where a lot of these states are. I mean, that's not where - Florida, you know.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 That's, that's my point. They don't have, a lot of these states like Wisconsin, they don't have a law on the books. When Scott Walker was...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 ...governor of Wisconsin, with the Republican legislature, they passed a 20-week ban, which would've resolved the problem in Wisconsin. Here's the other part, you're talking about the politics, the Democrats have gotten very, very good in these battleground states where you only have two percent of the voters that are deciding all of these elections now...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 ...in all of these states. They're microtargeting in places like Madison. They're paying, you know, - $400, here's ten people to get them to the polls and you get ten people and you get ten people, and it's all about abortion. And without an answer, on the other side of stumbling and bumbling your way through the campaign trail...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, but, but, I mean...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (FMR TRUMP WHITE HOUSE CHIEF OF STAFF/FMR RNC CHAIR)\par \par \uc2 ...you are going to get beat unless there's a clear answer on this issue from Republicans across the country.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, and, and Democrats think this will be a winning issue for them.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 Oh, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 I mean, they've already seen so many different elections on the local level, state level and obviously during the midterms, where we have seen just a lot of enthusiasm from the Democratic base. I do wanna say, one thing we won't be seeing anytime soon on Capitol Hill is a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A national ban. Yeah, there's not the votes for it. That's the bottom line.\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 It's just not gonna happen.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you very much. That's all for the Roundtable. But coming up, we have another anti-Trump candidate who has just jumped into the Republican presidential primary. Joining us live, former Texas Congressman \uc2 Will Hurd\uc2 , a Sunday exclusive.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230629ej6p00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE CHRIS CHRISTIE CHRISTIE MAKES CASE AGAINST TRUMP DESPITE VOTER PUSHBACK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,667 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, WAR, UK, RU, PRIGOZHIN, REVOLT, PUTIN, ZELENSKYY, WAGNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIAN REVOLT\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, WAR, 2024, SPEECH, TRUMP, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 That is not leadership, everybody. That is a failure of leadership. And I, you can boo all you want. But here's the thing, our faith teaches us that people have to take responsibility for what they do. People have to stand up and take accountability for what they do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE ROAD TO 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MUTINY THREAT EXPOSES DISARRAY IN RUSSIA'S WAR OPERATION\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  bluntly criticizing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before a skeptical crowd of social conservatives at the Faith and Freedom Conference in Washington. The former New Jersey governor and former ABC News contributor joins us now. Governor Christie, I want to get to that in a minute. But first, you heard Secretary Blinken talking about the situation in Moscow. There's a lot that the United States just doesn't know about what is going down. How would a President Christie be handling this situation?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, here's what we do know, Jon. What we do know is that America's support, and along with our allies in \uc2 NATO\uc2 , of Ukraine, has done a great deal to cause what we're seeing right now in Russia. Putin's misadventure and all of the missteps that happened by the Biden administration, the Trump administration and the Obama administration on this issue have led to this moment.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And I think you have to watch this very carefully, but we have to continue to support Ukraine. We have to give them the weapons they need to fight their battle against the Russians and to repel them. And I think that what this may do, Jon, is move us closer to a resolution of this battle because of Putin's weakness that's obvious now inside his own country, I think in large part because of the way he has prosecuted this war.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT DOES WAGNER MUTINY MEAN FOR PUTIN'S GRIP ON POWER?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As you know, there are increasingly loud voices within the Republican Party calling for the United States to stop aiding Ukraine. What's your message, including some of your opponents, what's your message to them in light of all this?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 That America has never been a great country and the leader of the world by filling in the moat and pulling up the draw bridge. You know, we need to make sure that we're engaged. Because, believe me, this is the first fight in the proxy war with China. China is funding this war for Russia by buying Russian oil. And they are saying very clearly that there is no limit to the partnership between Russia and China.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We need to make sure that we continue to engage in this way. We do not want a world that is dominated by communist China. And so, this is a fight that America needs to have. It always involves sacrifice. But in the end, at the end of the sacrifice, I am absolutely a believer in the fact that America will be bigger, stronger, richer, and more influential in the world because we stood by our principles and stood by our friends.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHRISTIE MAKES CASE AGAINST TRUMP DESPITE VOTER PUSHBACK\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. We heard the reaction to your speech at the Faith and Freedom Conference. I, I assume you well knew you were gonna get booed when you started slamming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's leadership. I did hear some applause in that crowd as well, but the boos were loud. What, what, what's your sense? And are, is the anti-Trump message, is there any evidence that, that, that it's resonating?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely evidence it's resonating, Jon. I've been in the, in the race for less than three weeks, and I'm already in third place in New Hampshire. Only four points behind \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has been in the race for a longer time and is supposed to be the co-frontrunner. Look, people understand that folks need to take responsibility for what they do. And my message to the folks at Faith and Freedom, which did get some good reaction, too, but of course I expected the boos that is predominantly a Trump crowd.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 But they need to hear the truth, too, that, you know, character is the single most important element of a president of the United States, because you can't know every, every issue that gonna come across a president's desk. It's not a litmus test with check boxes around them. What you need to know is what is the character of that person. And, frankly, when I, I listened to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's speech last night, he had the audacity to say that he got indicted for us.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Now, I don't know how it benefited the American people for him to take highly sensitive intelligence and secret documents out of the White House, to stonewall the government on returning them for over a year and a half, to subject himself to a raid by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , even though they had asked to voluntarily to return this stuff, and to then be subject to an indictment which is obviously gonna be one of great trouble for the country because no one wants to see this happen.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says that's for us, and it's, it's absurd, in same way he has absurdly claimed in the last week that he still won the 2020 election. And he said that's how he's gonna persuade suburban female voters to vote for him in 2024 that didn't vote for him in '20. Look, this guy lost in '18. He lost the Senate and the White House in '20, the House in '18. He lost two more governorships in his Senate race in 2022. He is a three-time loser.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We do not need our party to go to a fourth loss. Because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in my opinion, Jon, is an awful president and we can't afford to have him from age 82 to 86 in the White House, or even worse, have \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  assume the presidency. That's the stakes here. It's not about whether you think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been treated fairly or not by the media or by elements of the Justice Department. It is about whether he is a man of character who can lead this party to victory, and I don't believe he can.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS GRAPPLE WITH ABORTION DEBATE AHEAD OF 2024\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, I think we know where you stand. Let, let, let me ask you, before you go, the question of abortion. Yesterday, of course, was the one-year anniversary of the repeal of Roe. DeSantis, of course, signed into law a six-month abortion ban. Your position, as I understand it, is the states should decide. Do you think that six-month abortion ban makes DeSantis unelectable in a general election?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I think it's a six-week abortion ban, Jon.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Six, I'm sorry, six-week, six-week, excuse me, yes. The six-week abortion ban, yes, yeah, yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Right, six-week abortion ban. Look, Jon, conservatives, like me, for the last 50 years, have been arguing this is not a federal issue, it's a state issue and it's something the states should decide. The Dobbs case one year ago gave us the opportunity to let each state make this decision. And what I hope to see is that with each of the 50 states, but more importantly, the people of each of the 50 states, deciding this issue. We then could see a national consensus develop.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 If the national consensus develops, I have no problem with the federal government then stepping in and confirming that national consensus. But I think we should allow the states and the people of the states to be heard on this issue. It's an incredibly important issue. Jon, I'm pro-life. I've always been pro-life with exceptions for rape, incest and the life of the mother, and I remain pro-life and was a pro-life governor of a very blue state and was elected twice.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 But these are the kind of issues we need to, we need to be discussing on the debate stage on August 23rd. And as you know, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  said you need 40,000 donors to get on that stage. So, anybody who is listening this morning, go to ChrisChristie.com, donate a dollar.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Make sure we have these debates and the debate like I had in Faith and Freedom. We need to do that, Jon.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Governor Christie, thank you. Good to have you on "This Week." Take care. Up next, the Powerhouse...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE\uc2  (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Jon.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Up next, the Powerhouse Roundtable, with Donna Brazile and Reince Priebus, breaks down all the week's politics. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Roundtable is here and ready to go. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230629ej6p00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOP HOPEFULS VIE FOR VOTES AFTER THE FALL OF ROE CANDIDATES TOUT ANTI-ABORTION CREDENTIALS\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: REBELLION IN RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 MERCENARY, PUTIN, REBELS, MUTINY\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, PRIGOZHIN, MERCENARY, RUSSIANS, MILITARY, ABRAMS\par \par \uc2 TITAN, IMPLOSION, INVESTIGATION, KIRBY, CAMERON, SOHNLEIN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, CANDIDATES, PENCE, DESANTIS, COLON, BIDEN, JEAN-PIERRE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Today marks one year since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V Wade, allowing states to ban abortion. That issue is already heating up among 2024 presidential hopefuls. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze joins us now from Washington. And, Elizabeth, Republicans already trying to appeal to anti-abortion voters. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. That's right, some Republican presidential hopefuls are now renewing the push for a national abortion ban, saying that landmark Supreme Court decision reversing Roe V Wade didn't go far enough.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, one year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe V Wade, the political battle over abortion rights taking center stage. At the Faith and Freedom Coalition conference Friday in Washington, Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  challenging every GOP presidential hopeful to support a national ban on abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We must not rest and must not relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law in every state in this country.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  touting his state's strict new law that would ban abortions after just six weeks, before many women know they're pregnant.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 It was the right thing to do. Don't let anyone tell you it wasn't.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the Supreme Court ended the constitutional right to an abortion, 15 states have passed laws severely limiting access to reproductive care. Women in those states, like Mississippi, left with few options.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE COLON (CO-FOUNDER/EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR SHERO MISSISSIPPI)\par \par \uc2 There's still a lot of confusion and fear.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE RESPONDS TO ANTI-ABORTION MESSAGE. AMERICANS "DO NOT WANT POLITICIANS MAKING THEIR HEALTHCARE DECISIONS"\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After mobilizing voters in the midterm elections, President Biden says reproductive rights are again at stake in 2024.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, this election is about freedom on the ballot once again.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President signing a new largely symbolic executive order, calling on federal agencies to expand access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We know you're at the end of the line here when it comes to what you can do without steps from Congress.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 So, we don't believe this is symbolic. We believe that this is another step to do everything that we can to continue to fight for fundamental rights.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The split screen on abortion rights will be on full display today. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is set to give a major speech in North Carolina to abortion rights advocates while Former President Trump will rally evangelical voters here in Washington tonight. Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth, we appreciate your reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230712ej6o000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION ON THE BALLOT 2024 HOPEFULS CAMPAIGN ON ONE YEAR AFTER SCOTUS DECISION\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, MUTINY, PRIGOZHIN, PUTIN, PODOLYAK\par \par \uc2 WAR, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, MUTINY, WAGNER GROUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS IN RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, MUTINY, BIDEN, MILLEY\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, TRAIN, STAMEY, CHEMICAL SPILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAIN DERAILS IN YELLOWSTONE RIVER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADO AND FLOOD THREATS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, PEREZ, MCMANUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICERS CHARGED WITH MURDER\par \par \uc2 TITAN, IMPLOSION, FOX, S\u214\'00\'D6HNLEIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TITANIC SUB DISASTER PROBE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, HALEY, PENCE, HARRIS, BIDEN, ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the race for the White House and abortion on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The presidential hopefuls on the campaign trail today, trying to define their positions on abortion. And protests across the country marking the first anniversary of the Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Em Nguyen at the Supreme Court tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2024 HOPEFULS CAMPAIGN ON ONE YEAR AFTER SCOTUS DECISION\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, one year after the Supreme Court overruled Roe vs. Wade, abortion is taking center stage on the 2024 campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI HALEY (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Let's protect religious liberty.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (VO) Former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley telling voters today there is a place for a federal law on abortion, an about-face from last month, when she called it unrealistic. Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  calling on his GOP rivals to join him in supporting a 15-week federal abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We will never rest and never relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEAR OR TOTAL ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, 15 states have enacted laws for a total or near total abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Over the past 365 days, the women of our nation have suffered.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (VO) Prompting President Biden on Friday to sign an executive order aimed to strengthen access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake, this election is about freedom on the ballot once again.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Washington today, anti and pro-abortion rights activists say, in 2024, abortion is on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 PEDESTRIAN (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I am a single-issue voter. I care about the pro-life issue.\par \par \uc2 PEDESTRIAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Next year, you just really have to vote and get your voice heard.\par \par \uc2 EM NGUYEN. ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 (OC) According to the most recent poll by ABC News, 78% of Americans say a decision about abortion should be left to a woman and her doctor, including 58% of the Republicans. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Em Nguyen reporting tonight, thank you. There's still much more ahead on "World News Tonight" this Saturday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We'll take you back to Ukraine for an update on the fluid situation in Russia. And a 13-year-old attacked by an eight-foot gator, now detailing how he got away.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230627ej6o00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS BATTLE PENCE CALLS ON GOP CANDIDATES TO SUPPORT 15-WEEK BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TITAN, RUSH, BLOOM, MARQUET, DAWOOD, CAMERON, BALLARD\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PRIGOZHIN, WAGNER GROUP\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ROE V. WADE, PENCE, DESANTIS, BIDEN, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, one year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade. Republicans are calling for unity behind a federal ban on abortion. But they don't all agree on where to draw the line. President Biden, meantime, is doing what he can to shore up access to reproductive care. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENCE CALLS ON GOP CANDIDATES TO SUPPORT 15-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the eve of the anniversary of the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe vs. Wade, the future of abortion rights in this country front and center. Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  calling on his 2024 rivals to back a nationwide minimum 15-week abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Every Republican candidate for President should support a ban on abortion before 15 weeks as a minimum nationwide standard.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Aren't you glad to live in the free state of Florida?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has gone even further in his state, today defending the bill he signed that bans abortion at six weeks, before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It was the right thing to do. Don't let anyone tell you it wasn't.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the most he said on the subject since he launched his campaign for president after the frontrunner former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  criticized DeSantis for going too far. Saying in an interview, that many people within the pro-life movement feel that that was too harsh. But when Trump was pressed to clarify his own stance, he didn't answer.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Some people are at six weeks, some people are at three weeks. President Trump is going to make a determination what he thinks is great for the country and what's fair for the country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, 15 states have severely restricted access to abortion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN SIGNS EXECUTIVE ORDER PROTECTING CONTRACEPTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden today signing an executive order to protect access to birth control. But he has acknowledged there's only so much he could do alone.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I never ever thought I'd be signing an executive order protecting the right to contraception. But the only sure way to protect a woman's health and rights is for Congress to pass a law.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) According to a FiveThirtyEight analysis of recent polling data, more Americans now believe that abortion should be illegal in some cases. Both sides hoping to use this as a driving issue in 2024. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230627ej6n00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TIANNA MADISON SPEAKS OUT TWO-TIME OLYMPIAN ON BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH & HER PREGNANCY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,176 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS MORNING: THE HEAT IS ON!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PICKING UP THE PIECES\par \par \uc2 HEAT, STORM, TEXAS, FLORIDA, CONE, FEINSTEIN\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, TEXAS, PANHANDLE, PERRYTON, KERBL\par \par \uc2 SUMMER, TRAVEL, JUNETEENTH, HOLIDAY, TSA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR, BELARUS, NUCLEAR, TACTICAL\par \par \uc2 CHINA, BEIJING, BLINKEN, CONFLICT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, 2024\par \par \uc2 MINNEAPOLIS, EXCESSIVE FORCE, POLICE, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 SYNAGOGUE, PITTSBURGH, SHOOTER, DEATH PENALTY\par \par \uc2 DELTA, AMERICAN AIRLINES, INCIDENT, AIRPORT, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 CHARLES, MONARCH, JOBSON, TROOPING THE COLOUR\par \par \uc2 MORANT, \uc2 NBA\uc2 , SUSPENDED, GUN, MCNUTT, SMITH\par \par \uc2 SHARK, AMPUTATED, LEG, BOAT, BAHAMAS, ERNST, SKOMAL, REED\par \par \uc2 GRAMMYS, AI, MUSIC, PARMAR\par \par \uc2 TEENS, JOBS, HUTCHINSON, JOHNSON, BUNKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 KING CHARLES, TROOPING THE COLOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROYAL TRADITION FOR THE NEW KING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHARLES III'S FIRST TROOPING THE COLOUR AS MONARCH\par \par \uc2 SAFETY, WEIGHTED SLEEP SACKS, INFANT\par \par \uc2 PRIDE MONTH, ANTI-TRANS BILL, PROTEST, FARIA, CLICK\par \par \uc2 MADISON, MURTHY, PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIANNA MADISON SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO-TIME OLYMPIAN ON BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH & HER PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, well now to the story bringing much-needed attention to the black maternal health crisis. Olympian Tory Bowie dying unexpectedly of complications during childbirth this past May. Now, her teammates are speaking out about their own difficulties while pregnant, something that disproportionately affects black women. Allyson Felix penning an essay for "Time" magazine, asking for a wakeup call around the issue. And Tianna Madison posting on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  about her experience, saying, she went to the hospital with her medical advance directive and her will, giving birth to her son at just 26 weeks. I got the chance to sit down with her to ask her about that decision. Here's our conversation.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tianna Madison, the two-time Olympian was training for the Tokyo 2021 Olympics when she learned she was two months' pregnant. The unexpected pregnancy took another unexpected turn at just 26 weeks.\par \par \uc2 TIANNA MADISON (GOLD MEDAL OLYMPIAN TRACK & FIELD ATHLETE)\par \par \uc2 When I stepped out of the shower and dried off, there was blood on my towel. So, I went to my partner and said we need to go to the hospital. We went to the hospital, and I learned that I was already centimeters dilated.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While rushing to the hospital for help, Tianna grabbed not only her advance medical directive, but also her will.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What specifically made you think, if I'm going to the hospital right now, I need to have my will with me?\par \par \uc2 TIANNA MADISON (GOLD MEDAL OLYMPIAN TRACK & FIELD ATHLETE)\par \par \uc2 I knew what the stats were for black women when they go into the hospitals to give birth. So, my partner and I had discussed it. We were very prepared and we had a conversation. If it came between me and the baby, he would choose me if I was incapacitated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MATERNAL MORTALITY RATE IN THE UNITED STATES\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The latest report from the CDC finding shockingly high rates of maternal mortality in the US, a 40% spike in 2021 with black women three to four times more likely to die from a pregnancy-related cause than white woman during pregnancy and within a year of giving birth.\par \par \uc2 DR VIVEK MURTHY (US SURGEON GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 In 2021, we lost over 1,200 people to maternal mortality. And it turns out, more than 80% of those deaths were preventable.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thankfully, under medical care, Tianna and her baby survived. But the traumatic events of her pregnancy and the risks to black mothers have changed her future plans.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you plan on having more children?\par \par \uc2 TIANNA MADISON (GOLD MEDAL OLYMPIAN TRACK & FIELD ATHLETE)\par \par \uc2 No. We have discussed this extensively. To voluntarily put myself and my body at risk of doing that again is not something that my family is willing to do. Maybe that will all change but, as of right now, absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For doula and Mama Glow founder Latham Thomas, black mothers-to-be need to find the care team that works for them.\par \par \uc2 LATHAM THOMAS (FOUNDER MAMA GLOW)\par \par \uc2 You want to find providers who are like minded that you get along with well and you feel like you can voice your concerns with. A huge thing that comes up for a lot of black women and birthing people is that they do not feel heard or they might feel dismissed. And what happens when we don't get the adequate care that we need is sometimes we're underdiagnosed. Oftentimes we're misdiagnosed and things that can be treated earlier in a pregnancy might become lethal towards the end. And so, really important to have that communication with your care providers.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you have friends or family members, other black women tell you they're pregnant, what goes through your mind?\par \par \uc2 TIANNA MADISON (GOLD MEDAL OLYMPIAN TRACK & FIELD ATHLETE)\par \par \uc2 We need to put ourselves in position to save ourselves, educate ourselves and advocate. I want you to do what you need to do to come home alive so that you can raise your babies.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the federal government has invested in awareness, implicit bias training in health care, plus resources for women during pregnancy and the first year after giving birth, all with the hopes of reducing the number of maternal deaths. But experts say, these things that have been neglected for a long time and systematic change is necessary. In the meantime, if you need help, there is a national maternal health hotline, 1-833-TLC-MAMA. That's 1-833-852-6262. The hotline has licensed health care providers and mental health clinicians, plus certified doulas and educators. And one thing that I, it just dawned on me speaking with Tianna, because she, on her post, pointed out that three out of the four women on their relay have dealt with difficult births. One of them obviously didn't survive.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am a black woman. I am pregnant. And your socioeconomic status, your educational level, none of those things matter. And so, it is, it's something that, even reporting on, it doesn't make me immune to it. So, it is something that is top of mind and it's something we're living with.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As the surgeon general said, 80% of those deaths are preventable.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That shows how much of a difference can be made if they address this issue.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you really have been leading the way on this story. And it's so important because it affects so many women. So, thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Thank you, guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Janai.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230707ej6h0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES BUS CRASHES INTO BUILDING/IOWA ABORTION BAN BLOCKED\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TORNADO, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DESANTIS, HALEY, ELECTION 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN RE-ELECTION KICKOFF IN PHILLY\par \par \uc2 JOZEF, ALVAREZ, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIGRANT CHILD DEATH INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 PIETILA, THREAT, ANTISEMITISM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2 : SUSPECT PLANNED SYNAGOGUE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 FREDRICKSON, AIRPORT, CLOSE CALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLANE CLIPS WING ON TARMAC\par \par \uc2 ERNST, SKOMAL, SHARK, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DIVER: SHARK ATTACK WAS LIKE HORROR MOVIE\par \par \uc2 BUS, CRASH, IOWA, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUS CRASHES INTO BUILDING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Next, tonight, a frightening incident in Baltimore. A bus crashed into a building this morning as part of a multivehicle accident.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sixteen people were treated for injuries, none of them life-threatening. But the building was evacuated as a precaution while authorities assess the damage. The cause of the crash is under investigation.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IOWA ABORTION BAN BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Iowa will not be joining other Republican-led states in imposing strict abortion limits.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the state Supreme Court blocked a law that would ban abortions once cardiac activity could be detected. That's usually around six weeks of pregnancy before many women know they are pregnant. Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  says she is disappointed with the court's ruling and vowed to keep fighting for stricter abortion laws.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, an NFL player arrested at an airport. What the TSA says it found in his luggage.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230621ej6h00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POTENTIAL BREAKTHROUGH FOR BREAST CANCER PATIENTS DRUG COULD GREATLY REDUCE RISK OF RECURRENCE\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE PASSES DEBT LIMIT DEAL\par \par \uc2 DEBT DEAL, SENATE, REPUBLICANS, DEMOCRATS, SANDERS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBT DEAL, BIPARTISAN, ECONOMY, FALL\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ANALYSTS, ECONOMY, INFLATION, FED\par \par \uc2 COLLAPSE, MISSING, RECOVERY, BLADEL, ENGINEER, FEMA\par \par \uc2 FDA, WEIGHT LOSS, COMPOUNDED, SEMIGLUTIDE, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 RAINFALL, FLOODING, CARS, RESCUE, DROUGHT\par \par \uc2 APPS, CFPB, MONEY, VULNERABLE, CRISIS\par \par \uc2 NBA FINALS, \uc2 NUGGETS\uc2 , HEAT, GAME ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROPICAL DEPRESSION 2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, SHOT, CHEERLEADERS, CAR, RECOVERY, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 GPS, DRIVER, HAWAIIAN HARBOR, RESCUE, SOLMONSON\par \par \uc2 SHAH, SPELLING BEE, CHAMPION, PSAMMOPHILE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME DROUGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE PASSES DEAL OVERNIGHT: IT'S PASSED!\par \par \uc2 SENATE, DEBT, DEAL, PRESIDENT, GOVERNMENT, DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 REPORT, JOBS\par \par \uc2 SAMARITAN, SAVED, CAR, STOLEN, EVERMAN\par \par \uc2 JOEL, MADISON SQUARE GARDEN, RESIDENCY\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, RECURRENCE, REDUCE, SLAMON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "gma" Cover Story, the breakthrough for breast cancer patients you'll see first on "gma." New research shows a drug already on the market could dramatically reduce the risk of recurrence. Eva Pilgrim's gps finally worked (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The gps didn't work, but my legs do work (inaudible). For women diagnosed with breast cancer, getting to remission is often not the end of their journey. The fear of it coming back always lingering, but now there's some hope.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, exciting news for those diagnosed with early stage breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 MAMMOGRAM TECH (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Breathe and relax.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) New research reveals the drug Ribociclib, marketed under the name Kisqali, can lower the chances of recurrence for many of those diagnosed at earlier stages of the disease. Women who are hormone receptor positive and HER2 negative make up 70 percent of the breast cancer population. These patients are generally treated with chemotherapy and endocrine therapy, but the study shows adding this targeted therapy will further reduce the risk that the cancer returns.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR \uc2 DENNIS SLAMON\uc2  (CHIEF OF HEMATOLOGY AND ONCOLOGY UCLA HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 Women who have this subtype can have recurrences even 20 to 25 years after their initial diagnosis. We found that adding this drug to best available standard therapy will decrease the recurrence rate by as much as 25 percent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW HOPE TO REDUCE RISK OF BREAST CANCER'S RETURN. DRUG TAKEN AFTER INITIAL TREATMENT COULD PREVENT RECURRENCE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is big news for patients like 45-year-old mom, Suzanne Garner diagnosed with stage two five years ago. Doctors treated her with chemo and endocrine therapy.\par \par \uc2 SUZANNE GARNER (PARTICIPATED IN KISQALI CLINICAL TRIAL)\par \par \uc2 I didn't feel right. I felt that my risk of recurrence was still too high.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then she found the Kisqali clinical trial.\par \par \uc2 SUZANNE GARNER (PARTICIPATED IN KISQALI CLINICAL TRIAL)\par \par \uc2 I have a young daughter who needs her mom around for as long as possible, and I would absolutely do anything to reduce my risk of recurrence so I can be her mom for as long as she needs me.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And here's the good news. Kisqali is already fda approved for those with more advanced disease, and this new data means it could be used in even more patients. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that's some good news. Thank you, Eva.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230627ej620000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PROMISING ADVANCES IN BREAST CANCER DETECTION RESEARCHERS USING A.I. TO HELP DETERMINE SPREAD AND ANALYZE MEDICINE\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS ON THE MOVE: HOLIDAY CRUSH\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, MEMORIAL DAY, HOLIDAY, ROADS, BUTTIGIEG, BERG\par \par \uc2 MEMORIAL DAY, TRAVEL, BEACHES, ROADS\par \par \uc2 RAIN, EAST COAST, BEACHES, RIP CURRENT\par \par \uc2 DEBT, US, JUNE, BIDEN, MCHENRY, GEORGIEVA\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, DEFAULT, FINANCES\par \par \uc2 FRANCIS, HEALTH, FEVER, PONTIFF\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, COUNTEROFFENSIVE\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA, PLANE, EMERGENCY, DOOR\par \par \uc2 MEDICAID, PANDEMIC, BENEFITS, COVERAGE, TOLBERT, HAWKINS\par \par \uc2 2024, PRESIDENTIAL RACE, CANDIDATES, DESANTIS, TRUMP, GOP\par \par \uc2 CELTICS, BOSTON, MIAMI, \uc2 NBA\par \par \uc2 WALGREENS, BROWN, JUSTICE, SECURITY, SHOPLIFTER, BURRIS\par \par \uc2 SHARKS, BEACH, PATROL, RIP CURRENTS, BASDEO, SKOMAL\par \par \uc2 MEMORIAL DAY, DEALS, HOLIDAY, SALES, MCGRATH\par \par \uc2 THEME SONGS, "SUCCESSION", MUSIC, LIPSHUTZ\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, CONCERT, FANS, METLIFE\par \par \uc2 WHITSON, ISS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, MEMORIAL DAY\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, YELLEN, MCCARTHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEBT CEILING TALKS GO DOWN TO THE WIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TREASURY SECY SAYS U.S. WON'T BE ABLE TO PAY BILLS ON JUNE 5\par \par \uc2 CANCER, ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, TREATMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROMISING ADVANCES IN BREAST CANCER DETECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESEARCHERS USING A.I. TO HELP DETERMINE SPREAD AND ANALYZE MEDICINE\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to what we're learning about potentially promising advance in the deduction and treatment of breast cancer using artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Researchers are using AI to help determine whether a breast cancer patient's disease will spread. While the technology is being fully developed, AI is giving scientists new ways to analyze patterns in medicine, knowing whether a cancer will could potentially save thousands of lives by helping doctors more precisely target treatment before the disease advances. And, guys, this could be a game changer for so many, of course.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So important.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) AI taking over in so many different ways. This could be one really positive use.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, CELINE DION CANCELS TOUR\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here "GMA" on our "Moring Menu," Celine Dion canceling the rest of her world tour as she continues her battle with a rare neurological disorder. Her message to fans this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 5 MINUTES, TINA TURNER'S SIGNATURE STYLE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also, ahead, we are celebrating Tina Turner's most memorable looks. Legendary designer Bob Mackie is opening up to "GMA" about the passing of a rock and roll icon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT HALF HOUR, "MEET MODEL MAJORITY"\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And you don't want to miss this one. Coming up in our next half hour, meet the all-Asian comedy sketch group making a difference on stage. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230620ej5r00069\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SOUTH CAROLINA SENATE PASSES ABORTION BAN GOVERNOR EXPECTED TO SIGN BILL RESTRICTING PROCEDURE AFTER SIX WEEKS\b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLOCK\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, MCCARTHY, NEGOTIATIONS, REPUBLICANS, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, DEADLOCK, DEFAULT, HOUSE\par \par \uc2 DEBT CELLING, NEGOTIATIONS, WALL STREET, CREDIT, STOCKS\par \par \uc2 U-HAUL, ATTACK, WHITE HOUSE, KANDULA, NAZI, SECRET SERVICE\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, PRESIDENTIAL, CAMPAIGN, TWITTER, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, COURT, TRIAL, VIDEO, JUDGE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, SOUTH CAROLINA, MATTHEWS, SENN, FILIBUSTER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Aaron, thank you for your reporting. Now we move to South Carolina, becoming the latest state to pass restrictions on abortions, now banning the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy. Eva Pilgrim has the latest for us. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTH CAROLINA SENATE PASSES ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR EXPECTED TO SIGN BILL RESTRICTING PROCEDURE AFTER SIX WEEKS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. South Carolina is one of the last states in the southeast to restrict abortion access after Roe V. Wade was overturned. But getting this bill passed had a major hurdle, five female senators.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, South Carolina adding itself to the list of states enacting near total abortion bans. It took three failed attempts, but in a special legislative session, the Republican-led state senate passing a law that bans abortions after six weeks, that's before most women even know they're pregnant.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The South Carolina bill will require that pregnant women have two in-person doctors' appointments before receiving an abortion. 15 states have already stopped nearly all abortions. South Carolina's Governor already saying he will sign this bill into law soon, making it 16, effectively creating an abortion access desert for women in the southeast.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For weeks, an unlikely group of allies, the only five women in South Carolina's 46-seat Senate, prevented an abortion ban from passing. They call themselves the sister senators.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTH CAROLINA SENATE PASSES ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SISTER SENATORS" FROM BOTH SIDES OF AISLE FILIBUSTERED BILL\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How many of you are Democrats? How many are Republicans? How many are independents? Pro-life?\par \par \uc2 STATE SEN MARGIE BRIGHT-MATTHEWS (DEM) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 We're all pro-life. We're just not pro birth.\par \par \uc2 STATE SEN SANDY SENN (REP) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 Forced birth.\par \par \uc2 STATE SEN MARGIE BRIGHT-MATTHEWS (DEM) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 There you go. There's a difference. We all believe in life. Just, we believe in life for the woman as well as a well life for the child.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After three successful blocks, last night the sister senators filibuster failed to stop the six week ban. They are not giving up, and they hope they are encouraging other women to act.\par \par \uc2 STATE SEN SANDY SENN (REP) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 We are 51%, women are 51% of the South Carolina population. Only 14% of the general assembly, and even less than that in the Senate. But what I believe is the women are going to show up at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up on "GMA3," we will have more of the conversation with the sister senators. It's the first time they've sat down, all five of them, together for an interview. They a very different politically. So it's an interesting sisterhood. And, Michael, it was a very interesting conversation.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230616ej5o0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MORE WOMEN SET TO SUE TEXAS OVER ABORTION BAN DENIED PROCEDURE DESPITE FACING MEDICAL EMERGENCIES\b0\par\par\uc2 965 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEBT CEILING SHOWDOWN INTENSIFIES\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MCCARTHY, DEBT CEILING, NEGOTIATIONS, YELLEN\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, NEGOTIATIONS, DEMOCRATS, REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, DEFAULT, WALL STREET, PLUNGE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, BAKHMUT, ZELENSKYY, BIDEN, \uc2 G-7\par \par \uc2 WHELAN, RUSSIA, PRISON, ESPIONAGE, RELEASE\par \par \uc2 SCOTT, PRESIDENTIAL BID, REPUBLICANS, CONSERVATIVE\par \par \uc2 PGA CHAMPIONSHIP, KOEPKA, BLOCK, HOLE IN ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SEINFELD"\par \par \uc2 KOHBERGER, COURT, INDICTMENT, VICTIMS, GONCALVES, LLOYD, LABAR\par \par \uc2 SHARK, ATTACK, BLANCO, FISHING, TOURNIQUET, NAYLOR\par \par \uc2 UBER, TEENS, STERN, KANSAL, CREPPY, SAFETY, TRACKING\par \par \uc2 "AMERICAN IDOL", TONGI, WINNER, "MONSTERS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, MCCARTHY, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN & MCCARTHY SET TO MEET AS DEBT DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NO DEAL AFTER TENSE WEEKEND OF ON-AND-OFF NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, WALL STREET\par \par \uc2 GRINER, \uc2 WNBA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRITTNEY GRINER BACK ON THE COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAYS FIRST REGULAR SEASON WNBA GAME SINCE RELEASE FROM RUSSIAN PRISON\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, ABORTION, DENNARD, MILLER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're back now with our "GMA Cover Story" and an update on a story we brought you in March.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE WOMEN SET TO SUE TEXAS OVER ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAY THEY WERE DENIED PROCEDURE DESPITE FACING MEDICAL EMERGENCIES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a group of women suing the state Texas over its abortion law, saying they were denied the procedure even though they were facing medical emergencies that put their lives in jeopardy. That lawsuit is expected to expand this morning. Rachel Scott is back with that for us. Good morning again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning to you. Two women, a doctor and her patient, both had to travel out of the state of Texas to get an abortion within months of each other. They're now joining a much larger group of women suing the state, saying that that abortion ban put their lives at risk.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When the Texas abortion ban went into effect, Dr. Austin Dennard was so worried about the law, she struggled to even say the word.\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 I've had to change the way that I speak to my patients about abortion. It's even hard to say the word because you feel like you're going to get in trouble.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In July of 2022, Dennard got the news she and her husband had been waiting for. They were pregnant again and thrilled. But at her 11-week ultrasound visit, something startling on the monitor.\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 I could tell there was something not right with the brain. And it was just a moment of, sorry, just realizing that this is was not going to end up being a sibling for my children. And then I thought to myself, I can't believe I'm going to go out of state for an abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her unborn baby was diagnosed with anencephaly, a rare and fatal condition affecting the development of the brain. Still, if Dennard wanted an abortion, she would have to travel out of state to get one.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Was that a difficult process?\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 I'm an OBGYN. I understood my diagnosis. I had the means to pay for an abortion. I am the best-case scenario.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Dennard returned to work and continued to care for her patients, including Lauren Miller, who was expecting twins.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT-OF-STATE FOR AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I was like, you know, hopefully, I won't need help planning a camping trip to Colorado. Planning a camping trip to Colorado.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Planning a camping trip to Colorado, is that how the two of you were discussing traveling to get an abortion?\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm. Correct.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In coded language.\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 It seems surreal.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just a few weeks later, Miller would be facing a similar decision. Twelve weeks into her pregnancy, she learned one of her twins had a rare genetic condition and would likely not survive.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT-OF-STATE FOR AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It was clear I needed an abortion because, every day going on, it was putting my health and our healthy twin at risk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLAIM THEY WERE DENIED PROCEDURE, PUTTING THEIR LIVES AT RISK\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She ended up traveling to Colorado for an abortion. In March, Miller gave birth to one healthy baby boy, Henry, and joining a group of seven women filing a suit against the state of Texas, demanding more clarity on the portion of the law that allows a woman to get an abortion in emergency cases.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT-OF-STATE FOR AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 You just don't know what the law is. How close to dead do I have to be before I can fully access health care?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And today, eight more women expected to join that lawsuit, including Miller's own doctor.\par \par \uc2 DR AUSTIN DENNARD (OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 I want autonomy back as a woman and as a physician.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Dennard is now happily pregnant and is expecting a baby later this fall. When the lawsuit was first filed, a spokesperson for the Texas attorney general's office said that they are committed to protecting mothers, families and unborn children, while also defending Texas law. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you, Rachel, for being with us this morning. And I want everybody to know that they can see more of your reporting tonight on "Nightline."\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230616ej5m0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LANDMARK LAWSUIT ABORTION CARE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,899 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, TEXAS, LAWSUIT, MILLER, NORTHUP, DENNARD, ZURAWSKI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, thank you for joining us. We begin tonight with the women caught in the middle of the hot button issue of abortion. They were happy to be pregnant, but faced medical emergencies and were forced to leave their home state of Texas to save their lives. Now they're behind a first of its kind lawsuit. Here's ABC's congressional correspondent Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For 35-year-old Lauren Miller, the joy of holding her newborn son Henry still feels surreal.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Hi. Hi.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The journey to get here was filled with both pain and loss. Lauren first found out she was pregnant with twins in July 2022.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 So at first, when we first found out that it was twins, I was shocked but then ecstatic.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She kept a journal throughout the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Here it is at the very beginning. I hope, especially with the fall of Roe V. Wade, that this pregnancy is as uncomplicated and normal as my pregnancy with Logan. Was not. It took a very different turn.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At 12 weeks, she learned that one of her unborn twins, which the doctors had named baby B, would likely not survive.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 For baby B, they were also seeing these two large fluid masses is in his brain. I mean, it was just heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The baby had Trisomy 18, a condition with a very high likelihood of miscarriage or stillbirth and low survival rates beyond the first year of life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did it feel like your world turned upside down overnight?\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It did. I'm just thinking through, you know, what's it's gonna be growing up and people are going to refer to the Miller twins. There are no Miller twins. Just the one now.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lauren had to make an excruciating decision, for the best odds of survival for one twin, she would have to abort the other.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 There was just no decision, he had no future. And for his twin, I risked losing that one. So that was devastating too. I think about sometimes when I'm holding my newborn son, because of the laws in the state, he could have not made it. That's not even touching on the risks to myself.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a post-Roe world with Texas' restrictive abortion ban, Lauren says it was impossible to get the care she needed in her own hometown. At 15 weeks she flew to Colorado to have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 And I remember I was visibly pregnant and just going through the security lines, like could they pull us aside and asked why we're going? You just don't know, there's just this sense of fear that is so pervasive, and it shouldn't be.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Texas law bans abortion with few exceptions, leaving women like Lauren in impossible situations. Though Texas does have an exception for medical emergencies, the details are ambiguous. Now she is part of a group of women suing the state of Texas, saying they were denied "Necessary and potentially lifesaving obstetrical care because medical professionals throughout the state fear liability under Texas' abortion bans."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The lawsuit was originally filed in March, eight more women joined today. In March, a spokesperson for Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  said in a statement that Paxton will, "Continue to defend and enforce the laws duly enacted by the Texas legislature."\par \par \uc2 NANCY NORTHUP\uc2  (PRESIDENT & CEO CENTER FOR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS)\par \par \uc2 We had examples in the women who come forward in this lawsuit, is that their doctors have gone to the hospital boards seeking to have the permission to terminate a pregnancy, and the boards are saying no. And so they have to go back to their patients and say there's nothing that we can do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The suit is the first to be filed by women impacted by statewide abortion bans since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade last year. 15 states now have either a total or six-week abortion ban, before many women even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 NANCY NORTHUP\uc2  (PRESIDENT & CEO CENTER FOR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS)\par \par \uc2 States pass abortion bans and then say that because they have an exception for life, for saving your life, that that is okay. In reality, those aren't met. And we see that in this case in Texas, where the lead plaintiff had a life-threatening complication. She ended up in the ICU, and yet she wasn't granted an abortion until she was at death's door.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That lead plaintiff, Amanda Zurawski, says she was told he baby would not survive, but she could not get an abortion. It wasn't until she went into septic shock and nearly died that she received an emergency abortion delivering her stillborn daughter. The infection caused permanent damage to one of her fallopian tubes. She testified before Congress last month.\par \par \uc2 AMANDA ZURAWSKI (LEAD PLAINTIFF EMER ABORTION ACCESS LAWSUIT AGAINST TEXAS)\par \par \uc2 I wasn't permitted to have an abortion and the trauma and the PTSD and the depression that I have dealt with in the eight months since this happened to me, is paralyzing. I am still struggling to have children.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lauren, too, is grappling with the aftermath of what happened.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It wasn't until he was born I could finally hold my son that I was just so happy he was here. I think that's what I said to him. I think I said, you made it. It's hard to get over that. It's hard to grieve that fully. And frankly, it makes me mad, too.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It makes you angry?\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I shouldn't be looking at my son saying I'm so glad you made it despite the laws of the state. I was far enough along. I was, I was really excited for twins. And every time I see, you know, I'll see things for twins now and every single time, it kind of hits that my son is a twinless twin.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Dennard is Lauren's OB/GYN, and was by her side throughout her pregnancy. Both women worried about what it meant to be pregnant in a post-Roe era. In Texas, it is a second-degree felony to perform or attempt an abortion, punishable by up to life in prison or a fine of $100,000.\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 It's not that being a physician is my profession, it's part of me. It's who I am. It's like woven into my DNA at this point. So when these laws came into effect, it was not just violating the autonomy that I felt like I had with my own training, it was putting my own livelihood on the line in addition to, of course, my patients.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did you have to change the way that you talk to your patients, the type of conversations that you have?\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 I've had to change the way that I speak to my patients about, about abortion. It's even hard to say the word because you feel like you're going to get in trouble just by saying the word abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Dennard understands exactly what her patients are going through post-Roe. She's been there herself.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did you ever think as an OB/GYN that you would be sitting down to tell this story as both a doctor and a patient?\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 The short answer is no. I never ever thought that I would be getting an abortion or that I would be struggling to help my patients get abortions.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In July of 2022, Dennard got to the news she and her husband had been waiting for, they were pregnant again and thrilled to welcome their third child. But at her 11-week ultrasound, she saw something startling on the monitor.\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 I could tell there was something not right with the brain. And it was just a moment of, sorry. Sorry. Just realizing that this was not going to end up being a sibling for my children. And then I thought to myself, I can't believe I'm going to go out of state for an abortion. It just, it felt surreal.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her unborn baby was diagnosed with Anencephaly, a rare and fatal condition affecting the development of the brain. Still, if Dr. Dennard wanted an abortion, she, like her patient Lauren Miller, would have to travel out of state to get one.\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 I knew immediately that I didn't want to continue the pregnancy, and I think I didn't want to put my health, physical, mental emotional health at risk continuing my pregnancy. But for somebody else, carrying a pregnancy with Anencephaly, feeling their baby move, delivering their baby, holding their baby while it passes away, potentially, might be what's right for them. I just knew it wasn't right for me. So as soon as I had the diagnosis, I started seeking abortion care out of state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Dennard is now pregnant again, expecting her third child in the fall. Both she and Lauren hope this lawsuit could save lives.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MILLER (TRAVELED OUT OF STATE FOR ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 So for patients in this situation, I hope they are able to access the abortion care that they need. For lawmakers, I hope that they actually read our stories, absorb them, digest them, and realize that there are so many of us that they are hurting.\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 I just, I want autonomy back, as a woman and as a physician.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you feel like sitting down and doing this interview is even a risk?\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. Even surrounded by people that I love and care about and know, it's still scary.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you still believe it's worth it?\par \par \uc2 DR. AUSTIN DENNARD (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 I do. I do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRIUMPH OVER TRAGEDY\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel. Coming up, triumph over tragedy. The exclusive interview with Rick Allen, the drummer with the legendary rock band Def Leppard, known for classic songs like, "Photograph."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230524ej5m00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NORTH CAROLINA UPHOLDS RESTRICTIVE ABORTION BILL LAWMAKERS OVERRIDE GOVERNOR'S VETO OF 12-WEEK BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLIMMERS OF HOPE?\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, MCCARTHY, G-7, YELLEN, DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, BREACH, SULLIVAN, BREAK-IN, SECRET SERVICE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BILL, NORTH CAROLINA, GOP, COOPER, VETO\par \par \uc2 CIA, RUSSIAN, UKRAINE, KIRBY, DEFENSE SYSTEM, AMERICAN\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, VOITA, IVIE, SCHOFIELD, SUSPECT, MOTIVE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, BROWN, ANTHONY, HENDERSON, DA, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 AI, ALTMAN, BLUMENTHAL, REGULATED, CAPITOL HILL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , PLAYOFFS, \uc2 NUGGETS\uc2 , LAKERS, JOKIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAMAGING STORM REPORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, MURDER, TRIAL, GUILTY, HERNANDEZ, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 OLIVERSON, LITTLE LEAGUE, BUNK BEDS, LAWSUIT, FULGINTI\par \par \uc2 MEMORIAL DAY, SALES, JACKET, MATTRESSES, FURNITURE\par \par \uc2 KINDNESS, LINITA EDGE, \uc2 DETROIT TIGERS\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, MCCARTHY, MEETING, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLOCK TICKING ON DEBT CEILING SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT CUTS SHORT FOREIGN TRIP AFTER MEETING\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, REGULATION, NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH CAROLINA UPHOLDS RESTRICTIVE ABORTION BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWMAKERS OVERRIDE GOVERNOR'S VETO OF 12-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And George, to the rules overnight about abortion laws in North Carolina and the new restrictions. Faith Abubey is back with that. Good morning again, Faith.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. There were loud boos and chants in the North Carolina capitol as the Republican-led legislature approved the new restrictions on abortions, which essentially nullify the veto by the state's Democratic governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 . The law goes into effect on July 1, and it reduces abortion access in the state from 20 weeks currently down to 12 weeks. There are some exceptions, however, for rape or incest or in cases where the pregnant person's life might be in danger. Doctors who violate the new law could face fines, probation or even have their licenses revoked. Another notable detail in this law requires the father of the fetus to help raise the child even if that father offered to pay for the abortion. The North Carolina law is part of a new wave since last summer after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v Wade. And Michael, since then, 15 states have made almost all abortion services illegal. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you so much for that, Faith.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230615ej5h0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NORTH CAROLINA UPHOLDS RESTRICTIVE ABORTION BILL LAWMAKERS OVERRIDE GOVERNOR'S VETO OF 12-WEEK BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLIMMERS OF HOPE?\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, MCCARTHY, G-7, YELLEN, DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, BREACH, SULLIVAN, BREAK-IN, SECRET SERVICE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BILL, NORTH CAROLINA, GOP, COOPER, VETO\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No doubt with that. Okay, Pierre, thank you. Now to the news overnight about abortion laws in North Carolina, and the new restrictions. Faith Abubey has the latest for us. Good morning, Faith.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH CAROLINA UPHOLDS RESTRICTIVE ABORTION BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWMAKERS OVERRIDE GOVERNOR'S VETO OF 12-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. A major blow to abortion rights advocates in North Carolina. Overnight, the Republican led legislature approving new restrictions on abortions, overriding the veto by the state's Democratic Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 . Now the bill is called the care for women, children and families act, and it generally reduces abortion access from 20 weeks currently, to 12 weeks once the law goes into effect on July 1st.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are some exceptions. For examples, in cases of rape or incest, a person who will have up to 20 weeks for an abortion. And for fetal anomalies, up to 24 weeks. Abortions are also allowed in cases where the pregnant person's life might be in danger. The new rules require people seeking care to have in person consultations outlining potential risks and other available options to them before they get an abortion.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doctors who violate the new bill could face fines, probation or even have their licenses revoked. And since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade last summer, George, 15 states have made almost all abortion services illegal. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230615ej5h00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLE OVER ABORTION NORTH CAROLINA OVERRIDES GOVERNOR'S VETO OF BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRINCE HARRY, MARKLE, CAR CHASE, ADAMS, SAYEED, SINGH\par \par \uc2 SENTENCING, SAIPOV, MELISSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICTIMS CONFRONT NYC TRUCK TERRORIST\par \par \uc2 SULLIVAN, SECURITY BREACH, SECRET SERVICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCE: SECRET SERVICE DIRECTOR "LIVID"\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, CRISIS, PROTESTS, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIGRANT HOUSING PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, MCCARTHY, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: AMERICA WILL NOT DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, BAKER, ABORTION BAN, HAEFEN, DESANTIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, to another flash point tonight, the battle over abortion rights in the US after the Supreme Court overturned Roe. Tonight, two more states moving to severely restrict abortion, part of sweeping move across this country. And this evening, former President Trump taking credit for appointing justices who helped overturned Roe. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH CAROLINA OVERRIDES GOVERNOR'S VETO OF BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, both North Carolina and South Carolina moving to sharply curtail abortion rights with abortion now banned or deeply restricted across most of the south. Overnight, an emotional debate in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shame. Shame.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Republican-led legislature pushing through a bill to ban most abortions after 12 weeks after it was vetoed by the Democratic governor.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN BAKER (REP) (NORTH CAROLINA REPRESENTATIVE)\par \par \uc2 It balances protecting the life of the unborn child. It balances that with a woman's need for life-saving care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats were dismayed.\par \par \uc2 JULIE VON HAEFEN (DEM) (NORTH CAROLINA STATE REPRESENTATIVE)\par \par \uc2 Women did not ask for your oversight, they didn't ask for your supervision.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, in South Carolina, Republicans trying to push through a bill to ban abortion at six weeks before women even though they're pregnant. Since Roe vs. Wade was overturned a year ago, at least 15 states have stopped nearly all abortion services. Still, others have passed bans yet to go into effect like Florida, where Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a six-week ban. DeSantis, who is planning to run for president, challenged President Trump to say whether he would do the same.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 I signed a bill. I was proud to do it. He won't answer whether he would sign it or not.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He has yet to say if he supports a national ban. But today, he pointed to the three justices he handpicked that were appointed to the Supreme Court, declaring, "I was able to kill Roe vs Wade. Without me, the pro-life movement would've just kept losing."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, abortion is shaping up to be a major issue in the Republican primary and a divisive one among the candidates. While restrictions are very popular among the Republican base, some in the party fear that a hard-line approach could further push away voters that they need to win the general election, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With the race for the White House well underway. Rachel, tonight, thank you. Good to have you here in New York.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230519ej5h00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DESANTIS CHALLENGES TRUMP FL GOVERNOR AND FORMER PRESIDENT SPAR OVER ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, WILSON, KIMBELL, CRUM, DOWDY\par \par \uc2 SECURITY BREACH, SULLIVAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTRUDER IN BIDEN ADVISER'S HOME\par \par \uc2 CONNOLLY, PHAM, HATE CRIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT FACES HATE CRIME CHARGE\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, MCCARTHY, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES DEBT MEETING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE: MISSILE BARRAGE SHOT DOWN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DESANTIS, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESANTIS CHALLENGES TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back here at home tonight and to the race for the White House. On the Republican side, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  now taking on former President Trump after Trump refused to say whether he would sign a national abortion ban. Here's \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FL GOVERNOR AND FORMER PRESIDENT SPAR OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  moves towards a presidential run, his aides tell ABC News he will announce around Memorial Day, he's now facing off against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on a critical issue for Republican primary voters. Abortion. It comes after Trump criticized DeSantis for signing a law banning almost all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. "If you look at what DeSantis did, come a lot of people don't even know if he knew when he was doing," Trump told the new site "The Messenger." "But he signed six weeks, and many people within the pro-life movement feel that was too harsh." That comment triggered an immediate backlash from a key social conservative in Iowa, who responded, quote, "No, Mr. Former President, many in the pro-life community do not believe saving babies is too harsh." And today, DeSantis jumped on it, too.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Protecting an unborn child when there's the detectable heartbeat is something that almost probably 99% of pro-lifers support.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Such abortion bans are only possible because the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last year with the votes of all three justices Trump put on the court. But since then, Trump has refused to say what kind of an abortion ban he will be willing to sign as president.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Some people are at six weeks. Some people are three weeks. Two weeks.\par \par \uc2 HOST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Where is President Trump?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 President Trump is going to make the determination what he thinks is great for the country and what's fair for the country.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, DeSantis called Trump out for failing to take a stand.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 I signed the bill. I was proud to do it. He won't answer whether he would sign it or not.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As for the timing of DeSantis' presidential announcement, his team has told top donors and supporters to plan to be in Florida sometime the middle of next week. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  covering the race for the White House. Jon, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230518ej5g0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DESANTIS CHALLENGES TRUMP FL GOVERNOR AND FORMER PRESIDENT SPAR OVER ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, WILSON, KIMBELL, CRUM, DOWDY\par \par \uc2 SECURITY BREACH, SULLIVAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTRUDER IN BIDEN ADVISER'S HOME\par \par \uc2 CONNOLLY, PHAM, HATE CRIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT FACES HATE CRIME CHARGE\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, MCCARTHY, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES DEBT MEETING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE: MISSILE BARRAGE SHOT DOWN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DESANTIS, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESANTIS CHALLENGES TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back here at home tonight and to the race for the White House. On the Republican side, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  now taking on former President Trump after Trump refused to say whether he would sign a national abortion ban. Here's \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FL GOVERNOR AND FORMER PRESIDENT SPAR OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  moves towards a presidential run, his aides tell ABC News he will announce around Memorial Day, he's now facing off against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on a critical issue for Republican primary voters. Abortion. It comes after Trump criticized DeSantis for signing a law banning almost all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. "If you look at what DeSantis did